window.MG_LAZY_DATA["data/lazy/owner-courses/b242-505bf9ef2c18e9fe.json"]={sha256:"505bf9ef2c18e9fea559a6d6bfaa044ce840f8f62c6e794cb4553de6ee7d03b2",value:{"id":"b242","title":"土石壩反濾層設計","titleEn":"Filter-zone design for embankment dams","category":"water","kind":"course","status":"guided","contentStatus":"reviewable-educational-curriculum","summary":"本課以串連留土透水施工與連續性的反濾層設計為主線，先用留土粒徑與土類與透水能力與相容界定水力與構造條件，再將堆置分離與取樣、排水截面與水頭連結到變形相容與連續性。粒徑與水力算例只作篩選；反濾準則取決於被保護土分類、分散性與試驗程序。 每單元以原創算例、量測與失效辨識共同檢查推論。","summaryEn":"This course develops connecting retention permeability placement and continuity in filter design through Retention gradation and soil class and Permeability and compatibility, then connects Stockpile segregation and sampling and Drain area and hydraulic head to Deformation compatibility and continuity. Gradation and hydraulic examples are screening tools; filter criteria depend on base-soil classification dispersivity and test procedures. Each unit combines original calculation, measurement and failure diagnosis to test the inference.","scope":"依公開工程原理、官方資料與規範架構編寫的原創教學；步驟是可驗證的學習任務與假想算例，不是設計圖說、施工計畫、開挖、注漿或受限空間作業許可，也不是任何專案的設計文件。數值均為教學假設或公開資料，實際工程須由合格技師依規範與實測資料重新計算並簽證。","scopeEn":"Original teaching built from public engineering principles, official sources and code frameworks. Steps are verifiable learning tasks and hypothetical exercises, not design drawings, method statements, excavation, grouting or confined-space permits, or any project's design documents. Numbers are teaching assumptions or public data; real work must be recalculated and certified by qualified engineers using codes and measured data.","subcategory":"water-hydraulics","subcategoryTitle":"壩工監測、溢洪與壓力水路","subcategoryTitleEn":"Dam monitoring, spillways and pressure waterways","learningTrack":"water","learningSubdiscipline":"water-hydraulics","learningTags":["water","water-hydraulics","water"],"architectureFamily":"water-hydraulic","architectureNodes":[["留土粒徑與土類","Retention gradation and soil class"],["級配缺口與內穩","Gradation gaps and internal stability"],["堆置分離與取樣","Stockpile segregation and sampling"],["排水截面與水頭","Drain area and hydraulic head"],["變形相容與連續性","Deformation compatibility and continuity"]],"architectureEdges":[[0,1],[1,2],[2,3],[3,4],[0,3]],"diagram":{"type":"water-hydraulic","labels":["留土粒徑與土類","級配缺口與內穩","堆置分離與取樣","排水截面與水頭","變形相容與連續性"],"labelsEn":["Retention gradation and soil class","Gradation gaps and internal stability","Stockpile segregation and sampling","Drain area and hydraulic head","Deformation compatibility and continuity"],"original":true,"notToScale":true},"workedExample":{"title":"原創假想算例與邊界","titleEn":"Original hypothetical example and boundaries","text":"整合算例輸入全為教學假設，先檢查留土粒徑與土類：Illustrative D15filter=0.60 mm; d85base=0.20 mm; retentionRatio=0.60/0.20=3.00 dimensionless；再獨立檢查透水能力與相容：D15filter=0.60 mm; d15base=0.030 mm; permeabilityScreenRatio=0.60/0.030=20 dimensionless。敏感度：示意D15由0.60增至0.90mm時，對d85=0.20mm的比值由3增至4.5；這只顯示留土幾何改變，不能不分土類就以同一固定比值批准材料。 兩個結果須按各自量綱解釋，不能直接相加或當成完整設計。粒徑與水力算例只作篩選；反濾準則取決於被保護土分類、分散性與試驗程序。 將封閉前拍攝管底與兩側反濾接續並核對實測包絡尺寸作為獨立驗證，明確列出尚缺的現地輸入及其對結論的影響。","textEn":"Every input in this integrated example is a teaching assumption. First examine Retention gradation and soil class: Illustrative D15filter=0.60 mm; d85base=0.20 mm; retentionRatio=0.60/0.20=3.00 dimensionless. Independently examine Permeability and compatibility: D15filter=0.60 mm; d15base=0.030 mm; permeabilityScreenRatio=0.60/0.030=20 dimensionless. Sensitivity: raising illustrative D15 from0.60 to0.90mm changes the ratio to a0.20mm base d85 from3 to4.5; this illustrates retention geometry and does not authorize a universal acceptance ratio for every soil. Interpret each result in its own dimensions rather than adding them or treating them as a complete design. Gradation and hydraulic examples are screening tools; filter criteria depend on base-soil classification dispersivity and test procedures. Use the following independent check: Photograph filter continuity below and beside the conduit before closure and survey its envelope. Identify missing field inputs and state which conclusions depend on them.","assumptions":"數值是本課自行設定的教學假設，不代表任何專案的設計值、量測值或規範允許值；改變系統邊界或荷載組合後必須重算。","assumptionsEn":"Inputs are teaching assumptions, not any project's design values, measurements or code allowances; recalculate after changing the system boundary or load combination.","sourceScope":"原創數值練習；來源支援公開原理與工程背景，不宣稱來源提供這組數據。","sourceScopeEn":"Original numerical exercise; sources support public principles and project context, not these numbers."},"depth":5,"languageCoverage":["zh-TW","en"],"simulationOnly":true,"educationEdition":15,"enrichmentVersion":15,"stages":[{"id":"b242-v15-s1","title":"水文條件、邊界與工程系統","titleEn":"Hydrology, boundaries and engineering system","description":"本階段聚焦「留土粒徑與土類」與「透水能力與相容」：先建立機制、系統路徑與定量模型，再設計試驗驗證並診斷失效。","descriptionEn":"This stage covers \"Retention gradation and soil class\" and \"Permeability and compatibility\": establish the mechanism, system paths and quantitative model first, then design verification and diagnose failures.","steps":[{"id":"b242-v15-01","title":"留土粒徑與土類：機制與系統路徑","titleEn":"Retention gradation and soil class: mechanism and system paths","estimatedMinutes":20,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["b-src-water-manuals","v15s-usbr-filters","v15s-fema-seepage","v15s-usbr-embankment-history"],"prerequisiteIds":[],"objective":"說明「留土粒徑與土類」如何影響土石壩反濾層設計的受力、變形、水流或訊號表現，並畫出相關輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界。","objectiveEn":"Explain how “Retention gradation and soil class” governs forces, deformation, flow or signals in “Filter-zone design for embankment dams”, and map the relevant inputs, transfer paths and boundaries.","instruction":"反濾顆粒形成的孔隙須阻止被保護土持續遷移，又要讓局部細粒重新排列而不堵死。粒徑比只是土類相關準則的一環，細粒含量與分散性會改變判斷；不可把適用清潔砂的比值直接用在分散黏土，還需考慮基土代表性及侵蝕試驗。 驗證時應核對基土分組後的級配包絡並以指定反濾試驗檢驗持續侵蝕，並辨識以下失效情境：用平均級配代替最細基土會漏掉局部留土不足。這有助於確認模型的水流、受力或量測邊界是否仍成立。 師傅任務：以自由體圖、流路圖或訊號圖畫出相關物理量如何經過「留土粒徑與土類」傳到系統邊界，標出哪些量由設計決定、哪些由材料、施工或環境決定，再用三句話寫出機制摘要。","instructionEn":"Filter pores must prevent continuing migration of the protected soil while allowing limited particle rearrangement without sealing the drainage path. A grain-size ratio is only part of soil-specific criteria; fines and dispersivity change the interpretation. A criterion for clean sand cannot automatically be transferred to dispersive clay without representative sampling and erosion testing. Test this interpretation with the following evidence: Classify the base soil, compare gradation envelopes and test continuing erosion with the specified filter procedure. In particular, distinguish this failure mechanism: Using average gradation instead of the finer base soil overlooks local retention weakness. That distinction determines whether the model boundary or measurement assumption remains valid. Mentor task: draw a free-body, flow or signal diagram showing how relevant physical quantities pass through “Retention gradation and soil class” to the system boundary, mark which quantities are fixed by design and which by materials, construction or environment, then summarise the mechanism in three sentences.","observation":"量級提示：原創教學假設：Illustrative D15filter=0.60 mm; d85base=0.20 mm; retentionRatio=0.60/0.20=3.00 dimensionless。","observationEn":"Order-of-magnitude cue: Original teaching assumptions: Illustrative D15filter=0.60 mm; d85base=0.20 mm; retentionRatio=0.60/0.20=3.00 dimensionless.","failure":"常見誤解：「單一粒徑比可以批准所有不同土類反濾」這個說法忽略了上述機制；請在系統圖上指出它錯在哪一個環節。","failureEn":"Common misconception: \"One grain-size ratio can approve filters for every soil class\" It ignores the mechanism above; mark on your system diagram where it breaks down.","check":"系統圖標明「留土粒徑與土類」的輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界；三句摘要能解釋本步列出的誤解為何不成立。","checkEn":"The system diagram shows inputs, transfer paths and boundaries for “Retention gradation and soil class”; the three-sentence summary explains why the listed misconception fails.","knowledge":[{"id":"b242-v15-01-k1","title":"留土粒徑與土類","titleEn":"Retention gradation and soil class","text":"反濾顆粒形成的孔隙須阻止被保護土持續遷移，又要讓局部細粒重新排列而不堵死。粒徑比只是土類相關準則的一環，細粒含量與分散性會改變判斷；不可把適用清潔砂的比值直接用在分散黏土，還需考慮基土代表性及侵蝕試驗。","textEn":"Filter pores must prevent continuing migration of the protected soil while allowing limited particle rearrangement without sealing the drainage path. A grain-size ratio is only part of soil-specific criteria; fines and dispersivity change the interpretation.","sourceIds":["b-src-water-manuals","v15s-usbr-filters","v15s-fema-seepage","v15s-usbr-embankment-history"]},{"id":"b242-v15-01-k2","title":"誤解辨析","titleEn":"Misconception check","text":"誤解：單一粒徑比可以批准所有不同土類反濾 正確的工程判斷必須回到傳力機制與量級。","textEn":"Misconception: One grain-size ratio can approve filters for every soil class Sound engineering judgement goes back to the load path and magnitude.","sourceIds":["b-src-water-manuals","v15s-usbr-filters","v15s-fema-seepage","v15s-usbr-embankment-history"]}],"quiz":{"question":"關於「留土粒徑與土類」，下列哪一項敘述正確？","questionEn":"Which statement about \"Retention gradation and soil class\" is correct?","options":["單一粒徑比可以批准所有不同土類反濾","反濾顆粒形成的孔隙須阻止被保護土持續遷移，又要讓局部細粒重新排列而不堵死。","只要反濾材料比較粗就一定能留住基土"],"optionsEn":["One grain-size ratio can approve filters for every soil class","Filter pores must prevent continuing migration of the protected soil while allowing limited particle rearrangement without sealing the drainage path.","A coarser filter always retains the protected base soil"],"answer":1,"explanation":"反濾顆粒形成的孔隙須阻止被保護土持續遷移，又要讓局部細粒重新排列而不堵死。 其餘選項是常見誤解。","explanationEn":"Filter pores must prevent continuing migration of the protected soil while allowing limited particle rearrangement without sealing the drainage path. The other options are common misconceptions."},"unit":1,"unitFacet":"mechanism","order":1,"sequence":1},{"id":"b242-v15-02","title":"留土粒徑與土類：定量估算","titleEn":"Retention gradation and soil class: quantitative estimate","estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["b-src-water-manuals","v15s-usbr-filters","v15s-fema-seepage","v15s-usbr-embankment-history"],"prerequisiteIds":["b242-v15-01"],"objective":"以數值模型估算「留土粒徑與土類」的關鍵量，並判斷幾何、水頭、荷載或材料參數改變時結果的方向與幅度。","objectiveEn":"Estimate the key quantities of “Retention gradation and soil class” with a numerical model and judge the direction and size of change when geometry, water head, load or material parameters move.","instruction":"依下列模型逐步重算：原創教學假設：Illustrative D15filter=0.60 mm; d85base=0.20 mm; retentionRatio=0.60/0.20=3.00 dimensionless。數值只檢查量綱與機制，不是實測資料、設計設定或允收門檻。 師傅任務：保留單位重算一次，再只改變一個輸入（例如增加 10%），預測並計算輸出的變化，說明它是線性、平方或更高次方的關係，並指出規範或設計上通常如何處理這個敏感度。","instructionEn":"Recalculate step by step: Original teaching assumptions: Illustrative D15filter=0.60 mm; d85base=0.20 mm; retentionRatio=0.60/0.20=3.00 dimensionless. These values check dimensions and mechanism, not measured data, design settings or acceptance thresholds. Mentor task: redo the calculation keeping units, then change one input (for example by +10%), predict and compute the output change, state whether the dependence is linear, quadratic or steeper, and note how codes or designers usually handle this sensitivity.","observation":"如何核對：核對基土分組後的級配包絡並以指定反濾試驗檢驗持續侵蝕。","observationEn":"How to cross-check: Classify the base soil, compare gradation envelopes and test continuing erosion with the specified filter procedure.","failure":"計算陷阱：單位換算錯誤、把教學假設當成真實設計值、混淆標稱值與設計值（未乘載重或強度係數），或只看結果不檢查數量級，都會讓後續設計判斷失準。","failureEn":"Calculation traps: unit slips, treating teaching assumptions as real design values, mixing nominal and factored values, or accepting a result without checking its magnitude will mislead later design decisions.","check":"依模型顯示精度重現數值，列出單位與取整方式，並提交一個參數改變後的敏感度計算與工程解釋。","checkEn":"Reproduce the model values to their displayed precision, state units and rounding, and submit a sensitivity calculation for one changed parameter with an engineering explanation.","knowledge":[{"id":"b242-v15-02-k1","title":"定量模型","titleEn":"Quantitative model","text":"原創教學假設：Illustrative D15filter=0.60 mm; d85base=0.20 mm; retentionRatio=0.60/0.20=3.00 dimensionless。數值只檢查量綱與機制，不是實測資料、設計設定或允收門檻。","textEn":"Original teaching assumptions: Illustrative D15filter=0.60 mm; d85base=0.20 mm; retentionRatio=0.60/0.20=3.00 dimensionless. These values check dimensions and mechanism, not measured data, design settings or acceptance thresholds.","sourceIds":["b-src-water-manuals","v15s-usbr-filters","v15s-fema-seepage","v15s-usbr-embankment-history"]},{"id":"b242-v15-02-k2","title":"模型邊界","titleEn":"Model boundary","text":"本步數值為教學假設或公開資料的簡化；套用到實際工程前，必須依規範荷載組合、材料試驗與現場量測重新計算並由技師簽證。","textEn":"These numbers are teaching assumptions or simplified public data; before applying them to a real structure, recalculate with code load combinations, material tests and site measurements, certified by a qualified engineer.","sourceIds":["b-src-water-manuals","v15s-usbr-filters","v15s-fema-seepage","v15s-usbr-embankment-history"]}],"quiz":{"question":"依「留土粒徑與土類」的定量模型，下列哪一項敘述成立？","questionEn":"According to the quantitative model for \"Retention gradation and soil class\", which statement holds?","options":["圖上反濾厚度就是每個現地斷面的厚度","洗料耗水越高就保證反濾料越乾淨","原創教學假設：Illustrative D15filter=0.60 mm; d85base=0.20 mm; retentionRatio=0.60/0.20=3.00 dimensionless。"],"optionsEn":["Drawing thickness equals filter thickness at every field section","Greater washing-water use guarantees cleaner filter material","Original teaching assumptions: Illustrative D15filter=0.60 mm; d85base=0.20 mm; retentionRatio=0.60/0.20=3.00 dimensionless."],"answer":2,"explanation":"原創教學假設：Illustrative D15filter=0.60 mm; d85base=0.20 mm; retentionRatio=0.60/0.20=3.00 dimensionless。 重算時請保留單位。","explanationEn":"Original teaching assumptions: Illustrative D15filter=0.60 mm; d85base=0.20 mm; retentionRatio=0.60/0.20=3.00 dimensionless. Keep units when recalculating."},"unit":1,"unitFacet":"model","order":2,"sequence":2},{"id":"b242-v15-03","title":"留土粒徑與土類：試驗與驗證","titleEn":"Retention gradation and soil class: testing and verification","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["b-src-water-manuals","v15s-usbr-filters","v15s-fema-seepage","v15s-usbr-embankment-history"],"prerequisiteIds":["b242-v15-02"],"objective":"設計一項可重複的試驗、量測或檢查，驗證「留土粒徑與土類」是否符合模型與規範預期，並在量測前訂出允收準則與停工點。","objectiveEn":"Design a repeatable test, measurement or inspection that verifies whether “Retention gradation and soil class” meets the model and code expectation, fixing acceptance criteria and hold points before measuring.","instruction":"核對基土分組後的級配包絡並以指定反濾試驗檢驗持續侵蝕。應將原始量測與本單元模型的輸入條件對齊，並針對「用平均級配代替最細基土會漏掉局部留土不足」取得獨立證據；同時保留儀器校正、測點位置與時間，避免把不同工況的資料直接相減。 師傅任務：把上述方法寫成試驗或量測計畫，列出儀器與感測器、基準點或參考試體、步驟、比較對象、允收準則與停工點，並估計三項主要不確定度來源。","instructionEn":"Classify the base soil, compare gradation envelopes and test continuing erosion with the specified filter procedure. Match raw observations to the input conditions of this unit and obtain independent evidence for this specific scenario: Using average gradation instead of the finer base soil overlooks local retention weakness. Preserve calibration, location and timing so that unlike operating states are not directly subtracted. Mentor task: turn this into a test or measurement plan listing instruments and sensors, datums or reference specimens, procedure, comparison baseline, acceptance criteria and hold points, and estimate the three largest uncertainty contributions.","observation":"現場實務：交接時以核對基土分組後的級配包絡並以指定反濾試驗檢驗持續侵蝕作為可追溯證據，保存對應材料、構形與工況版本。針對用平均級配代替最細基土會漏掉局部留土不足，由負責工程師設定需補驗的項目與停留點，不能把教學結果當作現場操作許可。","observationEn":"Site practice: At handover, use the following traceable evidence: Classify the base soil, compare gradation envelopes and test continuing erosion with the specified filter procedure. Record material, geometry and operating-state versions. Address this scenario: Using average gradation instead of the finer base soil overlooks local retention weakness. The responsible engineer defines additional checks and hold points; the teaching result is not field operating authorization.","failure":"注意干擾：用平均級配代替最細基土會漏掉局部留土不足。 只量一次、沒有可追溯的基準，或不記錄溫度、水頭與施工荷重，就無法分辨真正的偏差與量測誤差。","failureEn":"Watch for interference: Using average gradation instead of the finer base soil overlooks local retention weakness. A single reading, no traceable datum, or unrecorded temperature, water head and construction loads make real deviations indistinguishable from measurement error.","check":"提交試驗或量測計畫：儀器、基準、步驟、允收準則、停工點與不確定度預算，並說明如何判定合格或不合格、由誰簽認。","checkEn":"Submit the test or measurement plan: instruments, datums, procedure, acceptance criteria, hold points and uncertainty budget, with the pass/fail rule and who signs it off.","knowledge":[{"id":"b242-v15-03-k1","title":"驗證方法","titleEn":"Verification method","text":"核對基土分組後的級配包絡並以指定反濾試驗檢驗持續侵蝕。應將原始量測與本單元模型的輸入條件對齊，並針對「用平均級配代替最細基土會漏掉局部留土不足」取得獨立證據；同時保留儀器校正、測點位置與時間，避免把不同工況的資料直接相減。","textEn":"Classify the base soil, compare gradation envelopes and test continuing erosion with the specified filter procedure. Match raw observations to the input conditions of this unit and obtain independent evidence for this specific scenario: Using average gradation instead of the finer base soil overlooks local retention weakness. Preserve calibration, location and timing so that unlike operating states are not directly subtracted.","sourceIds":["b-src-water-manuals","v15s-usbr-filters","v15s-fema-seepage","v15s-usbr-embankment-history"]},{"id":"b242-v15-03-k2","title":"現場實務","titleEn":"Site practice","text":"交接時以核對基土分組後的級配包絡並以指定反濾試驗檢驗持續侵蝕作為可追溯證據，保存對應材料、構形與工況版本。針對用平均級配代替最細基土會漏掉局部留土不足，由負責工程師設定需補驗的項目與停留點，不能把教學結果當作現場操作許可。","textEn":"At handover, use the following traceable evidence: Classify the base soil, compare gradation envelopes and test continuing erosion with the specified filter procedure. Record material, geometry and operating-state versions. Address this scenario: Using average gradation instead of the finer base soil overlooks local retention weakness. The responsible engineer defines additional checks and hold points; the teaching result is not field operating authorization.","sourceIds":["b-src-water-manuals","v15s-usbr-filters","v15s-fema-seepage","v15s-usbr-embankment-history"]}],"quiz":{"question":"要驗證「留土粒徑與土類」，下列哪一個做法最恰當？","questionEn":"Which approach best verifies \"Retention gradation and soil class\"?","options":["核對基土分組後的級配包絡並以指定反濾試驗檢驗持續侵蝕。","量測時不必記錄溫度、水頭、水位歷程與施工荷重，因為它們不會影響結果。","管頂反濾覆蓋充分就代表管底同樣連續"],"optionsEn":["Classify the base soil, compare gradation envelopes and test continuing erosion with the specified filter procedure.","Temperature, water head, water-level history and construction loads need not be recorded because they cannot affect the result.","Adequate filter cover above a conduit proves continuity below it"],"answer":0,"explanation":"核對基土分組後的級配包絡並以指定反濾試驗檢驗持續侵蝕。 驗證需要基準、重複性與事先訂定的允收準則。","explanationEn":"Classify the base soil, compare gradation envelopes and test continuing erosion with the specified filter procedure. Verification needs a datum, repeatability and acceptance criteria fixed in advance."},"unit":1,"unitFacet":"verification","order":3,"sequence":3},{"id":"b242-v15-04","title":"留土粒徑與土類：失效診斷","titleEn":"Retention gradation and soil class: failure diagnosis","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["b-src-water-manuals","v15s-usbr-filters","v15s-fema-seepage","v15s-usbr-embankment-history"],"prerequisiteIds":["b242-v15-03"],"objective":"從症狀倒推「留土粒徑與土類」的失效或劣化原因，提出能區分原因的檢查、矯正與預防措施。","objectiveEn":"Work back from symptoms to the failure or deterioration causes of “Retention gradation and soil class” and propose discriminating checks, corrective actions and prevention.","instruction":"用平均級配代替最細基土會漏掉局部留土不足。診斷時應採取以下查核：核對基土分組後的級配包絡並以指定反濾試驗檢驗持續侵蝕，確認異常是否同時出現在相關量測；未釐清原因就調整門檻，會使真正的機制變化被資料處理掩蓋。 師傅任務：建立失效樹——症狀、兩個以上可能原因、能區分它們的量測或檢測，以及矯正與預防措施；並說明此失效如何影響整體結構的安全、使用性、耐久或營運。","instructionEn":"Using average gradation instead of the finer base soil overlooks local retention weakness. Diagnose it by the following check: Classify the base soil, compare gradation envelopes and test continuing erosion with the specified filter procedure. Establish whether related measurements corroborate the anomaly; changing thresholds before identifying the cause can conceal a real change in the governing mechanism. Mentor task: build a fault tree with the symptom, at least two candidate causes, a measurement or inspection that tells them apart, and corrective and preventive actions; explain how the failure affects whole-structure safety, serviceability, durability or operation.","observation":"連結機制：這有助於確認模型的水流、受力或量測邊界是否仍成立。","observationEn":"Link to the mechanism: That distinction determines whether the model boundary or measurement assumption remains valid.","failure":"誤判風險：若相信「單一粒徑比可以批准所有不同土類反濾」，上述症狀可能被錯誤處理而反覆出現。","failureEn":"Misdiagnosis risk: believing \"One grain-size ratio can approve filters for every soil class\" leads to mishandling the symptom so it keeps returning.","check":"完成失效樹與矯正措施，指出哪一項量測或檢測能最快確認根因、需要哪些人簽認，以及如何防止再發。","checkEn":"Complete the fault tree and corrective actions, name the measurement or inspection that confirms the root cause fastest, who must sign off, and how recurrence is prevented.","knowledge":[{"id":"b242-v15-04-k1","title":"失效模式","titleEn":"Failure mode","text":"用平均級配代替最細基土會漏掉局部留土不足。診斷時應採取以下查核：核對基土分組後的級配包絡並以指定反濾試驗檢驗持續侵蝕，確認異常是否同時出現在相關量測；未釐清原因就調整門檻，會使真正的機制變化被資料處理掩蓋。","textEn":"Using average gradation instead of the finer base soil overlooks local retention weakness. Diagnose it by the following check: Classify the base soil, compare gradation envelopes and test continuing erosion with the specified filter procedure. Establish whether related measurements corroborate the anomaly; changing thresholds before identifying the cause can conceal a real change in the governing mechanism.","sourceIds":["b-src-water-manuals","v15s-usbr-filters","v15s-fema-seepage","v15s-usbr-embankment-history"]},{"id":"b242-v15-04-k2","title":"根因確認","titleEn":"Root-cause confirmation","text":"根因必須以可區分的量測或檢測確認；只補強外觀、更換構件或放寬允收值可能掩蓋問題。","textEn":"Confirm the root cause with a discriminating measurement or inspection; cosmetic repair, swapping components or relaxing limits can mask the problem.","sourceIds":["b-src-water-manuals","v15s-usbr-filters","v15s-fema-seepage","v15s-usbr-embankment-history"]}],"quiz":{"question":"在「留土粒徑與土類」出現異常時，下列哪一項判斷最合理？","questionEn":"When \"Retention gradation and soil class\" shows distress, which diagnosis is most reasonable?","options":["所有異常都來自施工人員失誤，設計與細部不需要檢討。","用平均級配代替最細基土會漏掉局部留土不足。","只要反濾材料比較粗就一定能留住基土"],"optionsEn":["Every anomaly is a workmanship error, so design and detailing never need review.","Using average gradation instead of the finer base soil overlooks local retention weakness.","A coarser filter always retains the protected base soil"],"answer":1,"explanation":"用平均級配代替最細基土會漏掉局部留土不足。 需以量測區分可能原因。","explanationEn":"Using average gradation instead of the finer base soil overlooks local retention weakness. Discriminate candidate causes by measurement."},"unit":1,"unitFacet":"failure","order":4,"sequence":4},{"id":"b242-v15-05","title":"透水能力與相容：機制與系統路徑","titleEn":"Permeability and compatibility: mechanism and system paths","estimatedMinutes":20,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["b-src-water-manuals","v15s-usbr-filters","v15s-fema-seepage","v15s-usbr-embankment-history"],"prerequisiteIds":["b242-v15-04"],"objective":"說明「透水能力與相容」如何影響土石壩反濾層設計的受力、變形、水流或訊號表現，並畫出相關輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界。","objectiveEn":"Explain how “Permeability and compatibility” governs forces, deformation, flow or signals in “Filter-zone design for embankment dams”, and map the relevant inputs, transfer paths and boundaries.","instruction":"反濾不只留住土，也須在預期滲流量下維持低水頭；粒徑較粗通常有較高導水能力，但不能犧牲留土與內部穩定性。以小粒徑比比較僅能作初步幾何指標，壓實密度、細粒堵塞與顆粒形狀對實際導水率仍需試驗量化。 驗證時應對設計密度下試體做定水頭或變水頭試驗並量測排水坡降，並辨識以下失效情境：細粒污染降低導水率後上游孔壓可能持續累積。這有助於確認模型的水流、受力或量測邊界是否仍成立。 師傅任務：以自由體圖、流路圖或訊號圖畫出相關物理量如何經過「透水能力與相容」傳到系統邊界，標出哪些量由設計決定、哪些由材料、施工或環境決定，再用三句話寫出機制摘要。","instructionEn":"A filter must maintain acceptable head while retaining soil. Coarser grains often improve drainage but may compromise retention or internal stability. A small-grain ratio is only a geometric screening indicator; compaction, pore clogging and grain shape influence actual conductivity and require hydraulic testing under representative placement conditions. Test this interpretation with the following evidence: Test conductivity at design density and measure the gradient needed for drainage. In particular, distinguish this failure mechanism: Fines contamination reduces conductivity and can allow upstream pore pressure to accumulate. That distinction determines whether the model boundary or measurement assumption remains valid. Mentor task: draw a free-body, flow or signal diagram showing how relevant physical quantities pass through “Permeability and compatibility” to the system boundary, mark which quantities are fixed by design and which by materials, construction or environment, then summarise the mechanism in three sentences.","observation":"量級提示：原創教學假設：D15filter=0.60 mm; d15base=0.030 mm; permeabilityScreenRatio=0.60/0.030=20 dimensionless。","observationEn":"Order-of-magnitude cue: Original teaching assumptions: D15filter=0.60 mm; d15base=0.030 mm; permeabilityScreenRatio=0.60/0.030=20 dimensionless.","failure":"常見誤解：「只要反濾材料比較粗就一定能留住基土」這個說法忽略了上述機制；請在系統圖上指出它錯在哪一個環節。","failureEn":"Common misconception: \"A coarser filter always retains the protected base soil\" It ignores the mechanism above; mark on your system diagram where it breaks down.","check":"系統圖標明「透水能力與相容」的輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界；三句摘要能解釋本步列出的誤解為何不成立。","checkEn":"The system diagram shows inputs, transfer paths and boundaries for “Permeability and compatibility”; the three-sentence summary explains why the listed misconception fails.","knowledge":[{"id":"b242-v15-05-k1","title":"透水能力與相容","titleEn":"Permeability and compatibility","text":"反濾不只留住土，也須在預期滲流量下維持低水頭；粒徑較粗通常有較高導水能力，但不能犧牲留土與內部穩定性。以小粒徑比比較僅能作初步幾何指標，壓實密度、細粒堵塞與顆粒形狀對實際導水率仍需試驗量化。","textEn":"A filter must maintain acceptable head while retaining soil. Coarser grains often improve drainage but may compromise retention or internal stability.","sourceIds":["b-src-water-manuals","v15s-usbr-filters","v15s-fema-seepage","v15s-usbr-embankment-history"]},{"id":"b242-v15-05-k2","title":"誤解辨析","titleEn":"Misconception check","text":"誤解：只要反濾材料比較粗就一定能留住基土 正確的工程判斷必須回到傳力機制與量級。","textEn":"Misconception: A coarser filter always retains the protected base soil Sound engineering judgement goes back to the load path and magnitude.","sourceIds":["b-src-water-manuals","v15s-usbr-filters","v15s-fema-seepage","v15s-usbr-embankment-history"]}],"quiz":{"question":"關於「透水能力與相容」，下列哪一項敘述正確？","questionEn":"Which statement about \"Permeability and compatibility\" is correct?","options":["只要反濾材料比較粗就一定能留住基土","界面留土合格就表示反濾自身永遠穩定","反濾不只留住土，也須在預期滲流量下維持低水頭；粒徑較粗通常有較高導水能力，但不能犧牲留土與內部穩定性。"],"optionsEn":["A coarser filter always retains the protected base soil","Successful interface retention proves permanent internal filter stability","A filter must maintain acceptable head while retaining soil."],"answer":2,"explanation":"反濾不只留住土，也須在預期滲流量下維持低水頭；粒徑較粗通常有較高導水能力，但不能犧牲留土與內部穩定性。 其餘選項是常見誤解。","explanationEn":"A filter must maintain acceptable head while retaining soil. The other options are common misconceptions."},"unit":2,"unitFacet":"mechanism","order":5,"sequence":5},{"id":"b242-v15-06","title":"透水能力與相容：定量估算","titleEn":"Permeability and compatibility: quantitative estimate","estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["b-src-water-manuals","v15s-usbr-filters","v15s-fema-seepage","v15s-usbr-embankment-history"],"prerequisiteIds":["b242-v15-05"],"objective":"以數值模型估算「透水能力與相容」的關鍵量，並判斷幾何、水頭、荷載或材料參數改變時結果的方向與幅度。","objectiveEn":"Estimate the key quantities of “Permeability and compatibility” with a numerical model and judge the direction and size of change when geometry, water head, load or material parameters move.","instruction":"依下列模型逐步重算：原創教學假設：D15filter=0.60 mm; d15base=0.030 mm; permeabilityScreenRatio=0.60/0.030=20 dimensionless。數值只檢查量綱與機制，不是實測資料、設計設定或允收門檻。 師傅任務：保留單位重算一次，再只改變一個輸入（例如增加 10%），預測並計算輸出的變化，說明它是線性、平方或更高次方的關係，並指出規範或設計上通常如何處理這個敏感度。","instructionEn":"Recalculate step by step: Original teaching assumptions: D15filter=0.60 mm; d15base=0.030 mm; permeabilityScreenRatio=0.60/0.030=20 dimensionless. These values check dimensions and mechanism, not measured data, design settings or acceptance thresholds. Mentor task: redo the calculation keeping units, then change one input (for example by +10%), predict and compute the output change, state whether the dependence is linear, quadratic or steeper, and note how codes or designers usually handle this sensitivity.","observation":"如何核對：對設計密度下試體做定水頭或變水頭試驗並量測排水坡降。","observationEn":"How to cross-check: Test conductivity at design density and measure the gradient needed for drainage.","failure":"計算陷阱：單位換算錯誤、把教學假設當成真實設計值、混淆標稱值與設計值（未乘載重或強度係數），或只看結果不檢查數量級，都會讓後續設計判斷失準。","failureEn":"Calculation traps: unit slips, treating teaching assumptions as real design values, mixing nominal and factored values, or accepting a result without checking its magnitude will mislead later design decisions.","check":"依模型顯示精度重現數值，列出單位與取整方式，並提交一個參數改變後的敏感度計算與工程解釋。","checkEn":"Reproduce the model values to their displayed precision, state units and rounding, and submit a sensitivity calculation for one changed parameter with an engineering explanation.","knowledge":[{"id":"b242-v15-06-k1","title":"定量模型","titleEn":"Quantitative model","text":"原創教學假設：D15filter=0.60 mm; d15base=0.030 mm; permeabilityScreenRatio=0.60/0.030=20 dimensionless。數值只檢查量綱與機制，不是實測資料、設計設定或允收門檻。","textEn":"Original teaching assumptions: D15filter=0.60 mm; d15base=0.030 mm; permeabilityScreenRatio=0.60/0.030=20 dimensionless. These values check dimensions and mechanism, not measured data, design settings or acceptance thresholds.","sourceIds":["b-src-water-manuals","v15s-usbr-filters","v15s-fema-seepage","v15s-usbr-embankment-history"]},{"id":"b242-v15-06-k2","title":"模型邊界","titleEn":"Model boundary","text":"本步數值為教學假設或公開資料的簡化；套用到實際工程前，必須依規範荷載組合、材料試驗與現場量測重新計算並由技師簽證。","textEn":"These numbers are teaching assumptions or simplified public data; before applying them to a real structure, recalculate with code load combinations, material tests and site measurements, certified by a qualified engineer.","sourceIds":["b-src-water-manuals","v15s-usbr-filters","v15s-fema-seepage","v15s-usbr-embankment-history"]}],"quiz":{"question":"依「透水能力與相容」的定量模型，下列哪一項敘述成立？","questionEn":"According to the quantitative model for \"Permeability and compatibility\", which statement holds?","options":["原創教學假設：D15filter=0.60 mm; d15base=0.030 mm; permeabilityScreenRatio=0.60/0.030=20 dimensionless。","批次平均合格就可以忽略局部材料分離","留土功能正常就表示排水出口一定暢通"],"optionsEn":["Original teaching assumptions: D15filter=0.60 mm; d15base=0.030 mm; permeabilityScreenRatio=0.60/0.030=20 dimensionless.","An acceptable batch average makes local segregation irrelevant","Successful soil retention guarantees an unobstructed drainage outlet"],"answer":0,"explanation":"原創教學假設：D15filter=0.60 mm; d15base=0.030 mm; permeabilityScreenRatio=0.60/0.030=20 dimensionless。 重算時請保留單位。","explanationEn":"Original teaching assumptions: D15filter=0.60 mm; d15base=0.030 mm; permeabilityScreenRatio=0.60/0.030=20 dimensionless. Keep units when recalculating."},"unit":2,"unitFacet":"model","order":6,"sequence":6},{"id":"b242-v15-07","title":"透水能力與相容：試驗與驗證","titleEn":"Permeability and compatibility: testing and verification","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["b-src-water-manuals","v15s-usbr-filters","v15s-fema-seepage","v15s-usbr-embankment-history"],"prerequisiteIds":["b242-v15-06"],"objective":"設計一項可重複的試驗、量測或檢查，驗證「透水能力與相容」是否符合模型與規範預期，並在量測前訂出允收準則與停工點。","objectiveEn":"Design a repeatable test, measurement or inspection that verifies whether “Permeability and compatibility” meets the model and code expectation, fixing acceptance criteria and hold points before measuring.","instruction":"對設計密度下試體做定水頭或變水頭試驗並量測排水坡降。應將原始量測與本單元模型的輸入條件對齊，並針對「細粒污染降低導水率後上游孔壓可能持續累積」取得獨立證據；同時保留儀器校正、測點位置與時間，避免把不同工況的資料直接相減。 師傅任務：把上述方法寫成試驗或量測計畫，列出儀器與感測器、基準點或參考試體、步驟、比較對象、允收準則與停工點，並估計三項主要不確定度來源。","instructionEn":"Test conductivity at design density and measure the gradient needed for drainage. Match raw observations to the input conditions of this unit and obtain independent evidence for this specific scenario: Fines contamination reduces conductivity and can allow upstream pore pressure to accumulate. Preserve calibration, location and timing so that unlike operating states are not directly subtracted. Mentor task: turn this into a test or measurement plan listing instruments and sensors, datums or reference specimens, procedure, comparison baseline, acceptance criteria and hold points, and estimate the three largest uncertainty contributions.","observation":"現場實務：交接時以對設計密度下試體做定水頭或變水頭試驗並量測排水坡降作為可追溯證據，保存對應材料、構形與工況版本。針對細粒污染降低導水率後上游孔壓可能持續累積，由負責工程師設定需補驗的項目與停留點，不能把教學結果當作現場操作許可。","observationEn":"Site practice: At handover, use the following traceable evidence: Test conductivity at design density and measure the gradient needed for drainage. Record material, geometry and operating-state versions. Address this scenario: Fines contamination reduces conductivity and can allow upstream pore pressure to accumulate. The responsible engineer defines additional checks and hold points; the teaching result is not field operating authorization.","failure":"注意干擾：細粒污染降低導水率後上游孔壓可能持續累積。 只量一次、沒有可追溯的基準，或不記錄溫度、水頭與施工荷重，就無法分辨真正的偏差與量測誤差。","failureEn":"Watch for interference: Fines contamination reduces conductivity and can allow upstream pore pressure to accumulate. A single reading, no traceable datum, or unrecorded temperature, water head and construction loads make real deviations indistinguishable from measurement error.","check":"提交試驗或量測計畫：儀器、基準、步驟、允收準則、停工點與不確定度預算，並說明如何判定合格或不合格、由誰簽認。","checkEn":"Submit the test or measurement plan: instruments, datums, procedure, acceptance criteria, hold points and uncertainty budget, with the pass/fail rule and who signs it off.","knowledge":[{"id":"b242-v15-07-k1","title":"驗證方法","titleEn":"Verification method","text":"對設計密度下試體做定水頭或變水頭試驗並量測排水坡降。應將原始量測與本單元模型的輸入條件對齊，並針對「細粒污染降低導水率後上游孔壓可能持續累積」取得獨立證據；同時保留儀器校正、測點位置與時間，避免把不同工況的資料直接相減。","textEn":"Test conductivity at design density and measure the gradient needed for drainage. Match raw observations to the input conditions of this unit and obtain independent evidence for this specific scenario: Fines contamination reduces conductivity and can allow upstream pore pressure to accumulate. Preserve calibration, location and timing so that unlike operating states are not directly subtracted.","sourceIds":["b-src-water-manuals","v15s-usbr-filters","v15s-fema-seepage","v15s-usbr-embankment-history"]},{"id":"b242-v15-07-k2","title":"現場實務","titleEn":"Site practice","text":"交接時以對設計密度下試體做定水頭或變水頭試驗並量測排水坡降作為可追溯證據，保存對應材料、構形與工況版本。針對細粒污染降低導水率後上游孔壓可能持續累積，由負責工程師設定需補驗的項目與停留點，不能把教學結果當作現場操作許可。","textEn":"At handover, use the following traceable evidence: Test conductivity at design density and measure the gradient needed for drainage. Record material, geometry and operating-state versions. Address this scenario: Fines contamination reduces conductivity and can allow upstream pore pressure to accumulate. The responsible engineer defines additional checks and hold points; the teaching result is not field operating authorization.","sourceIds":["b-src-water-manuals","v15s-usbr-filters","v15s-fema-seepage","v15s-usbr-embankment-history"]}],"quiz":{"question":"要驗證「透水能力與相容」，下列哪一個做法最恰當？","questionEn":"Which approach best verifies \"Permeability and compatibility\"?","options":["沿用另一處水工設施或流域的量測結果，就可視為本工程已完成驗證。","對設計密度下試體做定水頭或變水頭試驗並量測排水坡降。","初期出水清澈就證明持續侵蝕已經停止"],"optionsEn":["Reusing results from another hydraulic structure or catchment counts as verifying this structure.","Test conductivity at design density and measure the gradient needed for drainage.","Initially clear discharge proves that continuing erosion has stopped"],"answer":1,"explanation":"對設計密度下試體做定水頭或變水頭試驗並量測排水坡降。 驗證需要基準、重複性與事先訂定的允收準則。","explanationEn":"Test conductivity at design density and measure the gradient needed for drainage. Verification needs a datum, repeatability and acceptance criteria fixed in advance."},"unit":2,"unitFacet":"verification","order":7,"sequence":7},{"id":"b242-v15-08","title":"透水能力與相容：失效診斷","titleEn":"Permeability and compatibility: failure diagnosis","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["b-src-water-manuals","v15s-usbr-filters","v15s-fema-seepage","v15s-usbr-embankment-history"],"prerequisiteIds":["b242-v15-07"],"objective":"從症狀倒推「透水能力與相容」的失效或劣化原因，提出能區分原因的檢查、矯正與預防措施。","objectiveEn":"Work back from symptoms to the failure or deterioration causes of “Permeability and compatibility” and propose discriminating checks, corrective actions and prevention.","instruction":"細粒污染降低導水率後上游孔壓可能持續累積。診斷時應採取以下查核：對設計密度下試體做定水頭或變水頭試驗並量測排水坡降，確認異常是否同時出現在相關量測；未釐清原因就調整門檻，會使真正的機制變化被資料處理掩蓋。 師傅任務：建立失效樹——症狀、兩個以上可能原因、能區分它們的量測或檢測，以及矯正與預防措施；並說明此失效如何影響整體結構的安全、使用性、耐久或營運。","instructionEn":"Fines contamination reduces conductivity and can allow upstream pore pressure to accumulate. Diagnose it by the following check: Test conductivity at design density and measure the gradient needed for drainage. Establish whether related measurements corroborate the anomaly; changing thresholds before identifying the cause can conceal a real change in the governing mechanism. Mentor task: build a fault tree with the symptom, at least two candidate causes, a measurement or inspection that tells them apart, and corrective and preventive actions; explain how the failure affects whole-structure safety, serviceability, durability or operation.","observation":"連結機制：這有助於確認模型的水流、受力或量測邊界是否仍成立。","observationEn":"Link to the mechanism: That distinction determines whether the model boundary or measurement assumption remains valid.","failure":"誤判風險：若相信「只要反濾材料比較粗就一定能留住基土」，上述症狀可能被錯誤處理而反覆出現。","failureEn":"Misdiagnosis risk: believing \"A coarser filter always retains the protected base soil\" leads to mishandling the symptom so it keeps returning.","check":"完成失效樹與矯正措施，指出哪一項量測或檢測能最快確認根因、需要哪些人簽認，以及如何防止再發。","checkEn":"Complete the fault tree and corrective actions, name the measurement or inspection that confirms the root cause fastest, who must sign off, and how recurrence is prevented.","knowledge":[{"id":"b242-v15-08-k1","title":"失效模式","titleEn":"Failure mode","text":"細粒污染降低導水率後上游孔壓可能持續累積。診斷時應採取以下查核：對設計密度下試體做定水頭或變水頭試驗並量測排水坡降，確認異常是否同時出現在相關量測；未釐清原因就調整門檻，會使真正的機制變化被資料處理掩蓋。","textEn":"Fines contamination reduces conductivity and can allow upstream pore pressure to accumulate. Diagnose it by the following check: Test conductivity at design density and measure the gradient needed for drainage. Establish whether related measurements corroborate the anomaly; changing thresholds before identifying the cause can conceal a real change in the governing mechanism.","sourceIds":["b-src-water-manuals","v15s-usbr-filters","v15s-fema-seepage","v15s-usbr-embankment-history"]},{"id":"b242-v15-08-k2","title":"根因確認","titleEn":"Root-cause confirmation","text":"根因必須以可區分的量測或檢測確認；只補強外觀、更換構件或放寬允收值可能掩蓋問題。","textEn":"Confirm the root cause with a discriminating measurement or inspection; cosmetic repair, swapping components or relaxing limits can mask the problem.","sourceIds":["b-src-water-manuals","v15s-usbr-filters","v15s-fema-seepage","v15s-usbr-embankment-history"]}],"quiz":{"question":"在「透水能力與相容」出現異常時，下列哪一項判斷最合理？","questionEn":"When \"Permeability and compatibility\" shows distress, which diagnosis is most reasonable?","options":["補一層塗料或放寬允收值，就能解決大多數劣化問題。","界面留土合格就表示反濾自身永遠穩定","細粒污染降低導水率後上游孔壓可能持續累積。"],"optionsEn":["Adding a coat of paint or widening the acceptance limits solves most deterioration problems.","Successful interface retention proves permanent internal filter stability","Fines contamination reduces conductivity and can allow upstream pore pressure to accumulate."],"answer":2,"explanation":"細粒污染降低導水率後上游孔壓可能持續累積。 需以量測區分可能原因。","explanationEn":"Fines contamination reduces conductivity and can allow upstream pore pressure to accumulate. Discriminate candidate causes by measurement."},"unit":2,"unitFacet":"failure","order":8,"sequence":8}],"order":1},{"id":"b242-v15-s2","title":"水力機制、材料與定量模型","titleEn":"Hydraulics, materials and quantitative models","description":"本階段聚焦「級配缺口與內穩」與「鋪築厚度與偏差」：先建立機制、系統路徑與定量模型，再設計試驗驗證並診斷失效。","descriptionEn":"This stage covers \"Gradation gaps and internal stability\" and \"Placed thickness and tolerances\": establish the mechanism, system paths and quantitative model first, then design verification and diagnose failures.","steps":[{"id":"b242-v15-09","title":"級配缺口與內穩：機制與系統路徑","titleEn":"Gradation gaps and internal stability: mechanism and system paths","estimatedMinutes":20,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["b-src-water-manuals","v15s-usbr-filters","v15s-fema-seepage","v15s-usbr-embankment-history"],"prerequisiteIds":["b242-v15-08"],"objective":"說明「級配缺口與內穩」如何影響土石壩反濾層設計的受力、變形、水流或訊號表現，並畫出相關輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界。","objectiveEn":"Explain how “Gradation gaps and internal stability” governs forces, deformation, flow or signals in “Filter-zone design for embankment dams”, and map the relevant inputs, transfer paths and boundaries.","instruction":"級配寬廣不代表顆粒骨架能約束所有細料，缺級配材料可能讓細粒穿過粗粒孔隙形成潛蝕。應區分基土到反濾界面的留土與反濾自身的內部穩定；比較粒徑區段質量增量能提示缺口，仍需依適用方法與試驗確認。 驗證時應用密集篩孔資料重繪級配增量並檢驗滲流後流出顆粒組成，並辨識以下失效情境：只檢查界面粒徑比會漏掉反濾層自身的細粒流失。這有助於確認模型的水流、受力或量測邊界是否仍成立。 師傅任務：以自由體圖、流路圖或訊號圖畫出相關物理量如何經過「級配缺口與內穩」傳到系統邊界，標出哪些量由設計決定、哪些由材料、施工或環境決定，再用三句話寫出機制摘要。","instructionEn":"A broad gradation does not guarantee that the coarse skeleton restrains its own fines. Gap-graded material can lose smaller particles through larger pores. Distinguish interface retention from stability within the filter itself; incremental mass in size bands can flag a gap, but interpretation requires an applicable assessment method and testing. Test this interpretation with the following evidence: Replot gradation increments using closely spaced sieves and analyze particles discharged after seepage testing. In particular, distinguish this failure mechanism: Checking only interface ratios misses fine-particle loss within the filter itself. That distinction determines whether the model boundary or measurement assumption remains valid. Mentor task: draw a free-body, flow or signal diagram showing how relevant physical quantities pass through “Gradation gaps and internal stability” to the system boundary, mark which quantities are fixed by design and which by materials, construction or environment, then summarise the mechanism in three sentences.","observation":"量級提示：原創教學假設：Illustrative fractions: F(d)=12 percent; F(4d)=18 percent; H=18-12=6 percent; H/F=6/12=0.50 dimensionless。","observationEn":"Order-of-magnitude cue: Original teaching assumptions: Illustrative fractions: F(d)=12 percent; F(4d)=18 percent; H=18-12=6 percent; H/F=6/12=0.50 dimensionless.","failure":"常見誤解：「界面留土合格就表示反濾自身永遠穩定」這個說法忽略了上述機制；請在系統圖上指出它錯在哪一個環節。","failureEn":"Common misconception: \"Successful interface retention proves permanent internal filter stability\" It ignores the mechanism above; mark on your system diagram where it breaks down.","check":"系統圖標明「級配缺口與內穩」的輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界；三句摘要能解釋本步列出的誤解為何不成立。","checkEn":"The system diagram shows inputs, transfer paths and boundaries for “Gradation gaps and internal stability”; the three-sentence summary explains why the listed misconception fails.","knowledge":[{"id":"b242-v15-09-k1","title":"級配缺口與內穩","titleEn":"Gradation gaps and internal stability","text":"級配寬廣不代表顆粒骨架能約束所有細料，缺級配材料可能讓細粒穿過粗粒孔隙形成潛蝕。應區分基土到反濾界面的留土與反濾自身的內部穩定；比較粒徑區段質量增量能提示缺口，仍需依適用方法與試驗確認。","textEn":"A broad gradation does not guarantee that the coarse skeleton restrains its own fines. Gap-graded material can lose smaller particles through larger pores.","sourceIds":["b-src-water-manuals","v15s-usbr-filters","v15s-fema-seepage","v15s-usbr-embankment-history"]},{"id":"b242-v15-09-k2","title":"誤解辨析","titleEn":"Misconception check","text":"誤解：界面留土合格就表示反濾自身永遠穩定 正確的工程判斷必須回到傳力機制與量級。","textEn":"Misconception: Successful interface retention proves permanent internal filter stability Sound engineering judgement goes back to the load path and magnitude.","sourceIds":["b-src-water-manuals","v15s-usbr-filters","v15s-fema-seepage","v15s-usbr-embankment-history"]}],"quiz":{"question":"關於「級配缺口與內穩」，下列哪一項敘述正確？","questionEn":"Which statement about \"Gradation gaps and internal stability\" is correct?","options":["級配寬廣不代表顆粒骨架能約束所有細料，缺級配材料可能讓細粒穿過粗粒孔隙形成潛蝕。","界面留土合格就表示反濾自身永遠穩定","圖上反濾厚度就是每個現地斷面的厚度"],"optionsEn":["A broad gradation does not guarantee that the coarse skeleton restrains its own fines.","Successful interface retention proves permanent internal filter stability","Drawing thickness equals filter thickness at every field section"],"answer":0,"explanation":"級配寬廣不代表顆粒骨架能約束所有細料，缺級配材料可能讓細粒穿過粗粒孔隙形成潛蝕。 其餘選項是常見誤解。","explanationEn":"A broad gradation does not guarantee that the coarse skeleton restrains its own fines. The other options are common misconceptions."},"unit":3,"unitFacet":"mechanism","order":1,"sequence":9},{"id":"b242-v15-10","title":"級配缺口與內穩：定量估算","titleEn":"Gradation gaps and internal stability: quantitative estimate","estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["b-src-water-manuals","v15s-usbr-filters","v15s-fema-seepage","v15s-usbr-embankment-history"],"prerequisiteIds":["b242-v15-09"],"objective":"以數值模型估算「級配缺口與內穩」的關鍵量，並判斷幾何、水頭、荷載或材料參數改變時結果的方向與幅度。","objectiveEn":"Estimate the key quantities of “Gradation gaps and internal stability” with a numerical model and judge the direction and size of change when geometry, water head, load or material parameters move.","instruction":"依下列模型逐步重算：原創教學假設：Illustrative fractions: F(d)=12 percent; F(4d)=18 percent; H=18-12=6 percent; H/F=6/12=0.50 dimensionless。數值只檢查量綱與機制，不是實測資料、設計設定或允收門檻。 師傅任務：保留單位重算一次，再只改變一個輸入（例如增加 10%），預測並計算輸出的變化，說明它是線性、平方或更高次方的關係，並指出規範或設計上通常如何處理這個敏感度。","instructionEn":"Recalculate step by step: Original teaching assumptions: Illustrative fractions: F(d)=12 percent; F(4d)=18 percent; H=18-12=6 percent; H/F=6/12=0.50 dimensionless. These values check dimensions and mechanism, not measured data, design settings or acceptance thresholds. Mentor task: redo the calculation keeping units, then change one input (for example by +10%), predict and compute the output change, state whether the dependence is linear, quadratic or steeper, and note how codes or designers usually handle this sensitivity.","observation":"如何核對：用密集篩孔資料重繪級配增量並檢驗滲流後流出顆粒組成。","observationEn":"How to cross-check: Replot gradation increments using closely spaced sieves and analyze particles discharged after seepage testing.","failure":"計算陷阱：單位換算錯誤、把教學假設當成真實設計值、混淆標稱值與設計值（未乘載重或強度係數），或只看結果不檢查數量級，都會讓後續設計判斷失準。","failureEn":"Calculation traps: unit slips, treating teaching assumptions as real design values, mixing nominal and factored values, or accepting a result without checking its magnitude will mislead later design decisions.","check":"依模型顯示精度重現數值，列出單位與取整方式，並提交一個參數改變後的敏感度計算與工程解釋。","checkEn":"Reproduce the model values to their displayed precision, state units and rounding, and submit a sensitivity calculation for one changed parameter with an engineering explanation.","knowledge":[{"id":"b242-v15-10-k1","title":"定量模型","titleEn":"Quantitative model","text":"原創教學假設：Illustrative fractions: F(d)=12 percent; F(4d)=18 percent; H=18-12=6 percent; H/F=6/12=0.50 dimensionless。數值只檢查量綱與機制，不是實測資料、設計設定或允收門檻。","textEn":"Original teaching assumptions: Illustrative fractions: F(d)=12 percent; F(4d)=18 percent; H=18-12=6 percent; H/F=6/12=0.50 dimensionless. These values check dimensions and mechanism, not measured data, design settings or acceptance thresholds.","sourceIds":["b-src-water-manuals","v15s-usbr-filters","v15s-fema-seepage","v15s-usbr-embankment-history"]},{"id":"b242-v15-10-k2","title":"模型邊界","titleEn":"Model boundary","text":"本步數值為教學假設或公開資料的簡化；套用到實際工程前，必須依規範荷載組合、材料試驗與現場量測重新計算並由技師簽證。","textEn":"These numbers are teaching assumptions or simplified public data; before applying them to a real structure, recalculate with code load combinations, material tests and site measurements, certified by a qualified engineer.","sourceIds":["b-src-water-manuals","v15s-usbr-filters","v15s-fema-seepage","v15s-usbr-embankment-history"]}],"quiz":{"question":"依「級配缺口與內穩」的定量模型，下列哪一項敘述成立？","questionEn":"According to the quantitative model for \"Gradation gaps and internal stability\", which statement holds?","options":["洗料耗水越高就保證反濾料越乾淨","原創教學假設：Illustrative fractions: F(d)=12 percent; F(4d)=18 percent; H=18-12=6 percent; H/F=6/12=0.50 dimensionless。","管頂反濾覆蓋充分就代表管底同樣連續"],"optionsEn":["Greater washing-water use guarantees cleaner filter material","Original teaching assumptions: Illustrative fractions: F(d)=12 percent; F(4d)=18 percent; H=18-12=6 percent; H/F=6/12=0.50 dimensionless.","Adequate filter cover above a conduit proves continuity below it"],"answer":1,"explanation":"原創教學假設：Illustrative fractions: F(d)=12 percent; F(4d)=18 percent; H=18-12=6 percent; H/F=6/12=0.50 dimensionless。 重算時請保留單位。","explanationEn":"Original teaching assumptions: Illustrative fractions: F(d)=12 percent; F(4d)=18 percent; H=18-12=6 percent; H/F=6/12=0.50 dimensionless. Keep units when recalculating."},"unit":3,"unitFacet":"model","order":2,"sequence":10},{"id":"b242-v15-11","title":"級配缺口與內穩：試驗與驗證","titleEn":"Gradation gaps and internal stability: testing and verification","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["b-src-water-manuals","v15s-usbr-filters","v15s-fema-seepage","v15s-usbr-embankment-history"],"prerequisiteIds":["b242-v15-10"],"objective":"設計一項可重複的試驗、量測或檢查，驗證「級配缺口與內穩」是否符合模型與規範預期，並在量測前訂出允收準則與停工點。","objectiveEn":"Design a repeatable test, measurement or inspection that verifies whether “Gradation gaps and internal stability” meets the model and code expectation, fixing acceptance criteria and hold points before measuring.","instruction":"用密集篩孔資料重繪級配增量並檢驗滲流後流出顆粒組成。應將原始量測與本單元模型的輸入條件對齊，並針對「只檢查界面粒徑比會漏掉反濾層自身的細粒流失」取得獨立證據；同時保留儀器校正、測點位置與時間，避免把不同工況的資料直接相減。 師傅任務：把上述方法寫成試驗或量測計畫，列出儀器與感測器、基準點或參考試體、步驟、比較對象、允收準則與停工點，並估計三項主要不確定度來源。","instructionEn":"Replot gradation increments using closely spaced sieves and analyze particles discharged after seepage testing. Match raw observations to the input conditions of this unit and obtain independent evidence for this specific scenario: Checking only interface ratios misses fine-particle loss within the filter itself. Preserve calibration, location and timing so that unlike operating states are not directly subtracted. Mentor task: turn this into a test or measurement plan listing instruments and sensors, datums or reference specimens, procedure, comparison baseline, acceptance criteria and hold points, and estimate the three largest uncertainty contributions.","observation":"現場實務：交接時以用密集篩孔資料重繪級配增量並檢驗滲流後流出顆粒組成作為可追溯證據，保存對應材料、構形與工況版本。針對只檢查界面粒徑比會漏掉反濾層自身的細粒流失，由負責工程師設定需補驗的項目與停留點，不能把教學結果當作現場操作許可。","observationEn":"Site practice: At handover, use the following traceable evidence: Replot gradation increments using closely spaced sieves and analyze particles discharged after seepage testing. Record material, geometry and operating-state versions. Address this scenario: Checking only interface ratios misses fine-particle loss within the filter itself. The responsible engineer defines additional checks and hold points; the teaching result is not field operating authorization.","failure":"注意干擾：只檢查界面粒徑比會漏掉反濾層自身的細粒流失。 只量一次、沒有可追溯的基準，或不記錄溫度、水頭與施工荷重，就無法分辨真正的偏差與量測誤差。","failureEn":"Watch for interference: Checking only interface ratios misses fine-particle loss within the filter itself. A single reading, no traceable datum, or unrecorded temperature, water head and construction loads make real deviations indistinguishable from measurement error.","check":"提交試驗或量測計畫：儀器、基準、步驟、允收準則、停工點與不確定度預算，並說明如何判定合格或不合格、由誰簽認。","checkEn":"Submit the test or measurement plan: instruments, datums, procedure, acceptance criteria, hold points and uncertainty budget, with the pass/fail rule and who signs it off.","knowledge":[{"id":"b242-v15-11-k1","title":"驗證方法","titleEn":"Verification method","text":"用密集篩孔資料重繪級配增量並檢驗滲流後流出顆粒組成。應將原始量測與本單元模型的輸入條件對齊，並針對「只檢查界面粒徑比會漏掉反濾層自身的細粒流失」取得獨立證據；同時保留儀器校正、測點位置與時間，避免把不同工況的資料直接相減。","textEn":"Replot gradation increments using closely spaced sieves and analyze particles discharged after seepage testing. Match raw observations to the input conditions of this unit and obtain independent evidence for this specific scenario: Checking only interface ratios misses fine-particle loss within the filter itself. Preserve calibration, location and timing so that unlike operating states are not directly subtracted.","sourceIds":["b-src-water-manuals","v15s-usbr-filters","v15s-fema-seepage","v15s-usbr-embankment-history"]},{"id":"b242-v15-11-k2","title":"現場實務","titleEn":"Site practice","text":"交接時以用密集篩孔資料重繪級配增量並檢驗滲流後流出顆粒組成作為可追溯證據，保存對應材料、構形與工況版本。針對只檢查界面粒徑比會漏掉反濾層自身的細粒流失，由負責工程師設定需補驗的項目與停留點，不能把教學結果當作現場操作許可。","textEn":"At handover, use the following traceable evidence: Replot gradation increments using closely spaced sieves and analyze particles discharged after seepage testing. Record material, geometry and operating-state versions. Address this scenario: Checking only interface ratios misses fine-particle loss within the filter itself. The responsible engineer defines additional checks and hold points; the teaching result is not field operating authorization.","sourceIds":["b-src-water-manuals","v15s-usbr-filters","v15s-fema-seepage","v15s-usbr-embankment-history"]}],"quiz":{"question":"要驗證「級配缺口與內穩」，下列哪一個做法最恰當？","questionEn":"Which approach best verifies \"Gradation gaps and internal stability\"?","options":["只看一次讀值或外觀即可判定合格，不需要基準點、參考試體或重複量測。","顆粒可以重排就保證任何變形後仍連續","用密集篩孔資料重繪級配增量並檢驗滲流後流出顆粒組成。"],"optionsEn":["A single reading or a visual impression is enough to accept the work; no datum, reference specimen or repeat measurement is needed.","Particle rearrangement guarantees continuity after any amount of deformation","Replot gradation increments using closely spaced sieves and analyze particles discharged after seepage testing."],"answer":2,"explanation":"用密集篩孔資料重繪級配增量並檢驗滲流後流出顆粒組成。 驗證需要基準、重複性與事先訂定的允收準則。","explanationEn":"Replot gradation increments using closely spaced sieves and analyze particles discharged after seepage testing. Verification needs a datum, repeatability and acceptance criteria fixed in advance."},"unit":3,"unitFacet":"verification","order":3,"sequence":11},{"id":"b242-v15-12","title":"級配缺口與內穩：失效診斷","titleEn":"Gradation gaps and internal stability: failure diagnosis","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["b-src-water-manuals","v15s-usbr-filters","v15s-fema-seepage","v15s-usbr-embankment-history"],"prerequisiteIds":["b242-v15-11"],"objective":"從症狀倒推「級配缺口與內穩」的失效或劣化原因，提出能區分原因的檢查、矯正與預防措施。","objectiveEn":"Work back from symptoms to the failure or deterioration causes of “Gradation gaps and internal stability” and propose discriminating checks, corrective actions and prevention.","instruction":"只檢查界面粒徑比會漏掉反濾層自身的細粒流失。診斷時應採取以下查核：用密集篩孔資料重繪級配增量並檢驗滲流後流出顆粒組成，確認異常是否同時出現在相關量測；未釐清原因就調整門檻，會使真正的機制變化被資料處理掩蓋。 師傅任務：建立失效樹——症狀、兩個以上可能原因、能區分它們的量測或檢測，以及矯正與預防措施；並說明此失效如何影響整體結構的安全、使用性、耐久或營運。","instructionEn":"Checking only interface ratios misses fine-particle loss within the filter itself. Diagnose it by the following check: Replot gradation increments using closely spaced sieves and analyze particles discharged after seepage testing. Establish whether related measurements corroborate the anomaly; changing thresholds before identifying the cause can conceal a real change in the governing mechanism. Mentor task: build a fault tree with the symptom, at least two candidate causes, a measurement or inspection that tells them apart, and corrective and preventive actions; explain how the failure affects whole-structure safety, serviceability, durability or operation.","observation":"連結機制：這有助於確認模型的水流、受力或量測邊界是否仍成立。","observationEn":"Link to the mechanism: That distinction determines whether the model boundary or measurement assumption remains valid.","failure":"誤判風險：若相信「界面留土合格就表示反濾自身永遠穩定」，上述症狀可能被錯誤處理而反覆出現。","failureEn":"Misdiagnosis risk: believing \"Successful interface retention proves permanent internal filter stability\" leads to mishandling the symptom so it keeps returning.","check":"完成失效樹與矯正措施，指出哪一項量測或檢測能最快確認根因、需要哪些人簽認，以及如何防止再發。","checkEn":"Complete the fault tree and corrective actions, name the measurement or inspection that confirms the root cause fastest, who must sign off, and how recurrence is prevented.","knowledge":[{"id":"b242-v15-12-k1","title":"失效模式","titleEn":"Failure mode","text":"只檢查界面粒徑比會漏掉反濾層自身的細粒流失。診斷時應採取以下查核：用密集篩孔資料重繪級配增量並檢驗滲流後流出顆粒組成，確認異常是否同時出現在相關量測；未釐清原因就調整門檻，會使真正的機制變化被資料處理掩蓋。","textEn":"Checking only interface ratios misses fine-particle loss within the filter itself. Diagnose it by the following check: Replot gradation increments using closely spaced sieves and analyze particles discharged after seepage testing. Establish whether related measurements corroborate the anomaly; changing thresholds before identifying the cause can conceal a real change in the governing mechanism.","sourceIds":["b-src-water-manuals","v15s-usbr-filters","v15s-fema-seepage","v15s-usbr-embankment-history"]},{"id":"b242-v15-12-k2","title":"根因確認","titleEn":"Root-cause confirmation","text":"根因必須以可區分的量測或檢測確認；只補強外觀、更換構件或放寬允收值可能掩蓋問題。","textEn":"Confirm the root cause with a discriminating measurement or inspection; cosmetic repair, swapping components or relaxing limits can mask the problem.","sourceIds":["b-src-water-manuals","v15s-usbr-filters","v15s-fema-seepage","v15s-usbr-embankment-history"]}],"quiz":{"question":"在「級配缺口與內穩」出現異常時，下列哪一項判斷最合理？","questionEn":"When \"Gradation gaps and internal stability\" shows distress, which diagnosis is most reasonable?","options":["只檢查界面粒徑比會漏掉反濾層自身的細粒流失。","裂縫或異常只出現一次就可以忽略，不需要記錄或追蹤。","圖上反濾厚度就是每個現地斷面的厚度"],"optionsEn":["Checking only interface ratios misses fine-particle loss within the filter itself.","A crack or anomaly that appears only once can be ignored without logging or follow-up.","Drawing thickness equals filter thickness at every field section"],"answer":0,"explanation":"只檢查界面粒徑比會漏掉反濾層自身的細粒流失。 需以量測區分可能原因。","explanationEn":"Checking only interface ratios misses fine-particle loss within the filter itself. Discriminate candidate causes by measurement."},"unit":3,"unitFacet":"failure","order":4,"sequence":12},{"id":"b242-v15-13","title":"鋪築厚度與偏差：機制與系統路徑","titleEn":"Placed thickness and tolerances: mechanism and system paths","estimatedMinutes":20,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["b-src-water-manuals","v15s-usbr-filters","v15s-fema-seepage","v15s-usbr-embankment-history"],"prerequisiteIds":["b242-v15-12"],"objective":"說明「鋪築厚度與偏差」如何影響土石壩反濾層設計的受力、變形、水流或訊號表現，並畫出相關輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界。","objectiveEn":"Explain how “Placed thickness and tolerances” governs forces, deformation, flow or signals in “Filter-zone design for embankment dams”, and map the relevant inputs, transfer paths and boundaries.","instruction":"反濾帶的施工厚度須容納放樣、整平與相鄰土區交界的誤差，圖上厚度不等於每個剖面的連續有效厚度。保守幾何扣減可顯示容許誤差如何侵蝕施工餘量；實際評估仍需三維界面成果及接縫、轉角與穿越構造的細部。 驗證時應逐層量測兩側界面並在轉折與穿管位置增加橫斷面紀錄，並辨識以下失效情境：兩側土區同時侵入會使實際反濾帶局部中斷。這有助於確認模型的水流、受力或量測邊界是否仍成立。 師傅任務：以自由體圖、流路圖或訊號圖畫出相關物理量如何經過「鋪築厚度與偏差」傳到系統邊界，標出哪些量由設計決定、哪些由材料、施工或環境決定，再用三句話寫出機制摘要。","instructionEn":"Placed thickness must accommodate survey, grading and adjacent-zone interface errors. The drawing thickness is not the continuous effective thickness at every section. A conservative geometric deduction illustrates how tolerances consume margin; assessment still needs three-dimensional interface records at transitions, corners and penetrations where continuity is vulnerable. Test this interpretation with the following evidence: Survey both interfaces each lift and add cross-sections at bends and pipe penetrations. In particular, distinguish this failure mechanism: Encroachment from both adjacent zones can locally interrupt the filter band. That distinction determines whether the model boundary or measurement assumption remains valid. Mentor task: draw a free-body, flow or signal diagram showing how relevant physical quantities pass through “Placed thickness and tolerances” to the system boundary, mark which quantities are fixed by design and which by materials, construction or environment, then summarise the mechanism in three sentences.","observation":"量級提示：原創教學假設：NominalThickness=0.80 m; leftEncroachment=0.12 m; rightEncroachment=0.08 m; remainingThickness=0.80-0.12-0.08=0.60 m。","observationEn":"Order-of-magnitude cue: Original teaching assumptions: NominalThickness=0.80 m; leftEncroachment=0.12 m; rightEncroachment=0.08 m; remainingThickness=0.80-0.12-0.08=0.60 m.","failure":"常見誤解：「圖上反濾厚度就是每個現地斷面的厚度」這個說法忽略了上述機制；請在系統圖上指出它錯在哪一個環節。","failureEn":"Common misconception: \"Drawing thickness equals filter thickness at every field section\" It ignores the mechanism above; mark on your system diagram where it breaks down.","check":"系統圖標明「鋪築厚度與偏差」的輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界；三句摘要能解釋本步列出的誤解為何不成立。","checkEn":"The system diagram shows inputs, transfer paths and boundaries for “Placed thickness and tolerances”; the three-sentence summary explains why the listed misconception fails.","knowledge":[{"id":"b242-v15-13-k1","title":"鋪築厚度與偏差","titleEn":"Placed thickness and tolerances","text":"反濾帶的施工厚度須容納放樣、整平與相鄰土區交界的誤差，圖上厚度不等於每個剖面的連續有效厚度。保守幾何扣減可顯示容許誤差如何侵蝕施工餘量；實際評估仍需三維界面成果及接縫、轉角與穿越構造的細部。","textEn":"Placed thickness must accommodate survey, grading and adjacent-zone interface errors. The drawing thickness is not the continuous effective thickness at every section.","sourceIds":["b-src-water-manuals","v15s-usbr-filters","v15s-fema-seepage","v15s-usbr-embankment-history"]},{"id":"b242-v15-13-k2","title":"誤解辨析","titleEn":"Misconception check","text":"誤解：圖上反濾厚度就是每個現地斷面的厚度 正確的工程判斷必須回到傳力機制與量級。","textEn":"Misconception: Drawing thickness equals filter thickness at every field section Sound engineering judgement goes back to the load path and magnitude.","sourceIds":["b-src-water-manuals","v15s-usbr-filters","v15s-fema-seepage","v15s-usbr-embankment-history"]}],"quiz":{"question":"關於「鋪築厚度與偏差」，下列哪一項敘述正確？","questionEn":"Which statement about \"Placed thickness and tolerances\" is correct?","options":["圖上反濾厚度就是每個現地斷面的厚度","反濾帶的施工厚度須容納放樣、整平與相鄰土區交界的誤差，圖上厚度不等於每個剖面的連續有效厚度。","批次平均合格就可以忽略局部材料分離"],"optionsEn":["Drawing thickness equals filter thickness at every field section","Placed thickness must accommodate survey, grading and adjacent-zone interface errors.","An acceptable batch average makes local segregation irrelevant"],"answer":1,"explanation":"反濾帶的施工厚度須容納放樣、整平與相鄰土區交界的誤差，圖上厚度不等於每個剖面的連續有效厚度。 其餘選項是常見誤解。","explanationEn":"Placed thickness must accommodate survey, grading and adjacent-zone interface errors. The other options are common misconceptions."},"unit":4,"unitFacet":"mechanism","order":5,"sequence":13},{"id":"b242-v15-14","title":"鋪築厚度與偏差：定量估算","titleEn":"Placed thickness and tolerances: quantitative estimate","estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["b-src-water-manuals","v15s-usbr-filters","v15s-fema-seepage","v15s-usbr-embankment-history"],"prerequisiteIds":["b242-v15-13"],"objective":"以數值模型估算「鋪築厚度與偏差」的關鍵量，並判斷幾何、水頭、荷載或材料參數改變時結果的方向與幅度。","objectiveEn":"Estimate the key quantities of “Placed thickness and tolerances” with a numerical model and judge the direction and size of change when geometry, water head, load or material parameters move.","instruction":"依下列模型逐步重算：原創教學假設：NominalThickness=0.80 m; leftEncroachment=0.12 m; rightEncroachment=0.08 m; remainingThickness=0.80-0.12-0.08=0.60 m。數值只檢查量綱與機制，不是實測資料、設計設定或允收門檻。 師傅任務：保留單位重算一次，再只改變一個輸入（例如增加 10%），預測並計算輸出的變化，說明它是線性、平方或更高次方的關係，並指出規範或設計上通常如何處理這個敏感度。","instructionEn":"Recalculate step by step: Original teaching assumptions: NominalThickness=0.80 m; leftEncroachment=0.12 m; rightEncroachment=0.08 m; remainingThickness=0.80-0.12-0.08=0.60 m. These values check dimensions and mechanism, not measured data, design settings or acceptance thresholds. Mentor task: redo the calculation keeping units, then change one input (for example by +10%), predict and compute the output change, state whether the dependence is linear, quadratic or steeper, and note how codes or designers usually handle this sensitivity.","observation":"如何核對：逐層量測兩側界面並在轉折與穿管位置增加橫斷面紀錄。","observationEn":"How to cross-check: Survey both interfaces each lift and add cross-sections at bends and pipe penetrations.","failure":"計算陷阱：單位換算錯誤、把教學假設當成真實設計值、混淆標稱值與設計值（未乘載重或強度係數），或只看結果不檢查數量級，都會讓後續設計判斷失準。","failureEn":"Calculation traps: unit slips, treating teaching assumptions as real design values, mixing nominal and factored values, or accepting a result without checking its magnitude will mislead later design decisions.","check":"依模型顯示精度重現數值，列出單位與取整方式，並提交一個參數改變後的敏感度計算與工程解釋。","checkEn":"Reproduce the model values to their displayed precision, state units and rounding, and submit a sensitivity calculation for one changed parameter with an engineering explanation.","knowledge":[{"id":"b242-v15-14-k1","title":"定量模型","titleEn":"Quantitative model","text":"原創教學假設：NominalThickness=0.80 m; leftEncroachment=0.12 m; rightEncroachment=0.08 m; remainingThickness=0.80-0.12-0.08=0.60 m。數值只檢查量綱與機制，不是實測資料、設計設定或允收門檻。","textEn":"Original teaching assumptions: NominalThickness=0.80 m; leftEncroachment=0.12 m; rightEncroachment=0.08 m; remainingThickness=0.80-0.12-0.08=0.60 m. These values check dimensions and mechanism, not measured data, design settings or acceptance thresholds.","sourceIds":["b-src-water-manuals","v15s-usbr-filters","v15s-fema-seepage","v15s-usbr-embankment-history"]},{"id":"b242-v15-14-k2","title":"模型邊界","titleEn":"Model boundary","text":"本步數值為教學假設或公開資料的簡化；套用到實際工程前，必須依規範荷載組合、材料試驗與現場量測重新計算並由技師簽證。","textEn":"These numbers are teaching assumptions or simplified public data; before applying them to a real structure, recalculate with code load combinations, material tests and site measurements, certified by a qualified engineer.","sourceIds":["b-src-water-manuals","v15s-usbr-filters","v15s-fema-seepage","v15s-usbr-embankment-history"]}],"quiz":{"question":"依「鋪築厚度與偏差」的定量模型，下列哪一項敘述成立？","questionEn":"According to the quantitative model for \"Placed thickness and tolerances\", which statement holds?","options":["留土功能正常就表示排水出口一定暢通","初期出水清澈就證明持續侵蝕已經停止","原創教學假設：NominalThickness=0.80 m; leftEncroachment=0.12 m; rightEncroachment=0.08 m; remainingThickness=0.80-0.12-0.08=0.60 m。"],"optionsEn":["Successful soil retention guarantees an unobstructed drainage outlet","Initially clear discharge proves that continuing erosion has stopped","Original teaching assumptions: NominalThickness=0.80 m; leftEncroachment=0.12 m; rightEncroachment=0.08 m; remainingThickness=0.80-0.12-0.08=0.60 m."],"answer":2,"explanation":"原創教學假設：NominalThickness=0.80 m; leftEncroachment=0.12 m; rightEncroachment=0.08 m; remainingThickness=0.80-0.12-0.08=0.60 m。 重算時請保留單位。","explanationEn":"Original teaching assumptions: NominalThickness=0.80 m; leftEncroachment=0.12 m; rightEncroachment=0.08 m; remainingThickness=0.80-0.12-0.08=0.60 m. Keep units when recalculating."},"unit":4,"unitFacet":"model","order":6,"sequence":14},{"id":"b242-v15-15","title":"鋪築厚度與偏差：試驗與驗證","titleEn":"Placed thickness and tolerances: testing and verification","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["b-src-water-manuals","v15s-usbr-filters","v15s-fema-seepage","v15s-usbr-embankment-history"],"prerequisiteIds":["b242-v15-14"],"objective":"設計一項可重複的試驗、量測或檢查，驗證「鋪築厚度與偏差」是否符合模型與規範預期，並在量測前訂出允收準則與停工點。","objectiveEn":"Design a repeatable test, measurement or inspection that verifies whether “Placed thickness and tolerances” meets the model and code expectation, fixing acceptance criteria and hold points before measuring.","instruction":"逐層量測兩側界面並在轉折與穿管位置增加橫斷面紀錄。應將原始量測與本單元模型的輸入條件對齊，並針對「兩側土區同時侵入會使實際反濾帶局部中斷」取得獨立證據；同時保留儀器校正、測點位置與時間，避免把不同工況的資料直接相減。 師傅任務：把上述方法寫成試驗或量測計畫，列出儀器與感測器、基準點或參考試體、步驟、比較對象、允收準則與停工點，並估計三項主要不確定度來源。","instructionEn":"Survey both interfaces each lift and add cross-sections at bends and pipe penetrations. Match raw observations to the input conditions of this unit and obtain independent evidence for this specific scenario: Encroachment from both adjacent zones can locally interrupt the filter band. Preserve calibration, location and timing so that unlike operating states are not directly subtracted. Mentor task: turn this into a test or measurement plan listing instruments and sensors, datums or reference specimens, procedure, comparison baseline, acceptance criteria and hold points, and estimate the three largest uncertainty contributions.","observation":"現場實務：交接時以逐層量測兩側界面並在轉折與穿管位置增加橫斷面紀錄作為可追溯證據，保存對應材料、構形與工況版本。針對兩側土區同時侵入會使實際反濾帶局部中斷，由負責工程師設定需補驗的項目與停留點，不能把教學結果當作現場操作許可。","observationEn":"Site practice: At handover, use the following traceable evidence: Survey both interfaces each lift and add cross-sections at bends and pipe penetrations. Record material, geometry and operating-state versions. Address this scenario: Encroachment from both adjacent zones can locally interrupt the filter band. The responsible engineer defines additional checks and hold points; the teaching result is not field operating authorization.","failure":"注意干擾：兩側土區同時侵入會使實際反濾帶局部中斷。 只量一次、沒有可追溯的基準，或不記錄溫度、水頭與施工荷重，就無法分辨真正的偏差與量測誤差。","failureEn":"Watch for interference: Encroachment from both adjacent zones can locally interrupt the filter band. A single reading, no traceable datum, or unrecorded temperature, water head and construction loads make real deviations indistinguishable from measurement error.","check":"提交試驗或量測計畫：儀器、基準、步驟、允收準則、停工點與不確定度預算，並說明如何判定合格或不合格、由誰簽認。","checkEn":"Submit the test or measurement plan: instruments, datums, procedure, acceptance criteria, hold points and uncertainty budget, with the pass/fail rule and who signs it off.","knowledge":[{"id":"b242-v15-15-k1","title":"驗證方法","titleEn":"Verification method","text":"逐層量測兩側界面並在轉折與穿管位置增加橫斷面紀錄。應將原始量測與本單元模型的輸入條件對齊，並針對「兩側土區同時侵入會使實際反濾帶局部中斷」取得獨立證據；同時保留儀器校正、測點位置與時間，避免把不同工況的資料直接相減。","textEn":"Survey both interfaces each lift and add cross-sections at bends and pipe penetrations. Match raw observations to the input conditions of this unit and obtain independent evidence for this specific scenario: Encroachment from both adjacent zones can locally interrupt the filter band. Preserve calibration, location and timing so that unlike operating states are not directly subtracted.","sourceIds":["b-src-water-manuals","v15s-usbr-filters","v15s-fema-seepage","v15s-usbr-embankment-history"]},{"id":"b242-v15-15-k2","title":"現場實務","titleEn":"Site practice","text":"交接時以逐層量測兩側界面並在轉折與穿管位置增加橫斷面紀錄作為可追溯證據，保存對應材料、構形與工況版本。針對兩側土區同時侵入會使實際反濾帶局部中斷，由負責工程師設定需補驗的項目與停留點，不能把教學結果當作現場操作許可。","textEn":"At handover, use the following traceable evidence: Survey both interfaces each lift and add cross-sections at bends and pipe penetrations. Record material, geometry and operating-state versions. Address this scenario: Encroachment from both adjacent zones can locally interrupt the filter band. The responsible engineer defines additional checks and hold points; the teaching result is not field operating authorization.","sourceIds":["b-src-water-manuals","v15s-usbr-filters","v15s-fema-seepage","v15s-usbr-embankment-history"]}],"quiz":{"question":"要驗證「鋪築厚度與偏差」，下列哪一個做法最恰當？","questionEn":"Which approach best verifies \"Placed thickness and tolerances\"?","options":["逐層量測兩側界面並在轉折與穿管位置增加橫斷面紀錄。","不確定度太難估計，報告中只寫最佳值即可。","單一粒徑比可以批准所有不同土類反濾"],"optionsEn":["Survey both interfaces each lift and add cross-sections at bends and pipe penetrations.","Uncertainty is too hard to estimate, so the report may state only the best value.","One grain-size ratio can approve filters for every soil class"],"answer":0,"explanation":"逐層量測兩側界面並在轉折與穿管位置增加橫斷面紀錄。 驗證需要基準、重複性與事先訂定的允收準則。","explanationEn":"Survey both interfaces each lift and add cross-sections at bends and pipe penetrations. Verification needs a datum, repeatability and acceptance criteria fixed in advance."},"unit":4,"unitFacet":"verification","order":7,"sequence":15},{"id":"b242-v15-16","title":"鋪築厚度與偏差：失效診斷","titleEn":"Placed thickness and tolerances: failure diagnosis","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["b-src-water-manuals","v15s-usbr-filters","v15s-fema-seepage","v15s-usbr-embankment-history"],"prerequisiteIds":["b242-v15-15"],"objective":"從症狀倒推「鋪築厚度與偏差」的失效或劣化原因，提出能區分原因的檢查、矯正與預防措施。","objectiveEn":"Work back from symptoms to the failure or deterioration causes of “Placed thickness and tolerances” and propose discriminating checks, corrective actions and prevention.","instruction":"兩側土區同時侵入會使實際反濾帶局部中斷。診斷時應採取以下查核：逐層量測兩側界面並在轉折與穿管位置增加橫斷面紀錄，確認異常是否同時出現在相關量測；未釐清原因就調整門檻，會使真正的機制變化被資料處理掩蓋。 師傅任務：建立失效樹——症狀、兩個以上可能原因、能區分它們的量測或檢測，以及矯正與預防措施；並說明此失效如何影響整體結構的安全、使用性、耐久或營運。","instructionEn":"Encroachment from both adjacent zones can locally interrupt the filter band. Diagnose it by the following check: Survey both interfaces each lift and add cross-sections at bends and pipe penetrations. Establish whether related measurements corroborate the anomaly; changing thresholds before identifying the cause can conceal a real change in the governing mechanism. Mentor task: build a fault tree with the symptom, at least two candidate causes, a measurement or inspection that tells them apart, and corrective and preventive actions; explain how the failure affects whole-structure safety, serviceability, durability or operation.","observation":"連結機制：這有助於確認模型的水流、受力或量測邊界是否仍成立。","observationEn":"Link to the mechanism: That distinction determines whether the model boundary or measurement assumption remains valid.","failure":"誤判風險：若相信「圖上反濾厚度就是每個現地斷面的厚度」，上述症狀可能被錯誤處理而反覆出現。","failureEn":"Misdiagnosis risk: believing \"Drawing thickness equals filter thickness at every field section\" leads to mishandling the symptom so it keeps returning.","check":"完成失效樹與矯正措施，指出哪一項量測或檢測能最快確認根因、需要哪些人簽認，以及如何防止再發。","checkEn":"Complete the fault tree and corrective actions, name the measurement or inspection that confirms the root cause fastest, who must sign off, and how recurrence is prevented.","knowledge":[{"id":"b242-v15-16-k1","title":"失效模式","titleEn":"Failure mode","text":"兩側土區同時侵入會使實際反濾帶局部中斷。診斷時應採取以下查核：逐層量測兩側界面並在轉折與穿管位置增加橫斷面紀錄，確認異常是否同時出現在相關量測；未釐清原因就調整門檻，會使真正的機制變化被資料處理掩蓋。","textEn":"Encroachment from both adjacent zones can locally interrupt the filter band. Diagnose it by the following check: Survey both interfaces each lift and add cross-sections at bends and pipe penetrations. Establish whether related measurements corroborate the anomaly; changing thresholds before identifying the cause can conceal a real change in the governing mechanism.","sourceIds":["b-src-water-manuals","v15s-usbr-filters","v15s-fema-seepage","v15s-usbr-embankment-history"]},{"id":"b242-v15-16-k2","title":"根因確認","titleEn":"Root-cause confirmation","text":"根因必須以可區分的量測或檢測確認；只補強外觀、更換構件或放寬允收值可能掩蓋問題。","textEn":"Confirm the root cause with a discriminating measurement or inspection; cosmetic repair, swapping components or relaxing limits can mask the problem.","sourceIds":["b-src-water-manuals","v15s-usbr-filters","v15s-fema-seepage","v15s-usbr-embankment-history"]}],"quiz":{"question":"在「鋪築厚度與偏差」出現異常時，下列哪一項判斷最合理？","questionEn":"When \"Placed thickness and tolerances\" shows distress, which diagnosis is most reasonable?","options":["先更換最貴的構件；只要症狀消失，就代表已找到根因。","兩側土區同時侵入會使實際反濾帶局部中斷。","批次平均合格就可以忽略局部材料分離"],"optionsEn":["Replace the most expensive component first; if the symptom disappears, the root cause has been found.","Encroachment from both adjacent zones can locally interrupt the filter band.","An acceptable batch average makes local segregation irrelevant"],"answer":1,"explanation":"兩側土區同時侵入會使實際反濾帶局部中斷。 需以量測區分可能原因。","explanationEn":"Encroachment from both adjacent zones can locally interrupt the filter band. Discriminate candidate causes by measurement."},"unit":4,"unitFacet":"failure","order":8,"sequence":16}],"order":2},{"id":"b242-v15-s3","title":"施工方法與施工階段控制","titleEn":"Construction methods and stage control","description":"本階段聚焦「堆置分離與取樣」與「沖洗產率與污染」：先建立機制、系統路徑與定量模型，再設計試驗驗證並診斷失效。","descriptionEn":"This stage covers \"Stockpile segregation and sampling\" and \"Washing yield and contamination\": establish the mechanism, system paths and quantitative model first, then design verification and diagnose failures.","steps":[{"id":"b242-v15-17","title":"堆置分離與取樣：機制與系統路徑","titleEn":"Stockpile segregation and sampling: mechanism and system paths","estimatedMinutes":20,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["b-src-water-manuals","v15s-usbr-filters","v15s-fema-seepage","v15s-usbr-embankment-history"],"prerequisiteIds":["b242-v15-16"],"objective":"說明「堆置分離與取樣」如何影響土石壩反濾層設計的受力、變形、水流或訊號表現，並畫出相關輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界。","objectiveEn":"Explain how “Stockpile segregation and sampling” governs forces, deformation, flow or signals in “Filter-zone design for embankment dams”, and map the relevant inputs, transfer paths and boundaries.","instruction":"卸料時粗粒容易滾至堆腳而細粒集中堆頂，使單一料堆產生不同級配。取樣應覆蓋生產、運輸、鋪築後的位置，不能只取易到達的表面。加權平均可以示範批次質量，卻不能掩蓋局部過粗或過細層造成的流路弱點。 驗證時應比較堆頂堆腳與鋪築後的分區篩分析而非只報混合平均，並辨識以下失效情境：平均級配合格仍可能存在連續過粗條帶。這有助於確認模型的水流、受力或量測邊界是否仍成立。 師傅任務：以自由體圖、流路圖或訊號圖畫出相關物理量如何經過「堆置分離與取樣」傳到系統邊界，標出哪些量由設計決定、哪些由材料、施工或環境決定，再用三句話寫出機制摘要。","instructionEn":"During dumping, coarse particles roll toward the toe while fines remain higher in the pile. Sampling must cover production, transport and placed material rather than an accessible surface alone. A weighted mean describes batch mass balance but cannot conceal local coarse or fine seams that create hydraulic weaknesses. Test this interpretation with the following evidence: Compare sieve analyses from crest, toe and placed zones rather than only a blended average. In particular, distinguish this failure mechanism: An acceptable mean gradation can coexist with a continuous overly coarse strip. That distinction determines whether the model boundary or measurement assumption remains valid. Mentor task: draw a free-body, flow or signal diagram showing how relevant physical quantities pass through “Stockpile segregation and sampling” to the system boundary, mark which quantities are fixed by design and which by materials, construction or environment, then summarise the mechanism in three sentences.","observation":"量級提示：原創教學假設：Two sublots: 60 t at8 percent fines and40 t at2 percent; massWeightedFines=(60*8+40*2)/100=5.6 percent。","observationEn":"Order-of-magnitude cue: Original teaching assumptions: Two sublots: 60 t at8 percent fines and40 t at2 percent; massWeightedFines=(60*8+40*2)/100=5.6 percent.","failure":"常見誤解：「批次平均合格就可以忽略局部材料分離」這個說法忽略了上述機制；請在系統圖上指出它錯在哪一個環節。","failureEn":"Common misconception: \"An acceptable batch average makes local segregation irrelevant\" It ignores the mechanism above; mark on your system diagram where it breaks down.","check":"系統圖標明「堆置分離與取樣」的輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界；三句摘要能解釋本步列出的誤解為何不成立。","checkEn":"The system diagram shows inputs, transfer paths and boundaries for “Stockpile segregation and sampling”; the three-sentence summary explains why the listed misconception fails.","knowledge":[{"id":"b242-v15-17-k1","title":"堆置分離與取樣","titleEn":"Stockpile segregation and sampling","text":"卸料時粗粒容易滾至堆腳而細粒集中堆頂，使單一料堆產生不同級配。取樣應覆蓋生產、運輸、鋪築後的位置，不能只取易到達的表面。","textEn":"During dumping, coarse particles roll toward the toe while fines remain higher in the pile. Sampling must cover production, transport and placed material rather than an accessible surface alone.","sourceIds":["b-src-water-manuals","v15s-usbr-filters","v15s-fema-seepage","v15s-usbr-embankment-history"]},{"id":"b242-v15-17-k2","title":"誤解辨析","titleEn":"Misconception check","text":"誤解：批次平均合格就可以忽略局部材料分離 正確的工程判斷必須回到傳力機制與量級。","textEn":"Misconception: An acceptable batch average makes local segregation irrelevant Sound engineering judgement goes back to the load path and magnitude.","sourceIds":["b-src-water-manuals","v15s-usbr-filters","v15s-fema-seepage","v15s-usbr-embankment-history"]}],"quiz":{"question":"關於「堆置分離與取樣」，下列哪一項敘述正確？","questionEn":"Which statement about \"Stockpile segregation and sampling\" is correct?","options":["批次平均合格就可以忽略局部材料分離","洗料耗水越高就保證反濾料越乾淨","卸料時粗粒容易滾至堆腳而細粒集中堆頂，使單一料堆產生不同級配。"],"optionsEn":["An acceptable batch average makes local segregation irrelevant","Greater washing-water use guarantees cleaner filter material","During dumping, coarse particles roll toward the toe while fines remain higher in the pile."],"answer":2,"explanation":"卸料時粗粒容易滾至堆腳而細粒集中堆頂，使單一料堆產生不同級配。 其餘選項是常見誤解。","explanationEn":"During dumping, coarse particles roll toward the toe while fines remain higher in the pile. The other options are common misconceptions."},"unit":5,"unitFacet":"mechanism","order":1,"sequence":17},{"id":"b242-v15-18","title":"堆置分離與取樣：定量估算","titleEn":"Stockpile segregation and sampling: quantitative estimate","estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["b-src-water-manuals","v15s-usbr-filters","v15s-fema-seepage","v15s-usbr-embankment-history"],"prerequisiteIds":["b242-v15-17"],"objective":"以數值模型估算「堆置分離與取樣」的關鍵量，並判斷幾何、水頭、荷載或材料參數改變時結果的方向與幅度。","objectiveEn":"Estimate the key quantities of “Stockpile segregation and sampling” with a numerical model and judge the direction and size of change when geometry, water head, load or material parameters move.","instruction":"依下列模型逐步重算：原創教學假設：Two sublots: 60 t at8 percent fines and40 t at2 percent; massWeightedFines=(60*8+40*2)/100=5.6 percent。數值只檢查量綱與機制，不是實測資料、設計設定或允收門檻。 師傅任務：保留單位重算一次，再只改變一個輸入（例如增加 10%），預測並計算輸出的變化，說明它是線性、平方或更高次方的關係，並指出規範或設計上通常如何處理這個敏感度。","instructionEn":"Recalculate step by step: Original teaching assumptions: Two sublots: 60 t at8 percent fines and40 t at2 percent; massWeightedFines=(60*8+40*2)/100=5.6 percent. These values check dimensions and mechanism, not measured data, design settings or acceptance thresholds. Mentor task: redo the calculation keeping units, then change one input (for example by +10%), predict and compute the output change, state whether the dependence is linear, quadratic or steeper, and note how codes or designers usually handle this sensitivity.","observation":"如何核對：比較堆頂堆腳與鋪築後的分區篩分析而非只報混合平均。","observationEn":"How to cross-check: Compare sieve analyses from crest, toe and placed zones rather than only a blended average.","failure":"計算陷阱：單位換算錯誤、把教學假設當成真實設計值、混淆標稱值與設計值（未乘載重或強度係數），或只看結果不檢查數量級，都會讓後續設計判斷失準。","failureEn":"Calculation traps: unit slips, treating teaching assumptions as real design values, mixing nominal and factored values, or accepting a result without checking its magnitude will mislead later design decisions.","check":"依模型顯示精度重現數值，列出單位與取整方式，並提交一個參數改變後的敏感度計算與工程解釋。","checkEn":"Reproduce the model values to their displayed precision, state units and rounding, and submit a sensitivity calculation for one changed parameter with an engineering explanation.","knowledge":[{"id":"b242-v15-18-k1","title":"定量模型","titleEn":"Quantitative model","text":"原創教學假設：Two sublots: 60 t at8 percent fines and40 t at2 percent; massWeightedFines=(60*8+40*2)/100=5.6 percent。數值只檢查量綱與機制，不是實測資料、設計設定或允收門檻。","textEn":"Original teaching assumptions: Two sublots: 60 t at8 percent fines and40 t at2 percent; massWeightedFines=(60*8+40*2)/100=5.6 percent. These values check dimensions and mechanism, not measured data, design settings or acceptance thresholds.","sourceIds":["b-src-water-manuals","v15s-usbr-filters","v15s-fema-seepage","v15s-usbr-embankment-history"]},{"id":"b242-v15-18-k2","title":"模型邊界","titleEn":"Model boundary","text":"本步數值為教學假設或公開資料的簡化；套用到實際工程前，必須依規範荷載組合、材料試驗與現場量測重新計算並由技師簽證。","textEn":"These numbers are teaching assumptions or simplified public data; before applying them to a real structure, recalculate with code load combinations, material tests and site measurements, certified by a qualified engineer.","sourceIds":["b-src-water-manuals","v15s-usbr-filters","v15s-fema-seepage","v15s-usbr-embankment-history"]}],"quiz":{"question":"依「堆置分離與取樣」的定量模型，下列哪一項敘述成立？","questionEn":"According to the quantitative model for \"Stockpile segregation and sampling\", which statement holds?","options":["原創教學假設：Two sublots: 60 t at8 percent fines and40 t at2 percent; massWeightedFines=(60*8+40*2)/100=5.6 percent。","管頂反濾覆蓋充分就代表管底同樣連續","顆粒可以重排就保證任何變形後仍連續"],"optionsEn":["Original teaching assumptions: Two sublots: 60 t at8 percent fines and40 t at2 percent; massWeightedFines=(60*8+40*2)/100=5.6 percent.","Adequate filter cover above a conduit proves continuity below it","Particle rearrangement guarantees continuity after any amount of deformation"],"answer":0,"explanation":"原創教學假設：Two sublots: 60 t at8 percent fines and40 t at2 percent; massWeightedFines=(60*8+40*2)/100=5.6 percent。 重算時請保留單位。","explanationEn":"Original teaching assumptions: Two sublots: 60 t at8 percent fines and40 t at2 percent; massWeightedFines=(60*8+40*2)/100=5.6 percent. Keep units when recalculating."},"unit":5,"unitFacet":"model","order":2,"sequence":18},{"id":"b242-v15-19","title":"堆置分離與取樣：試驗與驗證","titleEn":"Stockpile segregation and sampling: testing and verification","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["b-src-water-manuals","v15s-usbr-filters","v15s-fema-seepage","v15s-usbr-embankment-history"],"prerequisiteIds":["b242-v15-18"],"objective":"設計一項可重複的試驗、量測或檢查，驗證「堆置分離與取樣」是否符合模型與規範預期，並在量測前訂出允收準則與停工點。","objectiveEn":"Design a repeatable test, measurement or inspection that verifies whether “Stockpile segregation and sampling” meets the model and code expectation, fixing acceptance criteria and hold points before measuring.","instruction":"比較堆頂堆腳與鋪築後的分區篩分析而非只報混合平均。應將原始量測與本單元模型的輸入條件對齊，並針對「平均級配合格仍可能存在連續過粗條帶」取得獨立證據；同時保留儀器校正、測點位置與時間，避免把不同工況的資料直接相減。 師傅任務：把上述方法寫成試驗或量測計畫，列出儀器與感測器、基準點或參考試體、步驟、比較對象、允收準則與停工點，並估計三項主要不確定度來源。","instructionEn":"Compare sieve analyses from crest, toe and placed zones rather than only a blended average. Match raw observations to the input conditions of this unit and obtain independent evidence for this specific scenario: An acceptable mean gradation can coexist with a continuous overly coarse strip. Preserve calibration, location and timing so that unlike operating states are not directly subtracted. Mentor task: turn this into a test or measurement plan listing instruments and sensors, datums or reference specimens, procedure, comparison baseline, acceptance criteria and hold points, and estimate the three largest uncertainty contributions.","observation":"現場實務：交接時以比較堆頂堆腳與鋪築後的分區篩分析而非只報混合平均作為可追溯證據，保存對應材料、構形與工況版本。針對平均級配合格仍可能存在連續過粗條帶，由負責工程師設定需補驗的項目與停留點，不能把教學結果當作現場操作許可。","observationEn":"Site practice: At handover, use the following traceable evidence: Compare sieve analyses from crest, toe and placed zones rather than only a blended average. Record material, geometry and operating-state versions. Address this scenario: An acceptable mean gradation can coexist with a continuous overly coarse strip. The responsible engineer defines additional checks and hold points; the teaching result is not field operating authorization.","failure":"注意干擾：平均級配合格仍可能存在連續過粗條帶。 只量一次、沒有可追溯的基準，或不記錄溫度、水頭與施工荷重，就無法分辨真正的偏差與量測誤差。","failureEn":"Watch for interference: An acceptable mean gradation can coexist with a continuous overly coarse strip. A single reading, no traceable datum, or unrecorded temperature, water head and construction loads make real deviations indistinguishable from measurement error.","check":"提交試驗或量測計畫：儀器、基準、步驟、允收準則、停工點與不確定度預算，並說明如何判定合格或不合格、由誰簽認。","checkEn":"Submit the test or measurement plan: instruments, datums, procedure, acceptance criteria, hold points and uncertainty budget, with the pass/fail rule and who signs it off.","knowledge":[{"id":"b242-v15-19-k1","title":"驗證方法","titleEn":"Verification method","text":"比較堆頂堆腳與鋪築後的分區篩分析而非只報混合平均。應將原始量測與本單元模型的輸入條件對齊，並針對「平均級配合格仍可能存在連續過粗條帶」取得獨立證據；同時保留儀器校正、測點位置與時間，避免把不同工況的資料直接相減。","textEn":"Compare sieve analyses from crest, toe and placed zones rather than only a blended average. Match raw observations to the input conditions of this unit and obtain independent evidence for this specific scenario: An acceptable mean gradation can coexist with a continuous overly coarse strip. Preserve calibration, location and timing so that unlike operating states are not directly subtracted.","sourceIds":["b-src-water-manuals","v15s-usbr-filters","v15s-fema-seepage","v15s-usbr-embankment-history"]},{"id":"b242-v15-19-k2","title":"現場實務","titleEn":"Site practice","text":"交接時以比較堆頂堆腳與鋪築後的分區篩分析而非只報混合平均作為可追溯證據，保存對應材料、構形與工況版本。針對平均級配合格仍可能存在連續過粗條帶，由負責工程師設定需補驗的項目與停留點，不能把教學結果當作現場操作許可。","textEn":"At handover, use the following traceable evidence: Compare sieve analyses from crest, toe and placed zones rather than only a blended average. Record material, geometry and operating-state versions. Address this scenario: An acceptable mean gradation can coexist with a continuous overly coarse strip. The responsible engineer defines additional checks and hold points; the teaching result is not field operating authorization.","sourceIds":["b-src-water-manuals","v15s-usbr-filters","v15s-fema-seepage","v15s-usbr-embankment-history"]}],"quiz":{"question":"要驗證「堆置分離與取樣」，下列哪一個做法最恰當？","questionEn":"Which approach best verifies \"Stockpile segregation and sampling\"?","options":["允收準則可以等看到量測數據後再決定。","比較堆頂堆腳與鋪築後的分區篩分析而非只報混合平均。","只要反濾材料比較粗就一定能留住基土"],"optionsEn":["Acceptance criteria can be decided after the measured data have been seen.","Compare sieve analyses from crest, toe and placed zones rather than only a blended average.","A coarser filter always retains the protected base soil"],"answer":1,"explanation":"比較堆頂堆腳與鋪築後的分區篩分析而非只報混合平均。 驗證需要基準、重複性與事先訂定的允收準則。","explanationEn":"Compare sieve analyses from crest, toe and placed zones rather than only a blended average. Verification needs a datum, repeatability and acceptance criteria fixed in advance."},"unit":5,"unitFacet":"verification","order":3,"sequence":19},{"id":"b242-v15-20","title":"堆置分離與取樣：失效診斷","titleEn":"Stockpile segregation and sampling: failure diagnosis","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["b-src-water-manuals","v15s-usbr-filters","v15s-fema-seepage","v15s-usbr-embankment-history"],"prerequisiteIds":["b242-v15-19"],"objective":"從症狀倒推「堆置分離與取樣」的失效或劣化原因，提出能區分原因的檢查、矯正與預防措施。","objectiveEn":"Work back from symptoms to the failure or deterioration causes of “Stockpile segregation and sampling” and propose discriminating checks, corrective actions and prevention.","instruction":"平均級配合格仍可能存在連續過粗條帶。診斷時應採取以下查核：比較堆頂堆腳與鋪築後的分區篩分析而非只報混合平均，確認異常是否同時出現在相關量測；未釐清原因就調整門檻，會使真正的機制變化被資料處理掩蓋。 師傅任務：建立失效樹——症狀、兩個以上可能原因、能區分它們的量測或檢測，以及矯正與預防措施；並說明此失效如何影響整體結構的安全、使用性、耐久或營運。","instructionEn":"An acceptable mean gradation can coexist with a continuous overly coarse strip. Diagnose it by the following check: Compare sieve analyses from crest, toe and placed zones rather than only a blended average. Establish whether related measurements corroborate the anomaly; changing thresholds before identifying the cause can conceal a real change in the governing mechanism. Mentor task: build a fault tree with the symptom, at least two candidate causes, a measurement or inspection that tells them apart, and corrective and preventive actions; explain how the failure affects whole-structure safety, serviceability, durability or operation.","observation":"連結機制：這有助於確認模型的水流、受力或量測邊界是否仍成立。","observationEn":"Link to the mechanism: That distinction determines whether the model boundary or measurement assumption remains valid.","failure":"誤判風險：若相信「批次平均合格就可以忽略局部材料分離」，上述症狀可能被錯誤處理而反覆出現。","failureEn":"Misdiagnosis risk: believing \"An acceptable batch average makes local segregation irrelevant\" leads to mishandling the symptom so it keeps returning.","check":"完成失效樹與矯正措施，指出哪一項量測或檢測能最快確認根因、需要哪些人簽認，以及如何防止再發。","checkEn":"Complete the fault tree and corrective actions, name the measurement or inspection that confirms the root cause fastest, who must sign off, and how recurrence is prevented.","knowledge":[{"id":"b242-v15-20-k1","title":"失效模式","titleEn":"Failure mode","text":"平均級配合格仍可能存在連續過粗條帶。診斷時應採取以下查核：比較堆頂堆腳與鋪築後的分區篩分析而非只報混合平均，確認異常是否同時出現在相關量測；未釐清原因就調整門檻，會使真正的機制變化被資料處理掩蓋。","textEn":"An acceptable mean gradation can coexist with a continuous overly coarse strip. Diagnose it by the following check: Compare sieve analyses from crest, toe and placed zones rather than only a blended average. Establish whether related measurements corroborate the anomaly; changing thresholds before identifying the cause can conceal a real change in the governing mechanism.","sourceIds":["b-src-water-manuals","v15s-usbr-filters","v15s-fema-seepage","v15s-usbr-embankment-history"]},{"id":"b242-v15-20-k2","title":"根因確認","titleEn":"Root-cause confirmation","text":"根因必須以可區分的量測或檢測確認；只補強外觀、更換構件或放寬允收值可能掩蓋問題。","textEn":"Confirm the root cause with a discriminating measurement or inspection; cosmetic repair, swapping components or relaxing limits can mask the problem.","sourceIds":["b-src-water-manuals","v15s-usbr-filters","v15s-fema-seepage","v15s-usbr-embankment-history"]}],"quiz":{"question":"在「堆置分離與取樣」出現異常時，下列哪一項判斷最合理？","questionEn":"When \"Stockpile segregation and sampling\" shows distress, which diagnosis is most reasonable?","options":["症狀相同就代表原因相同，不必用量測區分。","洗料耗水越高就保證反濾料越乾淨","平均級配合格仍可能存在連續過粗條帶。"],"optionsEn":["Identical symptoms always mean identical causes, so no discriminating measurement is needed.","Greater washing-water use guarantees cleaner filter material","An acceptable mean gradation can coexist with a continuous overly coarse strip."],"answer":2,"explanation":"平均級配合格仍可能存在連續過粗條帶。 需以量測區分可能原因。","explanationEn":"An acceptable mean gradation can coexist with a continuous overly coarse strip. Discriminate candidate causes by measurement."},"unit":5,"unitFacet":"failure","order":4,"sequence":20},{"id":"b242-v15-21","title":"沖洗產率與污染：機制與系統路徑","titleEn":"Washing yield and contamination: mechanism and system paths","estimatedMinutes":20,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["b-src-water-manuals","v15s-usbr-filters","v15s-fema-seepage","v15s-usbr-embankment-history"],"prerequisiteIds":["b242-v15-20"],"objective":"說明「沖洗產率與污染」如何影響土石壩反濾層設計的受力、變形、水流或訊號表現，並畫出相關輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界。","objectiveEn":"Explain how “Washing yield and contamination” governs forces, deformation, flow or signals in “Filter-zone design for embankment dams”, and map the relevant inputs, transfer paths and boundaries.","instruction":"洗料可移除過量細料，但排出的固體與製程用水需分別計量；產率下降不一定表示洗淨更好，也可能損失原本需要的細砂。以乾質量平衡追蹤進料、合格產物與廢料，再用成品級配及導水試驗確認功能，避免以耗水量代替品質。 驗證時應以乾燥基準質量帳核對洗料前後級配並檢查回用水含泥量，並辨識以下失效情境：高含泥回用水可把剛洗淨的反濾料再次污染。這有助於確認模型的水流、受力或量測邊界是否仍成立。 師傅任務：以自由體圖、流路圖或訊號圖畫出相關物理量如何經過「沖洗產率與污染」傳到系統邊界，標出哪些量由設計決定、哪些由材料、施工或環境決定，再用三句話寫出機制摘要。","instructionEn":"Washing removes excess fines, but solids and process water require separate accounting. Lower yield may mean loss of useful sand rather than better cleaning. Track dry feed, accepted product and rejected solids, then verify gradation and conductivity; water consumption is not a substitute for functional material quality. Test this interpretation with the following evidence: Reconcile dry-mass records with prewash and postwash gradations and inspect recycled-water solids. In particular, distinguish this failure mechanism: Solids-rich recycled water can contaminate freshly washed filter material again. That distinction determines whether the model boundary or measurement assumption remains valid. Mentor task: draw a free-body, flow or signal diagram showing how relevant physical quantities pass through “Washing yield and contamination” to the system boundary, mark which quantities are fixed by design and which by materials, construction or environment, then summarise the mechanism in three sentences.","observation":"量級提示：原創教學假設：DryFeed=120 t; rejectedSolids=9 t; acceptedDryMass=111 t; yield=111/120*100=92.5 percent。","observationEn":"Order-of-magnitude cue: Original teaching assumptions: DryFeed=120 t; rejectedSolids=9 t; acceptedDryMass=111 t; yield=111/120*100=92.5 percent.","failure":"常見誤解：「洗料耗水越高就保證反濾料越乾淨」這個說法忽略了上述機制；請在系統圖上指出它錯在哪一個環節。","failureEn":"Common misconception: \"Greater washing-water use guarantees cleaner filter material\" It ignores the mechanism above; mark on your system diagram where it breaks down.","check":"系統圖標明「沖洗產率與污染」的輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界；三句摘要能解釋本步列出的誤解為何不成立。","checkEn":"The system diagram shows inputs, transfer paths and boundaries for “Washing yield and contamination”; the three-sentence summary explains why the listed misconception fails.","knowledge":[{"id":"b242-v15-21-k1","title":"沖洗產率與污染","titleEn":"Washing yield and contamination","text":"洗料可移除過量細料，但排出的固體與製程用水需分別計量；產率下降不一定表示洗淨更好，也可能損失原本需要的細砂。以乾質量平衡追蹤進料、合格產物與廢料，再用成品級配及導水試驗確認功能，避免以耗水量代替品質。","textEn":"Washing removes excess fines, but solids and process water require separate accounting. Lower yield may mean loss of useful sand rather than better cleaning.","sourceIds":["b-src-water-manuals","v15s-usbr-filters","v15s-fema-seepage","v15s-usbr-embankment-history"]},{"id":"b242-v15-21-k2","title":"誤解辨析","titleEn":"Misconception check","text":"誤解：洗料耗水越高就保證反濾料越乾淨 正確的工程判斷必須回到傳力機制與量級。","textEn":"Misconception: Greater washing-water use guarantees cleaner filter material Sound engineering judgement goes back to the load path and magnitude.","sourceIds":["b-src-water-manuals","v15s-usbr-filters","v15s-fema-seepage","v15s-usbr-embankment-history"]}],"quiz":{"question":"關於「沖洗產率與污染」，下列哪一項敘述正確？","questionEn":"Which statement about \"Washing yield and contamination\" is correct?","options":["洗料可移除過量細料，但排出的固體與製程用水需分別計量；產率下降不一定表示洗淨更好，也可能損失原本需要的細砂。","洗料耗水越高就保證反濾料越乾淨","留土功能正常就表示排水出口一定暢通"],"optionsEn":["Washing removes excess fines, but solids and process water require separate accounting.","Greater washing-water use guarantees cleaner filter material","Successful soil retention guarantees an unobstructed drainage outlet"],"answer":0,"explanation":"洗料可移除過量細料，但排出的固體與製程用水需分別計量；產率下降不一定表示洗淨更好，也可能損失原本需要的細砂。 其餘選項是常見誤解。","explanationEn":"Washing removes excess fines, but solids and process water require separate accounting. The other options are common misconceptions."},"unit":6,"unitFacet":"mechanism","order":5,"sequence":21},{"id":"b242-v15-22","title":"沖洗產率與污染：定量估算","titleEn":"Washing yield and contamination: quantitative estimate","estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["b-src-water-manuals","v15s-usbr-filters","v15s-fema-seepage","v15s-usbr-embankment-history"],"prerequisiteIds":["b242-v15-21"],"objective":"以數值模型估算「沖洗產率與污染」的關鍵量，並判斷幾何、水頭、荷載或材料參數改變時結果的方向與幅度。","objectiveEn":"Estimate the key quantities of “Washing yield and contamination” with a numerical model and judge the direction and size of change when geometry, water head, load or material parameters move.","instruction":"依下列模型逐步重算：原創教學假設：DryFeed=120 t; rejectedSolids=9 t; acceptedDryMass=111 t; yield=111/120*100=92.5 percent。數值只檢查量綱與機制，不是實測資料、設計設定或允收門檻。 師傅任務：保留單位重算一次，再只改變一個輸入（例如增加 10%），預測並計算輸出的變化，說明它是線性、平方或更高次方的關係，並指出規範或設計上通常如何處理這個敏感度。","instructionEn":"Recalculate step by step: Original teaching assumptions: DryFeed=120 t; rejectedSolids=9 t; acceptedDryMass=111 t; yield=111/120*100=92.5 percent. These values check dimensions and mechanism, not measured data, design settings or acceptance thresholds. Mentor task: redo the calculation keeping units, then change one input (for example by +10%), predict and compute the output change, state whether the dependence is linear, quadratic or steeper, and note how codes or designers usually handle this sensitivity.","observation":"如何核對：以乾燥基準質量帳核對洗料前後級配並檢查回用水含泥量。","observationEn":"How to cross-check: Reconcile dry-mass records with prewash and postwash gradations and inspect recycled-water solids.","failure":"計算陷阱：單位換算錯誤、把教學假設當成真實設計值、混淆標稱值與設計值（未乘載重或強度係數），或只看結果不檢查數量級，都會讓後續設計判斷失準。","failureEn":"Calculation traps: unit slips, treating teaching assumptions as real design values, mixing nominal and factored values, or accepting a result without checking its magnitude will mislead later design decisions.","check":"依模型顯示精度重現數值，列出單位與取整方式，並提交一個參數改變後的敏感度計算與工程解釋。","checkEn":"Reproduce the model values to their displayed precision, state units and rounding, and submit a sensitivity calculation for one changed parameter with an engineering explanation.","knowledge":[{"id":"b242-v15-22-k1","title":"定量模型","titleEn":"Quantitative model","text":"原創教學假設：DryFeed=120 t; rejectedSolids=9 t; acceptedDryMass=111 t; yield=111/120*100=92.5 percent。數值只檢查量綱與機制，不是實測資料、設計設定或允收門檻。","textEn":"Original teaching assumptions: DryFeed=120 t; rejectedSolids=9 t; acceptedDryMass=111 t; yield=111/120*100=92.5 percent. These values check dimensions and mechanism, not measured data, design settings or acceptance thresholds.","sourceIds":["b-src-water-manuals","v15s-usbr-filters","v15s-fema-seepage","v15s-usbr-embankment-history"]},{"id":"b242-v15-22-k2","title":"模型邊界","titleEn":"Model boundary","text":"本步數值為教學假設或公開資料的簡化；套用到實際工程前，必須依規範荷載組合、材料試驗與現場量測重新計算並由技師簽證。","textEn":"These numbers are teaching assumptions or simplified public data; before applying them to a real structure, recalculate with code load combinations, material tests and site measurements, certified by a qualified engineer.","sourceIds":["b-src-water-manuals","v15s-usbr-filters","v15s-fema-seepage","v15s-usbr-embankment-history"]}],"quiz":{"question":"依「沖洗產率與污染」的定量模型，下列哪一項敘述成立？","questionEn":"According to the quantitative model for \"Washing yield and contamination\", which statement holds?","options":["初期出水清澈就證明持續侵蝕已經停止","原創教學假設：DryFeed=120 t; rejectedSolids=9 t; acceptedDryMass=111 t; yield=111/120*100=92.5 percent。","單一粒徑比可以批准所有不同土類反濾"],"optionsEn":["Initially clear discharge proves that continuing erosion has stopped","Original teaching assumptions: DryFeed=120 t; rejectedSolids=9 t; acceptedDryMass=111 t; yield=111/120*100=92.5 percent.","One grain-size ratio can approve filters for every soil class"],"answer":1,"explanation":"原創教學假設：DryFeed=120 t; rejectedSolids=9 t; acceptedDryMass=111 t; yield=111/120*100=92.5 percent。 重算時請保留單位。","explanationEn":"Original teaching assumptions: DryFeed=120 t; rejectedSolids=9 t; acceptedDryMass=111 t; yield=111/120*100=92.5 percent. Keep units when recalculating."},"unit":6,"unitFacet":"model","order":6,"sequence":22},{"id":"b242-v15-23","title":"沖洗產率與污染：試驗與驗證","titleEn":"Washing yield and contamination: testing and verification","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["b-src-water-manuals","v15s-usbr-filters","v15s-fema-seepage","v15s-usbr-embankment-history"],"prerequisiteIds":["b242-v15-22"],"objective":"設計一項可重複的試驗、量測或檢查，驗證「沖洗產率與污染」是否符合模型與規範預期，並在量測前訂出允收準則與停工點。","objectiveEn":"Design a repeatable test, measurement or inspection that verifies whether “Washing yield and contamination” meets the model and code expectation, fixing acceptance criteria and hold points before measuring.","instruction":"以乾燥基準質量帳核對洗料前後級配並檢查回用水含泥量。應將原始量測與本單元模型的輸入條件對齊，並針對「高含泥回用水可把剛洗淨的反濾料再次污染」取得獨立證據；同時保留儀器校正、測點位置與時間，避免把不同工況的資料直接相減。 師傅任務：把上述方法寫成試驗或量測計畫，列出儀器與感測器、基準點或參考試體、步驟、比較對象、允收準則與停工點，並估計三項主要不確定度來源。","instructionEn":"Reconcile dry-mass records with prewash and postwash gradations and inspect recycled-water solids. Match raw observations to the input conditions of this unit and obtain independent evidence for this specific scenario: Solids-rich recycled water can contaminate freshly washed filter material again. Preserve calibration, location and timing so that unlike operating states are not directly subtracted. Mentor task: turn this into a test or measurement plan listing instruments and sensors, datums or reference specimens, procedure, comparison baseline, acceptance criteria and hold points, and estimate the three largest uncertainty contributions.","observation":"現場實務：交接時以以乾燥基準質量帳核對洗料前後級配並檢查回用水含泥量作為可追溯證據，保存對應材料、構形與工況版本。針對高含泥回用水可把剛洗淨的反濾料再次污染，由負責工程師設定需補驗的項目與停留點，不能把教學結果當作現場操作許可。","observationEn":"Site practice: At handover, use the following traceable evidence: Reconcile dry-mass records with prewash and postwash gradations and inspect recycled-water solids. Record material, geometry and operating-state versions. Address this scenario: Solids-rich recycled water can contaminate freshly washed filter material again. The responsible engineer defines additional checks and hold points; the teaching result is not field operating authorization.","failure":"注意干擾：高含泥回用水可把剛洗淨的反濾料再次污染。 只量一次、沒有可追溯的基準，或不記錄溫度、水頭與施工荷重，就無法分辨真正的偏差與量測誤差。","failureEn":"Watch for interference: Solids-rich recycled water can contaminate freshly washed filter material again. A single reading, no traceable datum, or unrecorded temperature, water head and construction loads make real deviations indistinguishable from measurement error.","check":"提交試驗或量測計畫：儀器、基準、步驟、允收準則、停工點與不確定度預算，並說明如何判定合格或不合格、由誰簽認。","checkEn":"Submit the test or measurement plan: instruments, datums, procedure, acceptance criteria, hold points and uncertainty budget, with the pass/fail rule and who signs it off.","knowledge":[{"id":"b242-v15-23-k1","title":"驗證方法","titleEn":"Verification method","text":"以乾燥基準質量帳核對洗料前後級配並檢查回用水含泥量。應將原始量測與本單元模型的輸入條件對齊，並針對「高含泥回用水可把剛洗淨的反濾料再次污染」取得獨立證據；同時保留儀器校正、測點位置與時間，避免把不同工況的資料直接相減。","textEn":"Reconcile dry-mass records with prewash and postwash gradations and inspect recycled-water solids. Match raw observations to the input conditions of this unit and obtain independent evidence for this specific scenario: Solids-rich recycled water can contaminate freshly washed filter material again. Preserve calibration, location and timing so that unlike operating states are not directly subtracted.","sourceIds":["b-src-water-manuals","v15s-usbr-filters","v15s-fema-seepage","v15s-usbr-embankment-history"]},{"id":"b242-v15-23-k2","title":"現場實務","titleEn":"Site practice","text":"交接時以以乾燥基準質量帳核對洗料前後級配並檢查回用水含泥量作為可追溯證據，保存對應材料、構形與工況版本。針對高含泥回用水可把剛洗淨的反濾料再次污染，由負責工程師設定需補驗的項目與停留點，不能把教學結果當作現場操作許可。","textEn":"At handover, use the following traceable evidence: Reconcile dry-mass records with prewash and postwash gradations and inspect recycled-water solids. Record material, geometry and operating-state versions. Address this scenario: Solids-rich recycled water can contaminate freshly washed filter material again. The responsible engineer defines additional checks and hold points; the teaching result is not field operating authorization.","sourceIds":["b-src-water-manuals","v15s-usbr-filters","v15s-fema-seepage","v15s-usbr-embankment-history"]}],"quiz":{"question":"要驗證「沖洗產率與污染」，下列哪一個做法最恰當？","questionEn":"Which approach best verifies \"Washing yield and contamination\"?","options":["只要結構分析模型看起來合理，就可以省略現場量測與試驗。","界面留土合格就表示反濾自身永遠穩定","以乾燥基準質量帳核對洗料前後級配並檢查回用水含泥量。"],"optionsEn":["If the structural model looks reasonable, site measurement and testing can be skipped.","Successful interface retention proves permanent internal filter stability","Reconcile dry-mass records with prewash and postwash gradations and inspect recycled-water solids."],"answer":2,"explanation":"以乾燥基準質量帳核對洗料前後級配並檢查回用水含泥量。 驗證需要基準、重複性與事先訂定的允收準則。","explanationEn":"Reconcile dry-mass records with prewash and postwash gradations and inspect recycled-water solids. Verification needs a datum, repeatability and acceptance criteria fixed in advance."},"unit":6,"unitFacet":"verification","order":7,"sequence":23},{"id":"b242-v15-24","title":"沖洗產率與污染：失效診斷","titleEn":"Washing yield and contamination: failure diagnosis","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["b-src-water-manuals","v15s-usbr-filters","v15s-fema-seepage","v15s-usbr-embankment-history"],"prerequisiteIds":["b242-v15-23"],"objective":"從症狀倒推「沖洗產率與污染」的失效或劣化原因，提出能區分原因的檢查、矯正與預防措施。","objectiveEn":"Work back from symptoms to the failure or deterioration causes of “Washing yield and contamination” and propose discriminating checks, corrective actions and prevention.","instruction":"高含泥回用水可把剛洗淨的反濾料再次污染。診斷時應採取以下查核：以乾燥基準質量帳核對洗料前後級配並檢查回用水含泥量，確認異常是否同時出現在相關量測；未釐清原因就調整門檻，會使真正的機制變化被資料處理掩蓋。 師傅任務：建立失效樹——症狀、兩個以上可能原因、能區分它們的量測或檢測，以及矯正與預防措施；並說明此失效如何影響整體結構的安全、使用性、耐久或營運。","instructionEn":"Solids-rich recycled water can contaminate freshly washed filter material again. Diagnose it by the following check: Reconcile dry-mass records with prewash and postwash gradations and inspect recycled-water solids. Establish whether related measurements corroborate the anomaly; changing thresholds before identifying the cause can conceal a real change in the governing mechanism. Mentor task: build a fault tree with the symptom, at least two candidate causes, a measurement or inspection that tells them apart, and corrective and preventive actions; explain how the failure affects whole-structure safety, serviceability, durability or operation.","observation":"連結機制：這有助於確認模型的水流、受力或量測邊界是否仍成立。","observationEn":"Link to the mechanism: That distinction determines whether the model boundary or measurement assumption remains valid.","failure":"誤判風險：若相信「洗料耗水越高就保證反濾料越乾淨」，上述症狀可能被錯誤處理而反覆出現。","failureEn":"Misdiagnosis risk: believing \"Greater washing-water use guarantees cleaner filter material\" leads to mishandling the symptom so it keeps returning.","check":"完成失效樹與矯正措施，指出哪一項量測或檢測能最快確認根因、需要哪些人簽認，以及如何防止再發。","checkEn":"Complete the fault tree and corrective actions, name the measurement or inspection that confirms the root cause fastest, who must sign off, and how recurrence is prevented.","knowledge":[{"id":"b242-v15-24-k1","title":"失效模式","titleEn":"Failure mode","text":"高含泥回用水可把剛洗淨的反濾料再次污染。診斷時應採取以下查核：以乾燥基準質量帳核對洗料前後級配並檢查回用水含泥量，確認異常是否同時出現在相關量測；未釐清原因就調整門檻，會使真正的機制變化被資料處理掩蓋。","textEn":"Solids-rich recycled water can contaminate freshly washed filter material again. Diagnose it by the following check: Reconcile dry-mass records with prewash and postwash gradations and inspect recycled-water solids. Establish whether related measurements corroborate the anomaly; changing thresholds before identifying the cause can conceal a real change in the governing mechanism.","sourceIds":["b-src-water-manuals","v15s-usbr-filters","v15s-fema-seepage","v15s-usbr-embankment-history"]},{"id":"b242-v15-24-k2","title":"根因確認","titleEn":"Root-cause confirmation","text":"根因必須以可區分的量測或檢測確認；只補強外觀、更換構件或放寬允收值可能掩蓋問題。","textEn":"Confirm the root cause with a discriminating measurement or inspection; cosmetic repair, swapping components or relaxing limits can mask the problem.","sourceIds":["b-src-water-manuals","v15s-usbr-filters","v15s-fema-seepage","v15s-usbr-embankment-history"]}],"quiz":{"question":"在「沖洗產率與污染」出現異常時，下列哪一項判斷最合理？","questionEn":"When \"Washing yield and contamination\" shows distress, which diagnosis is most reasonable?","options":["高含泥回用水可把剛洗淨的反濾料再次污染。","只要結構還沒倒，就代表安全餘裕仍然足夠。","留土功能正常就表示排水出口一定暢通"],"optionsEn":["Solids-rich recycled water can contaminate freshly washed filter material again.","As long as the structure is still standing, its safety margin must still be adequate.","Successful soil retention guarantees an unobstructed drainage outlet"],"answer":0,"explanation":"高含泥回用水可把剛洗淨的反濾料再次污染。 需以量測區分可能原因。","explanationEn":"Solids-rich recycled water can contaminate freshly washed filter material again. Discriminate candidate causes by measurement."},"unit":6,"unitFacet":"failure","order":8,"sequence":24}],"order":3},{"id":"b242-v15-s4","title":"試驗、量測與監測驗證","titleEn":"Testing, measurement and monitoring","description":"本階段聚焦「排水截面與水頭」與「穿越構造與反濾環」：先建立機制、系統路徑與定量模型，再設計試驗驗證並診斷失效。","descriptionEn":"This stage covers \"Drain area and hydraulic head\" and \"Penetrations and filter diaphragms\": establish the mechanism, system paths and quantitative model first, then design verification and diagnose failures.","steps":[{"id":"b242-v15-25","title":"排水截面與水頭：機制與系統路徑","titleEn":"Drain area and hydraulic head: mechanism and system paths","estimatedMinutes":20,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["b-src-water-manuals","v15s-usbr-filters","v15s-fema-seepage","v15s-usbr-embankment-history"],"prerequisiteIds":["b242-v15-24"],"objective":"說明「排水截面與水頭」如何影響土石壩反濾層設計的受力、變形、水流或訊號表現，並畫出相關輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界。","objectiveEn":"Explain how “Drain area and hydraulic head” governs forces, deformation, flow or signals in “Filter-zone design for embankment dams”, and map the relevant inputs, transfer paths and boundaries.","instruction":"排水帶應將反濾截獲的水導向可觀測出口，否則留土成功仍可能伴隨不利孔壓。達西估算把導水率、通水面積與長度連到所需水頭差；邊界受堵、局部不飽和或集中流會偏離簡化模型，因此不能以名義尺寸宣稱排水餘裕。 驗證時應以出口流量與沿排水帶孔壓驗證水頭分布並檢查堵塞位置，並辨識以下失效情境：出口堵塞會把原本排水邊界轉成蓄水邊界。這有助於確認模型的水流、受力或量測邊界是否仍成立。 師傅任務：以自由體圖、流路圖或訊號圖畫出相關物理量如何經過「排水截面與水頭」傳到系統邊界，標出哪些量由設計決定、哪些由材料、施工或環境決定，再用三句話寫出機制摘要。","instructionEn":"A drainage zone must carry intercepted water toward an observable outlet; successful retention alone does not prevent adverse pore pressure. A Darcy estimate relates conductivity, area and length to required head difference. Blocked boundaries, partial saturation or concentrated flow can invalidate the simple representation, so nominal geometry does not establish drainage reserve. Test this interpretation with the following evidence: Compare outlet discharge and piezometric heads along the drain and inspect possible blockages. In particular, distinguish this failure mechanism: A blocked outlet changes a drainage boundary into a water-storage boundary. That distinction determines whether the model boundary or measurement assumption remains valid. Mentor task: draw a free-body, flow or signal diagram showing how relevant physical quantities pass through “Drain area and hydraulic head” to the system boundary, mark which quantities are fixed by design and which by materials, construction or environment, then summarise the mechanism in three sentences.","observation":"量級提示：原創教學假設：Q=0.003 m3/s; L=30 m; k=0.01 m/s; A=6 m2; requiredHead=Q*L/(k*A)=1.50 m。","observationEn":"Order-of-magnitude cue: Original teaching assumptions: Q=0.003 m3/s; L=30 m; k=0.01 m/s; A=6 m2; requiredHead=Q*L/(k*A)=1.50 m.","failure":"常見誤解：「留土功能正常就表示排水出口一定暢通」這個說法忽略了上述機制；請在系統圖上指出它錯在哪一個環節。","failureEn":"Common misconception: \"Successful soil retention guarantees an unobstructed drainage outlet\" It ignores the mechanism above; mark on your system diagram where it breaks down.","check":"系統圖標明「排水截面與水頭」的輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界；三句摘要能解釋本步列出的誤解為何不成立。","checkEn":"The system diagram shows inputs, transfer paths and boundaries for “Drain area and hydraulic head”; the three-sentence summary explains why the listed misconception fails.","knowledge":[{"id":"b242-v15-25-k1","title":"排水截面與水頭","titleEn":"Drain area and hydraulic head","text":"排水帶應將反濾截獲的水導向可觀測出口，否則留土成功仍可能伴隨不利孔壓。達西估算把導水率、通水面積與長度連到所需水頭差；邊界受堵、局部不飽和或集中流會偏離簡化模型，因此不能以名義尺寸宣稱排水餘裕。","textEn":"A drainage zone must carry intercepted water toward an observable outlet; successful retention alone does not prevent adverse pore pressure. A Darcy estimate relates conductivity, area and length to required head difference.","sourceIds":["b-src-water-manuals","v15s-usbr-filters","v15s-fema-seepage","v15s-usbr-embankment-history"]},{"id":"b242-v15-25-k2","title":"誤解辨析","titleEn":"Misconception check","text":"誤解：留土功能正常就表示排水出口一定暢通 正確的工程判斷必須回到傳力機制與量級。","textEn":"Misconception: Successful soil retention guarantees an unobstructed drainage outlet Sound engineering judgement goes back to the load path and magnitude.","sourceIds":["b-src-water-manuals","v15s-usbr-filters","v15s-fema-seepage","v15s-usbr-embankment-history"]}],"quiz":{"question":"關於「排水截面與水頭」，下列哪一項敘述正確？","questionEn":"Which statement about \"Drain area and hydraulic head\" is correct?","options":["留土功能正常就表示排水出口一定暢通","排水帶應將反濾截獲的水導向可觀測出口，否則留土成功仍可能伴隨不利孔壓。","管頂反濾覆蓋充分就代表管底同樣連續"],"optionsEn":["Successful soil retention guarantees an unobstructed drainage outlet","A drainage zone must carry intercepted water toward an observable outlet; successful retention alone does not prevent adverse pore pressure.","Adequate filter cover above a conduit proves continuity below it"],"answer":1,"explanation":"排水帶應將反濾截獲的水導向可觀測出口，否則留土成功仍可能伴隨不利孔壓。 其餘選項是常見誤解。","explanationEn":"A drainage zone must carry intercepted water toward an observable outlet; successful retention alone does not prevent adverse pore pressure. The other options are common misconceptions."},"unit":7,"unitFacet":"mechanism","order":1,"sequence":25},{"id":"b242-v15-26","title":"排水截面與水頭：定量估算","titleEn":"Drain area and hydraulic head: quantitative estimate","estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["b-src-water-manuals","v15s-usbr-filters","v15s-fema-seepage","v15s-usbr-embankment-history"],"prerequisiteIds":["b242-v15-25"],"objective":"以數值模型估算「排水截面與水頭」的關鍵量，並判斷幾何、水頭、荷載或材料參數改變時結果的方向與幅度。","objectiveEn":"Estimate the key quantities of “Drain area and hydraulic head” with a numerical model and judge the direction and size of change when geometry, water head, load or material parameters move.","instruction":"依下列模型逐步重算：原創教學假設：Q=0.003 m3/s; L=30 m; k=0.01 m/s; A=6 m2; requiredHead=Q*L/(k*A)=1.50 m。數值只檢查量綱與機制，不是實測資料、設計設定或允收門檻。 師傅任務：保留單位重算一次，再只改變一個輸入（例如增加 10%），預測並計算輸出的變化，說明它是線性、平方或更高次方的關係，並指出規範或設計上通常如何處理這個敏感度。","instructionEn":"Recalculate step by step: Original teaching assumptions: Q=0.003 m3/s; L=30 m; k=0.01 m/s; A=6 m2; requiredHead=Q*L/(k*A)=1.50 m. These values check dimensions and mechanism, not measured data, design settings or acceptance thresholds. Mentor task: redo the calculation keeping units, then change one input (for example by +10%), predict and compute the output change, state whether the dependence is linear, quadratic or steeper, and note how codes or designers usually handle this sensitivity.","observation":"如何核對：以出口流量與沿排水帶孔壓驗證水頭分布並檢查堵塞位置。","observationEn":"How to cross-check: Compare outlet discharge and piezometric heads along the drain and inspect possible blockages.","failure":"計算陷阱：單位換算錯誤、把教學假設當成真實設計值、混淆標稱值與設計值（未乘載重或強度係數），或只看結果不檢查數量級，都會讓後續設計判斷失準。","failureEn":"Calculation traps: unit slips, treating teaching assumptions as real design values, mixing nominal and factored values, or accepting a result without checking its magnitude will mislead later design decisions.","check":"依模型顯示精度重現數值，列出單位與取整方式，並提交一個參數改變後的敏感度計算與工程解釋。","checkEn":"Reproduce the model values to their displayed precision, state units and rounding, and submit a sensitivity calculation for one changed parameter with an engineering explanation.","knowledge":[{"id":"b242-v15-26-k1","title":"定量模型","titleEn":"Quantitative model","text":"原創教學假設：Q=0.003 m3/s; L=30 m; k=0.01 m/s; A=6 m2; requiredHead=Q*L/(k*A)=1.50 m。數值只檢查量綱與機制，不是實測資料、設計設定或允收門檻。","textEn":"Original teaching assumptions: Q=0.003 m3/s; L=30 m; k=0.01 m/s; A=6 m2; requiredHead=Q*L/(k*A)=1.50 m. These values check dimensions and mechanism, not measured data, design settings or acceptance thresholds.","sourceIds":["b-src-water-manuals","v15s-usbr-filters","v15s-fema-seepage","v15s-usbr-embankment-history"]},{"id":"b242-v15-26-k2","title":"模型邊界","titleEn":"Model boundary","text":"本步數值為教學假設或公開資料的簡化；套用到實際工程前，必須依規範荷載組合、材料試驗與現場量測重新計算並由技師簽證。","textEn":"These numbers are teaching assumptions or simplified public data; before applying them to a real structure, recalculate with code load combinations, material tests and site measurements, certified by a qualified engineer.","sourceIds":["b-src-water-manuals","v15s-usbr-filters","v15s-fema-seepage","v15s-usbr-embankment-history"]}],"quiz":{"question":"依「排水截面與水頭」的定量模型，下列哪一項敘述成立？","questionEn":"According to the quantitative model for \"Drain area and hydraulic head\", which statement holds?","options":["顆粒可以重排就保證任何變形後仍連續","只要反濾材料比較粗就一定能留住基土","原創教學假設：Q=0.003 m3/s; L=30 m; k=0.01 m/s; A=6 m2; requiredHead=Q*L/(k*A)=1.50 m。"],"optionsEn":["Particle rearrangement guarantees continuity after any amount of deformation","A coarser filter always retains the protected base soil","Original teaching assumptions: Q=0.003 m3/s; L=30 m; k=0.01 m/s; A=6 m2; requiredHead=Q*L/(k*A)=1.50 m."],"answer":2,"explanation":"原創教學假設：Q=0.003 m3/s; L=30 m; k=0.01 m/s; A=6 m2; requiredHead=Q*L/(k*A)=1.50 m。 重算時請保留單位。","explanationEn":"Original teaching assumptions: Q=0.003 m3/s; L=30 m; k=0.01 m/s; A=6 m2; requiredHead=Q*L/(k*A)=1.50 m. Keep units when recalculating."},"unit":7,"unitFacet":"model","order":2,"sequence":26},{"id":"b242-v15-27","title":"排水截面與水頭：試驗與驗證","titleEn":"Drain area and hydraulic head: testing and verification","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["b-src-water-manuals","v15s-usbr-filters","v15s-fema-seepage","v15s-usbr-embankment-history"],"prerequisiteIds":["b242-v15-26"],"objective":"設計一項可重複的試驗、量測或檢查，驗證「排水截面與水頭」是否符合模型與規範預期，並在量測前訂出允收準則與停工點。","objectiveEn":"Design a repeatable test, measurement or inspection that verifies whether “Drain area and hydraulic head” meets the model and code expectation, fixing acceptance criteria and hold points before measuring.","instruction":"以出口流量與沿排水帶孔壓驗證水頭分布並檢查堵塞位置。應將原始量測與本單元模型的輸入條件對齊，並針對「出口堵塞會把原本排水邊界轉成蓄水邊界」取得獨立證據；同時保留儀器校正、測點位置與時間，避免把不同工況的資料直接相減。 師傅任務：把上述方法寫成試驗或量測計畫，列出儀器與感測器、基準點或參考試體、步驟、比較對象、允收準則與停工點，並估計三項主要不確定度來源。","instructionEn":"Compare outlet discharge and piezometric heads along the drain and inspect possible blockages. Match raw observations to the input conditions of this unit and obtain independent evidence for this specific scenario: A blocked outlet changes a drainage boundary into a water-storage boundary. Preserve calibration, location and timing so that unlike operating states are not directly subtracted. Mentor task: turn this into a test or measurement plan listing instruments and sensors, datums or reference specimens, procedure, comparison baseline, acceptance criteria and hold points, and estimate the three largest uncertainty contributions.","observation":"現場實務：交接時以以出口流量與沿排水帶孔壓驗證水頭分布並檢查堵塞位置作為可追溯證據，保存對應材料、構形與工況版本。針對出口堵塞會把原本排水邊界轉成蓄水邊界，由負責工程師設定需補驗的項目與停留點，不能把教學結果當作現場操作許可。","observationEn":"Site practice: At handover, use the following traceable evidence: Compare outlet discharge and piezometric heads along the drain and inspect possible blockages. Record material, geometry and operating-state versions. Address this scenario: A blocked outlet changes a drainage boundary into a water-storage boundary. The responsible engineer defines additional checks and hold points; the teaching result is not field operating authorization.","failure":"注意干擾：出口堵塞會把原本排水邊界轉成蓄水邊界。 只量一次、沒有可追溯的基準，或不記錄溫度、水頭與施工荷重，就無法分辨真正的偏差與量測誤差。","failureEn":"Watch for interference: A blocked outlet changes a drainage boundary into a water-storage boundary. A single reading, no traceable datum, or unrecorded temperature, water head and construction loads make real deviations indistinguishable from measurement error.","check":"提交試驗或量測計畫：儀器、基準、步驟、允收準則、停工點與不確定度預算，並說明如何判定合格或不合格、由誰簽認。","checkEn":"Submit the test or measurement plan: instruments, datums, procedure, acceptance criteria, hold points and uncertainty budget, with the pass/fail rule and who signs it off.","knowledge":[{"id":"b242-v15-27-k1","title":"驗證方法","titleEn":"Verification method","text":"以出口流量與沿排水帶孔壓驗證水頭分布並檢查堵塞位置。應將原始量測與本單元模型的輸入條件對齊，並針對「出口堵塞會把原本排水邊界轉成蓄水邊界」取得獨立證據；同時保留儀器校正、測點位置與時間，避免把不同工況的資料直接相減。","textEn":"Compare outlet discharge and piezometric heads along the drain and inspect possible blockages. Match raw observations to the input conditions of this unit and obtain independent evidence for this specific scenario: A blocked outlet changes a drainage boundary into a water-storage boundary. Preserve calibration, location and timing so that unlike operating states are not directly subtracted.","sourceIds":["b-src-water-manuals","v15s-usbr-filters","v15s-fema-seepage","v15s-usbr-embankment-history"]},{"id":"b242-v15-27-k2","title":"現場實務","titleEn":"Site practice","text":"交接時以以出口流量與沿排水帶孔壓驗證水頭分布並檢查堵塞位置作為可追溯證據，保存對應材料、構形與工況版本。針對出口堵塞會把原本排水邊界轉成蓄水邊界，由負責工程師設定需補驗的項目與停留點，不能把教學結果當作現場操作許可。","textEn":"At handover, use the following traceable evidence: Compare outlet discharge and piezometric heads along the drain and inspect possible blockages. Record material, geometry and operating-state versions. Address this scenario: A blocked outlet changes a drainage boundary into a water-storage boundary. The responsible engineer defines additional checks and hold points; the teaching result is not field operating authorization.","sourceIds":["b-src-water-manuals","v15s-usbr-filters","v15s-fema-seepage","v15s-usbr-embankment-history"]}],"quiz":{"question":"要驗證「排水截面與水頭」，下列哪一個做法最恰當？","questionEn":"Which approach best verifies \"Drain area and hydraulic head\"?","options":["以出口流量與沿排水帶孔壓驗證水頭分布並檢查堵塞位置。","量測時不必記錄溫度、水頭、水位歷程與施工荷重，因為它們不會影響結果。","圖上反濾厚度就是每個現地斷面的厚度"],"optionsEn":["Compare outlet discharge and piezometric heads along the drain and inspect possible blockages.","Temperature, water head, water-level history and construction loads need not be recorded because they cannot affect the result.","Drawing thickness equals filter thickness at every field section"],"answer":0,"explanation":"以出口流量與沿排水帶孔壓驗證水頭分布並檢查堵塞位置。 驗證需要基準、重複性與事先訂定的允收準則。","explanationEn":"Compare outlet discharge and piezometric heads along the drain and inspect possible blockages. Verification needs a datum, repeatability and acceptance criteria fixed in advance."},"unit":7,"unitFacet":"verification","order":3,"sequence":27},{"id":"b242-v15-28","title":"排水截面與水頭：失效診斷","titleEn":"Drain area and hydraulic head: failure diagnosis","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["b-src-water-manuals","v15s-usbr-filters","v15s-fema-seepage","v15s-usbr-embankment-history"],"prerequisiteIds":["b242-v15-27"],"objective":"從症狀倒推「排水截面與水頭」的失效或劣化原因，提出能區分原因的檢查、矯正與預防措施。","objectiveEn":"Work back from symptoms to the failure or deterioration causes of “Drain area and hydraulic head” and propose discriminating checks, corrective actions and prevention.","instruction":"出口堵塞會把原本排水邊界轉成蓄水邊界。診斷時應採取以下查核：以出口流量與沿排水帶孔壓驗證水頭分布並檢查堵塞位置，確認異常是否同時出現在相關量測；未釐清原因就調整門檻，會使真正的機制變化被資料處理掩蓋。 師傅任務：建立失效樹——症狀、兩個以上可能原因、能區分它們的量測或檢測，以及矯正與預防措施；並說明此失效如何影響整體結構的安全、使用性、耐久或營運。","instructionEn":"A blocked outlet changes a drainage boundary into a water-storage boundary. Diagnose it by the following check: Compare outlet discharge and piezometric heads along the drain and inspect possible blockages. Establish whether related measurements corroborate the anomaly; changing thresholds before identifying the cause can conceal a real change in the governing mechanism. Mentor task: build a fault tree with the symptom, at least two candidate causes, a measurement or inspection that tells them apart, and corrective and preventive actions; explain how the failure affects whole-structure safety, serviceability, durability or operation.","observation":"連結機制：這有助於確認模型的水流、受力或量測邊界是否仍成立。","observationEn":"Link to the mechanism: That distinction determines whether the model boundary or measurement assumption remains valid.","failure":"誤判風險：若相信「留土功能正常就表示排水出口一定暢通」，上述症狀可能被錯誤處理而反覆出現。","failureEn":"Misdiagnosis risk: believing \"Successful soil retention guarantees an unobstructed drainage outlet\" leads to mishandling the symptom so it keeps returning.","check":"完成失效樹與矯正措施，指出哪一項量測或檢測能最快確認根因、需要哪些人簽認，以及如何防止再發。","checkEn":"Complete the fault tree and corrective actions, name the measurement or inspection that confirms the root cause fastest, who must sign off, and how recurrence is prevented.","knowledge":[{"id":"b242-v15-28-k1","title":"失效模式","titleEn":"Failure mode","text":"出口堵塞會把原本排水邊界轉成蓄水邊界。診斷時應採取以下查核：以出口流量與沿排水帶孔壓驗證水頭分布並檢查堵塞位置，確認異常是否同時出現在相關量測；未釐清原因就調整門檻，會使真正的機制變化被資料處理掩蓋。","textEn":"A blocked outlet changes a drainage boundary into a water-storage boundary. Diagnose it by the following check: Compare outlet discharge and piezometric heads along the drain and inspect possible blockages. Establish whether related measurements corroborate the anomaly; changing thresholds before identifying the cause can conceal a real change in the governing mechanism.","sourceIds":["b-src-water-manuals","v15s-usbr-filters","v15s-fema-seepage","v15s-usbr-embankment-history"]},{"id":"b242-v15-28-k2","title":"根因確認","titleEn":"Root-cause confirmation","text":"根因必須以可區分的量測或檢測確認；只補強外觀、更換構件或放寬允收值可能掩蓋問題。","textEn":"Confirm the root cause with a discriminating measurement or inspection; cosmetic repair, swapping components or relaxing limits can mask the problem.","sourceIds":["b-src-water-manuals","v15s-usbr-filters","v15s-fema-seepage","v15s-usbr-embankment-history"]}],"quiz":{"question":"在「排水截面與水頭」出現異常時，下列哪一項判斷最合理？","questionEn":"When \"Drain area and hydraulic head\" shows distress, which diagnosis is most reasonable?","options":["所有異常都來自施工人員失誤，設計與細部不需要檢討。","出口堵塞會把原本排水邊界轉成蓄水邊界。","管頂反濾覆蓋充分就代表管底同樣連續"],"optionsEn":["Every anomaly is a workmanship error, so design and detailing never need review.","A blocked outlet changes a drainage boundary into a water-storage boundary.","Adequate filter cover above a conduit proves continuity below it"],"answer":1,"explanation":"出口堵塞會把原本排水邊界轉成蓄水邊界。 需以量測區分可能原因。","explanationEn":"A blocked outlet changes a drainage boundary into a water-storage boundary. Discriminate candidate causes by measurement."},"unit":7,"unitFacet":"failure","order":4,"sequence":28},{"id":"b242-v15-29","title":"穿越構造與反濾環：機制與系統路徑","titleEn":"Penetrations and filter diaphragms: mechanism and system paths","estimatedMinutes":20,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["b-src-water-manuals","v15s-usbr-filters","v15s-fema-seepage","v15s-usbr-embankment-history"],"prerequisiteIds":["b242-v15-28"],"objective":"說明「穿越構造與反濾環」如何影響土石壩反濾層設計的受力、變形、水流或訊號表現，並畫出相關輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界。","objectiveEn":"Explain how “Penetrations and filter diaphragms” governs forces, deformation, flow or signals in “Filter-zone design for embankment dams”, and map the relevant inputs, transfer paths and boundaries.","instruction":"穿壩管周圍常因夯實受限與差異沉陷形成優先流路，反濾保護需包絡可能的裂縫出口並連接排水。環狀面積算例只量化幾何覆蓋，不能替代基土留土試驗與施工可達性；接頭、底部及側翼的連續性尤其要在封閉前確認。 驗證時應封閉前拍攝管底與兩側反濾接續並核對實測包絡尺寸，並辨識以下失效情境：管底反濾缺口可讓集中滲流繞過已驗收的上部材料。這有助於確認模型的水流、受力或量測邊界是否仍成立。 師傅任務：以自由體圖、流路圖或訊號圖畫出相關物理量如何經過「穿越構造與反濾環」傳到系統邊界，標出哪些量由設計決定、哪些由材料、施工或環境決定，再用三句話寫出機制摘要。","instructionEn":"Conduit surroundings can develop preferential paths through restricted compaction and differential settlement. Filter protection must intercept plausible crack exits and connect to drainage. Annular area quantifies coverage only; it does not replace retention testing or construction access. Check continuity beneath the pipe, at joints and along flanks before burial. Test this interpretation with the following evidence: Photograph filter continuity below and beside the conduit before closure and survey its envelope. In particular, distinguish this failure mechanism: A gap beneath the conduit lets concentrated seepage bypass accepted material above. That distinction determines whether the model boundary or measurement assumption remains valid. Mentor task: draw a free-body, flow or signal diagram showing how relevant physical quantities pass through “Penetrations and filter diaphragms” to the system boundary, mark which quantities are fixed by design and which by materials, construction or environment, then summarise the mechanism in three sentences.","observation":"量級提示：原創教學假設：OuterRadius=1.8 m; conduitRadius=0.6 m; annularArea=pi*(1.8**2-0.6**2)=9.04779 m2。","observationEn":"Order-of-magnitude cue: Original teaching assumptions: OuterRadius=1.8 m; conduitRadius=0.6 m; annularArea=pi*(1.8**2-0.6**2)=9.04779 m2.","failure":"常見誤解：「管頂反濾覆蓋充分就代表管底同樣連續」這個說法忽略了上述機制；請在系統圖上指出它錯在哪一個環節。","failureEn":"Common misconception: \"Adequate filter cover above a conduit proves continuity below it\" It ignores the mechanism above; mark on your system diagram where it breaks down.","check":"系統圖標明「穿越構造與反濾環」的輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界；三句摘要能解釋本步列出的誤解為何不成立。","checkEn":"The system diagram shows inputs, transfer paths and boundaries for “Penetrations and filter diaphragms”; the three-sentence summary explains why the listed misconception fails.","knowledge":[{"id":"b242-v15-29-k1","title":"穿越構造與反濾環","titleEn":"Penetrations and filter diaphragms","text":"穿壩管周圍常因夯實受限與差異沉陷形成優先流路，反濾保護需包絡可能的裂縫出口並連接排水。環狀面積算例只量化幾何覆蓋，不能替代基土留土試驗與施工可達性；接頭、底部及側翼的連續性尤其要在封閉前確認。","textEn":"Conduit surroundings can develop preferential paths through restricted compaction and differential settlement. Filter protection must intercept plausible crack exits and connect to drainage.","sourceIds":["b-src-water-manuals","v15s-usbr-filters","v15s-fema-seepage","v15s-usbr-embankment-history"]},{"id":"b242-v15-29-k2","title":"誤解辨析","titleEn":"Misconception check","text":"誤解：管頂反濾覆蓋充分就代表管底同樣連續 正確的工程判斷必須回到傳力機制與量級。","textEn":"Misconception: Adequate filter cover above a conduit proves continuity below it Sound engineering judgement goes back to the load path and magnitude.","sourceIds":["b-src-water-manuals","v15s-usbr-filters","v15s-fema-seepage","v15s-usbr-embankment-history"]}],"quiz":{"question":"關於「穿越構造與反濾環」，下列哪一項敘述正確？","questionEn":"Which statement about \"Penetrations and filter diaphragms\" is correct?","options":["管頂反濾覆蓋充分就代表管底同樣連續","初期出水清澈就證明持續侵蝕已經停止","穿壩管周圍常因夯實受限與差異沉陷形成優先流路，反濾保護需包絡可能的裂縫出口並連接排水。"],"optionsEn":["Adequate filter cover above a conduit proves continuity below it","Initially clear discharge proves that continuing erosion has stopped","Conduit surroundings can develop preferential paths through restricted compaction and differential settlement."],"answer":2,"explanation":"穿壩管周圍常因夯實受限與差異沉陷形成優先流路，反濾保護需包絡可能的裂縫出口並連接排水。 其餘選項是常見誤解。","explanationEn":"Conduit surroundings can develop preferential paths through restricted compaction and differential settlement. The other options are common misconceptions."},"unit":8,"unitFacet":"mechanism","order":5,"sequence":29},{"id":"b242-v15-30","title":"穿越構造與反濾環：定量估算","titleEn":"Penetrations and filter diaphragms: quantitative estimate","estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["b-src-water-manuals","v15s-usbr-filters","v15s-fema-seepage","v15s-usbr-embankment-history"],"prerequisiteIds":["b242-v15-29"],"objective":"以數值模型估算「穿越構造與反濾環」的關鍵量，並判斷幾何、水頭、荷載或材料參數改變時結果的方向與幅度。","objectiveEn":"Estimate the key quantities of “Penetrations and filter diaphragms” with a numerical model and judge the direction and size of change when geometry, water head, load or material parameters move.","instruction":"依下列模型逐步重算：原創教學假設：OuterRadius=1.8 m; conduitRadius=0.6 m; annularArea=pi*(1.8**2-0.6**2)=9.04779 m2。數值只檢查量綱與機制，不是實測資料、設計設定或允收門檻。 師傅任務：保留單位重算一次，再只改變一個輸入（例如增加 10%），預測並計算輸出的變化，說明它是線性、平方或更高次方的關係，並指出規範或設計上通常如何處理這個敏感度。","instructionEn":"Recalculate step by step: Original teaching assumptions: OuterRadius=1.8 m; conduitRadius=0.6 m; annularArea=pi*(1.8**2-0.6**2)=9.04779 m2. These values check dimensions and mechanism, not measured data, design settings or acceptance thresholds. Mentor task: redo the calculation keeping units, then change one input (for example by +10%), predict and compute the output change, state whether the dependence is linear, quadratic or steeper, and note how codes or designers usually handle this sensitivity.","observation":"如何核對：封閉前拍攝管底與兩側反濾接續並核對實測包絡尺寸。","observationEn":"How to cross-check: Photograph filter continuity below and beside the conduit before closure and survey its envelope.","failure":"計算陷阱：單位換算錯誤、把教學假設當成真實設計值、混淆標稱值與設計值（未乘載重或強度係數），或只看結果不檢查數量級，都會讓後續設計判斷失準。","failureEn":"Calculation traps: unit slips, treating teaching assumptions as real design values, mixing nominal and factored values, or accepting a result without checking its magnitude will mislead later design decisions.","check":"依模型顯示精度重現數值，列出單位與取整方式，並提交一個參數改變後的敏感度計算與工程解釋。","checkEn":"Reproduce the model values to their displayed precision, state units and rounding, and submit a sensitivity calculation for one changed parameter with an engineering explanation.","knowledge":[{"id":"b242-v15-30-k1","title":"定量模型","titleEn":"Quantitative model","text":"原創教學假設：OuterRadius=1.8 m; conduitRadius=0.6 m; annularArea=pi*(1.8**2-0.6**2)=9.04779 m2。數值只檢查量綱與機制，不是實測資料、設計設定或允收門檻。","textEn":"Original teaching assumptions: OuterRadius=1.8 m; conduitRadius=0.6 m; annularArea=pi*(1.8**2-0.6**2)=9.04779 m2. These values check dimensions and mechanism, not measured data, design settings or acceptance thresholds.","sourceIds":["b-src-water-manuals","v15s-usbr-filters","v15s-fema-seepage","v15s-usbr-embankment-history"]},{"id":"b242-v15-30-k2","title":"模型邊界","titleEn":"Model boundary","text":"本步數值為教學假設或公開資料的簡化；套用到實際工程前，必須依規範荷載組合、材料試驗與現場量測重新計算並由技師簽證。","textEn":"These numbers are teaching assumptions or simplified public data; before applying them to a real structure, recalculate with code load combinations, material tests and site measurements, certified by a qualified engineer.","sourceIds":["b-src-water-manuals","v15s-usbr-filters","v15s-fema-seepage","v15s-usbr-embankment-history"]}],"quiz":{"question":"依「穿越構造與反濾環」的定量模型，下列哪一項敘述成立？","questionEn":"According to the quantitative model for \"Penetrations and filter diaphragms\", which statement holds?","options":["原創教學假設：OuterRadius=1.8 m; conduitRadius=0.6 m; annularArea=pi*(1.8**2-0.6**2)=9.04779 m2。","單一粒徑比可以批准所有不同土類反濾","界面留土合格就表示反濾自身永遠穩定"],"optionsEn":["Original teaching assumptions: OuterRadius=1.8 m; conduitRadius=0.6 m; annularArea=pi*(1.8**2-0.6**2)=9.04779 m2.","One grain-size ratio can approve filters for every soil class","Successful interface retention proves permanent internal filter stability"],"answer":0,"explanation":"原創教學假設：OuterRadius=1.8 m; conduitRadius=0.6 m; annularArea=pi*(1.8**2-0.6**2)=9.04779 m2。 重算時請保留單位。","explanationEn":"Original teaching assumptions: OuterRadius=1.8 m; conduitRadius=0.6 m; annularArea=pi*(1.8**2-0.6**2)=9.04779 m2. Keep units when recalculating."},"unit":8,"unitFacet":"model","order":6,"sequence":30},{"id":"b242-v15-31","title":"穿越構造與反濾環：試驗與驗證","titleEn":"Penetrations and filter diaphragms: testing and verification","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["b-src-water-manuals","v15s-usbr-filters","v15s-fema-seepage","v15s-usbr-embankment-history"],"prerequisiteIds":["b242-v15-30"],"objective":"設計一項可重複的試驗、量測或檢查，驗證「穿越構造與反濾環」是否符合模型與規範預期，並在量測前訂出允收準則與停工點。","objectiveEn":"Design a repeatable test, measurement or inspection that verifies whether “Penetrations and filter diaphragms” meets the model and code expectation, fixing acceptance criteria and hold points before measuring.","instruction":"封閉前拍攝管底與兩側反濾接續並核對實測包絡尺寸。應將原始量測與本單元模型的輸入條件對齊，並針對「管底反濾缺口可讓集中滲流繞過已驗收的上部材料」取得獨立證據；同時保留儀器校正、測點位置與時間，避免把不同工況的資料直接相減。 師傅任務：把上述方法寫成試驗或量測計畫，列出儀器與感測器、基準點或參考試體、步驟、比較對象、允收準則與停工點，並估計三項主要不確定度來源。","instructionEn":"Photograph filter continuity below and beside the conduit before closure and survey its envelope. Match raw observations to the input conditions of this unit and obtain independent evidence for this specific scenario: A gap beneath the conduit lets concentrated seepage bypass accepted material above. Preserve calibration, location and timing so that unlike operating states are not directly subtracted. Mentor task: turn this into a test or measurement plan listing instruments and sensors, datums or reference specimens, procedure, comparison baseline, acceptance criteria and hold points, and estimate the three largest uncertainty contributions.","observation":"現場實務：交接時以封閉前拍攝管底與兩側反濾接續並核對實測包絡尺寸作為可追溯證據，保存對應材料、構形與工況版本。針對管底反濾缺口可讓集中滲流繞過已驗收的上部材料，由負責工程師設定需補驗的項目與停留點，不能把教學結果當作現場操作許可。","observationEn":"Site practice: At handover, use the following traceable evidence: Photograph filter continuity below and beside the conduit before closure and survey its envelope. Record material, geometry and operating-state versions. Address this scenario: A gap beneath the conduit lets concentrated seepage bypass accepted material above. The responsible engineer defines additional checks and hold points; the teaching result is not field operating authorization.","failure":"注意干擾：管底反濾缺口可讓集中滲流繞過已驗收的上部材料。 只量一次、沒有可追溯的基準，或不記錄溫度、水頭與施工荷重，就無法分辨真正的偏差與量測誤差。","failureEn":"Watch for interference: A gap beneath the conduit lets concentrated seepage bypass accepted material above. A single reading, no traceable datum, or unrecorded temperature, water head and construction loads make real deviations indistinguishable from measurement error.","check":"提交試驗或量測計畫：儀器、基準、步驟、允收準則、停工點與不確定度預算，並說明如何判定合格或不合格、由誰簽認。","checkEn":"Submit the test or measurement plan: instruments, datums, procedure, acceptance criteria, hold points and uncertainty budget, with the pass/fail rule and who signs it off.","knowledge":[{"id":"b242-v15-31-k1","title":"驗證方法","titleEn":"Verification method","text":"封閉前拍攝管底與兩側反濾接續並核對實測包絡尺寸。應將原始量測與本單元模型的輸入條件對齊，並針對「管底反濾缺口可讓集中滲流繞過已驗收的上部材料」取得獨立證據；同時保留儀器校正、測點位置與時間，避免把不同工況的資料直接相減。","textEn":"Photograph filter continuity below and beside the conduit before closure and survey its envelope. Match raw observations to the input conditions of this unit and obtain independent evidence for this specific scenario: A gap beneath the conduit lets concentrated seepage bypass accepted material above. Preserve calibration, location and timing so that unlike operating states are not directly subtracted.","sourceIds":["b-src-water-manuals","v15s-usbr-filters","v15s-fema-seepage","v15s-usbr-embankment-history"]},{"id":"b242-v15-31-k2","title":"現場實務","titleEn":"Site practice","text":"交接時以封閉前拍攝管底與兩側反濾接續並核對實測包絡尺寸作為可追溯證據，保存對應材料、構形與工況版本。針對管底反濾缺口可讓集中滲流繞過已驗收的上部材料，由負責工程師設定需補驗的項目與停留點，不能把教學結果當作現場操作許可。","textEn":"At handover, use the following traceable evidence: Photograph filter continuity below and beside the conduit before closure and survey its envelope. Record material, geometry and operating-state versions. Address this scenario: A gap beneath the conduit lets concentrated seepage bypass accepted material above. The responsible engineer defines additional checks and hold points; the teaching result is not field operating authorization.","sourceIds":["b-src-water-manuals","v15s-usbr-filters","v15s-fema-seepage","v15s-usbr-embankment-history"]}],"quiz":{"question":"要驗證「穿越構造與反濾環」，下列哪一個做法最恰當？","questionEn":"Which approach best verifies \"Penetrations and filter diaphragms\"?","options":["沿用另一處水工設施或流域的量測結果，就可視為本工程已完成驗證。","封閉前拍攝管底與兩側反濾接續並核對實測包絡尺寸。","批次平均合格就可以忽略局部材料分離"],"optionsEn":["Reusing results from another hydraulic structure or catchment counts as verifying this structure.","Photograph filter continuity below and beside the conduit before closure and survey its envelope.","An acceptable batch average makes local segregation irrelevant"],"answer":1,"explanation":"封閉前拍攝管底與兩側反濾接續並核對實測包絡尺寸。 驗證需要基準、重複性與事先訂定的允收準則。","explanationEn":"Photograph filter continuity below and beside the conduit before closure and survey its envelope. Verification needs a datum, repeatability and acceptance criteria fixed in advance."},"unit":8,"unitFacet":"verification","order":7,"sequence":31},{"id":"b242-v15-32","title":"穿越構造與反濾環：失效診斷","titleEn":"Penetrations and filter diaphragms: failure diagnosis","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["b-src-water-manuals","v15s-usbr-filters","v15s-fema-seepage","v15s-usbr-embankment-history"],"prerequisiteIds":["b242-v15-31"],"objective":"從症狀倒推「穿越構造與反濾環」的失效或劣化原因，提出能區分原因的檢查、矯正與預防措施。","objectiveEn":"Work back from symptoms to the failure or deterioration causes of “Penetrations and filter diaphragms” and propose discriminating checks, corrective actions and prevention.","instruction":"管底反濾缺口可讓集中滲流繞過已驗收的上部材料。診斷時應採取以下查核：封閉前拍攝管底與兩側反濾接續並核對實測包絡尺寸，確認異常是否同時出現在相關量測；未釐清原因就調整門檻，會使真正的機制變化被資料處理掩蓋。 師傅任務：建立失效樹——症狀、兩個以上可能原因、能區分它們的量測或檢測，以及矯正與預防措施；並說明此失效如何影響整體結構的安全、使用性、耐久或營運。","instructionEn":"A gap beneath the conduit lets concentrated seepage bypass accepted material above. Diagnose it by the following check: Photograph filter continuity below and beside the conduit before closure and survey its envelope. Establish whether related measurements corroborate the anomaly; changing thresholds before identifying the cause can conceal a real change in the governing mechanism. Mentor task: build a fault tree with the symptom, at least two candidate causes, a measurement or inspection that tells them apart, and corrective and preventive actions; explain how the failure affects whole-structure safety, serviceability, durability or operation.","observation":"連結機制：這有助於確認模型的水流、受力或量測邊界是否仍成立。","observationEn":"Link to the mechanism: That distinction determines whether the model boundary or measurement assumption remains valid.","failure":"誤判風險：若相信「管頂反濾覆蓋充分就代表管底同樣連續」，上述症狀可能被錯誤處理而反覆出現。","failureEn":"Misdiagnosis risk: believing \"Adequate filter cover above a conduit proves continuity below it\" leads to mishandling the symptom so it keeps returning.","check":"完成失效樹與矯正措施，指出哪一項量測或檢測能最快確認根因、需要哪些人簽認，以及如何防止再發。","checkEn":"Complete the fault tree and corrective actions, name the measurement or inspection that confirms the root cause fastest, who must sign off, and how recurrence is prevented.","knowledge":[{"id":"b242-v15-32-k1","title":"失效模式","titleEn":"Failure mode","text":"管底反濾缺口可讓集中滲流繞過已驗收的上部材料。診斷時應採取以下查核：封閉前拍攝管底與兩側反濾接續並核對實測包絡尺寸，確認異常是否同時出現在相關量測；未釐清原因就調整門檻，會使真正的機制變化被資料處理掩蓋。","textEn":"A gap beneath the conduit lets concentrated seepage bypass accepted material above. Diagnose it by the following check: Photograph filter continuity below and beside the conduit before closure and survey its envelope. Establish whether related measurements corroborate the anomaly; changing thresholds before identifying the cause can conceal a real change in the governing mechanism.","sourceIds":["b-src-water-manuals","v15s-usbr-filters","v15s-fema-seepage","v15s-usbr-embankment-history"]},{"id":"b242-v15-32-k2","title":"根因確認","titleEn":"Root-cause confirmation","text":"根因必須以可區分的量測或檢測確認；只補強外觀、更換構件或放寬允收值可能掩蓋問題。","textEn":"Confirm the root cause with a discriminating measurement or inspection; cosmetic repair, swapping components or relaxing limits can mask the problem.","sourceIds":["b-src-water-manuals","v15s-usbr-filters","v15s-fema-seepage","v15s-usbr-embankment-history"]}],"quiz":{"question":"在「穿越構造與反濾環」出現異常時，下列哪一項判斷最合理？","questionEn":"When \"Penetrations and filter diaphragms\" shows distress, which diagnosis is most reasonable?","options":["補一層塗料或放寬允收值，就能解決大多數劣化問題。","初期出水清澈就證明持續侵蝕已經停止","管底反濾缺口可讓集中滲流繞過已驗收的上部材料。"],"optionsEn":["Adding a coat of paint or widening the acceptance limits solves most deterioration problems.","Initially clear discharge proves that continuing erosion has stopped","A gap beneath the conduit lets concentrated seepage bypass accepted material above."],"answer":2,"explanation":"管底反濾缺口可讓集中滲流繞過已驗收的上部材料。 需以量測區分可能原因。","explanationEn":"A gap beneath the conduit lets concentrated seepage bypass accepted material above. Discriminate candidate causes by measurement."},"unit":8,"unitFacet":"failure","order":8,"sequence":32}],"order":4},{"id":"b242-v15-s5","title":"耐久、維護與工程交接","titleEn":"Durability, maintenance and engineering handoff","description":"本階段聚焦「裂縫流量與留土試驗」與「變形相容與連續性」：先建立機制、系統路徑與定量模型，再設計試驗驗證並診斷失效。","descriptionEn":"This stage covers \"Crack discharge and retention testing\" and \"Deformation compatibility and continuity\": establish the mechanism, system paths and quantitative model first, then design verification and diagnose failures.","steps":[{"id":"b242-v15-33","title":"裂縫流量與留土試驗：機制與系統路徑","titleEn":"Crack discharge and retention testing: mechanism and system paths","estimatedMinutes":20,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["b-src-water-manuals","v15s-usbr-filters","v15s-fema-seepage","v15s-usbr-embankment-history"],"prerequisiteIds":["b242-v15-32"],"objective":"說明「裂縫流量與留土試驗」如何影響土石壩反濾層設計的受力、變形、水流或訊號表現，並畫出相關輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界。","objectiveEn":"Explain how “Crack discharge and retention testing” governs forces, deformation, flow or signals in “Filter-zone design for embankment dams”, and map the relevant inputs, transfer paths and boundaries.","instruction":"反濾應能在基土裂縫供水下阻止持續侵蝕，但裂縫幾何與壓力集中不能由均質達西模型代表。矩形水槽式流量只是給定平均速度的連續方程，不預測裂縫速度；試驗需觀察侵蝕是否停止及流量是否穩定，而非只看最初清水外觀。 驗證時應在指定試驗壓差下同步量測出流與流失乾土質量直到趨勢可判讀，並辨識以下失效情境：只在低壓差做短時試驗可能漏掉後續持續侵蝕。這有助於確認模型的水流、受力或量測邊界是否仍成立。 師傅任務：以自由體圖、流路圖或訊號圖畫出相關物理量如何經過「裂縫流量與留土試驗」傳到系統邊界，標出哪些量由設計決定、哪些由材料、施工或環境決定，再用三句話寫出機制摘要。","instructionEn":"Filters must arrest continuing erosion when a base-soil crack supplies water, a concentrated condition poorly represented by uniform Darcy flow. A rectangular opening calculation applies continuity at a prescribed mean velocity and does not predict crack velocity. Test whether erosion arrests and flow stabilizes rather than judging initial water clarity. Test this interpretation with the following evidence: Measure discharge and lost dry-soil mass together under the specified pressure difference. In particular, distinguish this failure mechanism: A short low-head test may miss continuing erosion at later conditions. That distinction determines whether the model boundary or measurement assumption remains valid. Mentor task: draw a free-body, flow or signal diagram showing how relevant physical quantities pass through “Crack discharge and retention testing” to the system boundary, mark which quantities are fixed by design and which by materials, construction or environment, then summarise the mechanism in three sentences.","observation":"量級提示：原創教學假設：Assumed crack opening=0.004 m; height=0.50 m; measuredMeanVelocity=0.30 m/s; Q=0.004*0.50*0.30=0.00060 m3/s。","observationEn":"Order-of-magnitude cue: Original teaching assumptions: Assumed crack opening=0.004 m; height=0.50 m; measuredMeanVelocity=0.30 m/s; Q=0.004*0.50*0.30=0.00060 m3/s.","failure":"常見誤解：「初期出水清澈就證明持續侵蝕已經停止」這個說法忽略了上述機制；請在系統圖上指出它錯在哪一個環節。","failureEn":"Common misconception: \"Initially clear discharge proves that continuing erosion has stopped\" It ignores the mechanism above; mark on your system diagram where it breaks down.","check":"系統圖標明「裂縫流量與留土試驗」的輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界；三句摘要能解釋本步列出的誤解為何不成立。","checkEn":"The system diagram shows inputs, transfer paths and boundaries for “Crack discharge and retention testing”; the three-sentence summary explains why the listed misconception fails.","knowledge":[{"id":"b242-v15-33-k1","title":"裂縫流量與留土試驗","titleEn":"Crack discharge and retention testing","text":"反濾應能在基土裂縫供水下阻止持續侵蝕，但裂縫幾何與壓力集中不能由均質達西模型代表。矩形水槽式流量只是給定平均速度的連續方程，不預測裂縫速度；試驗需觀察侵蝕是否停止及流量是否穩定，而非只看最初清水外觀。","textEn":"Filters must arrest continuing erosion when a base-soil crack supplies water, a concentrated condition poorly represented by uniform Darcy flow. A rectangular opening calculation applies continuity at a prescribed mean velocity and does not predict crack velocity.","sourceIds":["b-src-water-manuals","v15s-usbr-filters","v15s-fema-seepage","v15s-usbr-embankment-history"]},{"id":"b242-v15-33-k2","title":"誤解辨析","titleEn":"Misconception check","text":"誤解：初期出水清澈就證明持續侵蝕已經停止 正確的工程判斷必須回到傳力機制與量級。","textEn":"Misconception: Initially clear discharge proves that continuing erosion has stopped Sound engineering judgement goes back to the load path and magnitude.","sourceIds":["b-src-water-manuals","v15s-usbr-filters","v15s-fema-seepage","v15s-usbr-embankment-history"]}],"quiz":{"question":"關於「裂縫流量與留土試驗」，下列哪一項敘述正確？","questionEn":"Which statement about \"Crack discharge and retention testing\" is correct?","options":["反濾應能在基土裂縫供水下阻止持續侵蝕，但裂縫幾何與壓力集中不能由均質達西模型代表。","初期出水清澈就證明持續侵蝕已經停止","顆粒可以重排就保證任何變形後仍連續"],"optionsEn":["Filters must arrest continuing erosion when a base-soil crack supplies water, a concentrated condition poorly represented by uniform Darcy flow.","Initially clear discharge proves that continuing erosion has stopped","Particle rearrangement guarantees continuity after any amount of deformation"],"answer":0,"explanation":"反濾應能在基土裂縫供水下阻止持續侵蝕，但裂縫幾何與壓力集中不能由均質達西模型代表。 其餘選項是常見誤解。","explanationEn":"Filters must arrest continuing erosion when a base-soil crack supplies water, a concentrated condition poorly represented by uniform Darcy flow. The other options are common misconceptions."},"unit":9,"unitFacet":"mechanism","order":1,"sequence":33},{"id":"b242-v15-34","title":"裂縫流量與留土試驗：定量估算","titleEn":"Crack discharge and retention testing: quantitative estimate","estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["b-src-water-manuals","v15s-usbr-filters","v15s-fema-seepage","v15s-usbr-embankment-history"],"prerequisiteIds":["b242-v15-33"],"objective":"以數值模型估算「裂縫流量與留土試驗」的關鍵量，並判斷幾何、水頭、荷載或材料參數改變時結果的方向與幅度。","objectiveEn":"Estimate the key quantities of “Crack discharge and retention testing” with a numerical model and judge the direction and size of change when geometry, water head, load or material parameters move.","instruction":"依下列模型逐步重算：原創教學假設：Assumed crack opening=0.004 m; height=0.50 m; measuredMeanVelocity=0.30 m/s; Q=0.004*0.50*0.30=0.00060 m3/s。數值只檢查量綱與機制，不是實測資料、設計設定或允收門檻。 師傅任務：保留單位重算一次，再只改變一個輸入（例如增加 10%），預測並計算輸出的變化，說明它是線性、平方或更高次方的關係，並指出規範或設計上通常如何處理這個敏感度。","instructionEn":"Recalculate step by step: Original teaching assumptions: Assumed crack opening=0.004 m; height=0.50 m; measuredMeanVelocity=0.30 m/s; Q=0.004*0.50*0.30=0.00060 m3/s. These values check dimensions and mechanism, not measured data, design settings or acceptance thresholds. Mentor task: redo the calculation keeping units, then change one input (for example by +10%), predict and compute the output change, state whether the dependence is linear, quadratic or steeper, and note how codes or designers usually handle this sensitivity.","observation":"如何核對：在指定試驗壓差下同步量測出流與流失乾土質量直到趨勢可判讀。","observationEn":"How to cross-check: Measure discharge and lost dry-soil mass together under the specified pressure difference.","failure":"計算陷阱：單位換算錯誤、把教學假設當成真實設計值、混淆標稱值與設計值（未乘載重或強度係數），或只看結果不檢查數量級，都會讓後續設計判斷失準。","failureEn":"Calculation traps: unit slips, treating teaching assumptions as real design values, mixing nominal and factored values, or accepting a result without checking its magnitude will mislead later design decisions.","check":"依模型顯示精度重現數值，列出單位與取整方式，並提交一個參數改變後的敏感度計算與工程解釋。","checkEn":"Reproduce the model values to their displayed precision, state units and rounding, and submit a sensitivity calculation for one changed parameter with an engineering explanation.","knowledge":[{"id":"b242-v15-34-k1","title":"定量模型","titleEn":"Quantitative model","text":"原創教學假設：Assumed crack opening=0.004 m; height=0.50 m; measuredMeanVelocity=0.30 m/s; Q=0.004*0.50*0.30=0.00060 m3/s。數值只檢查量綱與機制，不是實測資料、設計設定或允收門檻。","textEn":"Original teaching assumptions: Assumed crack opening=0.004 m; height=0.50 m; measuredMeanVelocity=0.30 m/s; Q=0.004*0.50*0.30=0.00060 m3/s. These values check dimensions and mechanism, not measured data, design settings or acceptance thresholds.","sourceIds":["b-src-water-manuals","v15s-usbr-filters","v15s-fema-seepage","v15s-usbr-embankment-history"]},{"id":"b242-v15-34-k2","title":"模型邊界","titleEn":"Model boundary","text":"本步數值為教學假設或公開資料的簡化；套用到實際工程前，必須依規範荷載組合、材料試驗與現場量測重新計算並由技師簽證。","textEn":"These numbers are teaching assumptions or simplified public data; before applying them to a real structure, recalculate with code load combinations, material tests and site measurements, certified by a qualified engineer.","sourceIds":["b-src-water-manuals","v15s-usbr-filters","v15s-fema-seepage","v15s-usbr-embankment-history"]}],"quiz":{"question":"依「裂縫流量與留土試驗」的定量模型，下列哪一項敘述成立？","questionEn":"According to the quantitative model for \"Crack discharge and retention testing\", which statement holds?","options":["只要反濾材料比較粗就一定能留住基土","原創教學假設：Assumed crack opening=0.004 m; height=0.50 m; measuredMeanVelocity=0.30 m/s; Q=0.004*0.50*0.30=0.00060 m3/s。","圖上反濾厚度就是每個現地斷面的厚度"],"optionsEn":["A coarser filter always retains the protected base soil","Original teaching assumptions: Assumed crack opening=0.004 m; height=0.50 m; measuredMeanVelocity=0.30 m/s; Q=0.004*0.50*0.30=0.00060 m3/s.","Drawing thickness equals filter thickness at every field section"],"answer":1,"explanation":"原創教學假設：Assumed crack opening=0.004 m; height=0.50 m; measuredMeanVelocity=0.30 m/s; Q=0.004*0.50*0.30=0.00060 m3/s。 重算時請保留單位。","explanationEn":"Original teaching assumptions: Assumed crack opening=0.004 m; height=0.50 m; measuredMeanVelocity=0.30 m/s; Q=0.004*0.50*0.30=0.00060 m3/s. Keep units when recalculating."},"unit":9,"unitFacet":"model","order":2,"sequence":34},{"id":"b242-v15-35","title":"裂縫流量與留土試驗：試驗與驗證","titleEn":"Crack discharge and retention testing: testing and verification","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["b-src-water-manuals","v15s-usbr-filters","v15s-fema-seepage","v15s-usbr-embankment-history"],"prerequisiteIds":["b242-v15-34"],"objective":"設計一項可重複的試驗、量測或檢查，驗證「裂縫流量與留土試驗」是否符合模型與規範預期，並在量測前訂出允收準則與停工點。","objectiveEn":"Design a repeatable test, measurement or inspection that verifies whether “Crack discharge and retention testing” meets the model and code expectation, fixing acceptance criteria and hold points before measuring.","instruction":"在指定試驗壓差下同步量測出流與流失乾土質量直到趨勢可判讀。應將原始量測與本單元模型的輸入條件對齊，並針對「只在低壓差做短時試驗可能漏掉後續持續侵蝕」取得獨立證據；同時保留儀器校正、測點位置與時間，避免把不同工況的資料直接相減。 師傅任務：把上述方法寫成試驗或量測計畫，列出儀器與感測器、基準點或參考試體、步驟、比較對象、允收準則與停工點，並估計三項主要不確定度來源。","instructionEn":"Measure discharge and lost dry-soil mass together under the specified pressure difference. Match raw observations to the input conditions of this unit and obtain independent evidence for this specific scenario: A short low-head test may miss continuing erosion at later conditions. Preserve calibration, location and timing so that unlike operating states are not directly subtracted. Mentor task: turn this into a test or measurement plan listing instruments and sensors, datums or reference specimens, procedure, comparison baseline, acceptance criteria and hold points, and estimate the three largest uncertainty contributions.","observation":"現場實務：交接時以在指定試驗壓差下同步量測出流與流失乾土質量直到趨勢可判讀作為可追溯證據，保存對應材料、構形與工況版本。針對只在低壓差做短時試驗可能漏掉後續持續侵蝕，由負責工程師設定需補驗的項目與停留點，不能把教學結果當作現場操作許可。","observationEn":"Site practice: At handover, use the following traceable evidence: Measure discharge and lost dry-soil mass together under the specified pressure difference. Record material, geometry and operating-state versions. Address this scenario: A short low-head test may miss continuing erosion at later conditions. The responsible engineer defines additional checks and hold points; the teaching result is not field operating authorization.","failure":"注意干擾：只在低壓差做短時試驗可能漏掉後續持續侵蝕。 只量一次、沒有可追溯的基準，或不記錄溫度、水頭與施工荷重，就無法分辨真正的偏差與量測誤差。","failureEn":"Watch for interference: A short low-head test may miss continuing erosion at later conditions. A single reading, no traceable datum, or unrecorded temperature, water head and construction loads make real deviations indistinguishable from measurement error.","check":"提交試驗或量測計畫：儀器、基準、步驟、允收準則、停工點與不確定度預算，並說明如何判定合格或不合格、由誰簽認。","checkEn":"Submit the test or measurement plan: instruments, datums, procedure, acceptance criteria, hold points and uncertainty budget, with the pass/fail rule and who signs it off.","knowledge":[{"id":"b242-v15-35-k1","title":"驗證方法","titleEn":"Verification method","text":"在指定試驗壓差下同步量測出流與流失乾土質量直到趨勢可判讀。應將原始量測與本單元模型的輸入條件對齊，並針對「只在低壓差做短時試驗可能漏掉後續持續侵蝕」取得獨立證據；同時保留儀器校正、測點位置與時間，避免把不同工況的資料直接相減。","textEn":"Measure discharge and lost dry-soil mass together under the specified pressure difference. Match raw observations to the input conditions of this unit and obtain independent evidence for this specific scenario: A short low-head test may miss continuing erosion at later conditions. Preserve calibration, location and timing so that unlike operating states are not directly subtracted.","sourceIds":["b-src-water-manuals","v15s-usbr-filters","v15s-fema-seepage","v15s-usbr-embankment-history"]},{"id":"b242-v15-35-k2","title":"現場實務","titleEn":"Site practice","text":"交接時以在指定試驗壓差下同步量測出流與流失乾土質量直到趨勢可判讀作為可追溯證據，保存對應材料、構形與工況版本。針對只在低壓差做短時試驗可能漏掉後續持續侵蝕，由負責工程師設定需補驗的項目與停留點，不能把教學結果當作現場操作許可。","textEn":"At handover, use the following traceable evidence: Measure discharge and lost dry-soil mass together under the specified pressure difference. Record material, geometry and operating-state versions. Address this scenario: A short low-head test may miss continuing erosion at later conditions. The responsible engineer defines additional checks and hold points; the teaching result is not field operating authorization.","sourceIds":["b-src-water-manuals","v15s-usbr-filters","v15s-fema-seepage","v15s-usbr-embankment-history"]}],"quiz":{"question":"要驗證「裂縫流量與留土試驗」，下列哪一個做法最恰當？","questionEn":"Which approach best verifies \"Crack discharge and retention testing\"?","options":["只看一次讀值或外觀即可判定合格，不需要基準點、參考試體或重複量測。","洗料耗水越高就保證反濾料越乾淨","在指定試驗壓差下同步量測出流與流失乾土質量直到趨勢可判讀。"],"optionsEn":["A single reading or a visual impression is enough to accept the work; no datum, reference specimen or repeat measurement is needed.","Greater washing-water use guarantees cleaner filter material","Measure discharge and lost dry-soil mass together under the specified pressure difference."],"answer":2,"explanation":"在指定試驗壓差下同步量測出流與流失乾土質量直到趨勢可判讀。 驗證需要基準、重複性與事先訂定的允收準則。","explanationEn":"Measure discharge and lost dry-soil mass together under the specified pressure difference. Verification needs a datum, repeatability and acceptance criteria fixed in advance."},"unit":9,"unitFacet":"verification","order":3,"sequence":35},{"id":"b242-v15-36","title":"裂縫流量與留土試驗：失效診斷","titleEn":"Crack discharge and retention testing: failure diagnosis","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["b-src-water-manuals","v15s-usbr-filters","v15s-fema-seepage","v15s-usbr-embankment-history"],"prerequisiteIds":["b242-v15-35"],"objective":"從症狀倒推「裂縫流量與留土試驗」的失效或劣化原因，提出能區分原因的檢查、矯正與預防措施。","objectiveEn":"Work back from symptoms to the failure or deterioration causes of “Crack discharge and retention testing” and propose discriminating checks, corrective actions and prevention.","instruction":"只在低壓差做短時試驗可能漏掉後續持續侵蝕。診斷時應採取以下查核：在指定試驗壓差下同步量測出流與流失乾土質量直到趨勢可判讀，確認異常是否同時出現在相關量測；未釐清原因就調整門檻，會使真正的機制變化被資料處理掩蓋。 師傅任務：建立失效樹——症狀、兩個以上可能原因、能區分它們的量測或檢測，以及矯正與預防措施；並說明此失效如何影響整體結構的安全、使用性、耐久或營運。","instructionEn":"A short low-head test may miss continuing erosion at later conditions. Diagnose it by the following check: Measure discharge and lost dry-soil mass together under the specified pressure difference. Establish whether related measurements corroborate the anomaly; changing thresholds before identifying the cause can conceal a real change in the governing mechanism. Mentor task: build a fault tree with the symptom, at least two candidate causes, a measurement or inspection that tells them apart, and corrective and preventive actions; explain how the failure affects whole-structure safety, serviceability, durability or operation.","observation":"連結機制：這有助於確認模型的水流、受力或量測邊界是否仍成立。","observationEn":"Link to the mechanism: That distinction determines whether the model boundary or measurement assumption remains valid.","failure":"誤判風險：若相信「初期出水清澈就證明持續侵蝕已經停止」，上述症狀可能被錯誤處理而反覆出現。","failureEn":"Misdiagnosis risk: believing \"Initially clear discharge proves that continuing erosion has stopped\" leads to mishandling the symptom so it keeps returning.","check":"完成失效樹與矯正措施，指出哪一項量測或檢測能最快確認根因、需要哪些人簽認，以及如何防止再發。","checkEn":"Complete the fault tree and corrective actions, name the measurement or inspection that confirms the root cause fastest, who must sign off, and how recurrence is prevented.","knowledge":[{"id":"b242-v15-36-k1","title":"失效模式","titleEn":"Failure mode","text":"只在低壓差做短時試驗可能漏掉後續持續侵蝕。診斷時應採取以下查核：在指定試驗壓差下同步量測出流與流失乾土質量直到趨勢可判讀，確認異常是否同時出現在相關量測；未釐清原因就調整門檻，會使真正的機制變化被資料處理掩蓋。","textEn":"A short low-head test may miss continuing erosion at later conditions. Diagnose it by the following check: Measure discharge and lost dry-soil mass together under the specified pressure difference. Establish whether related measurements corroborate the anomaly; changing thresholds before identifying the cause can conceal a real change in the governing mechanism.","sourceIds":["b-src-water-manuals","v15s-usbr-filters","v15s-fema-seepage","v15s-usbr-embankment-history"]},{"id":"b242-v15-36-k2","title":"根因確認","titleEn":"Root-cause confirmation","text":"根因必須以可區分的量測或檢測確認；只補強外觀、更換構件或放寬允收值可能掩蓋問題。","textEn":"Confirm the root cause with a discriminating measurement or inspection; cosmetic repair, swapping components or relaxing limits can mask the problem.","sourceIds":["b-src-water-manuals","v15s-usbr-filters","v15s-fema-seepage","v15s-usbr-embankment-history"]}],"quiz":{"question":"在「裂縫流量與留土試驗」出現異常時，下列哪一項判斷最合理？","questionEn":"When \"Crack discharge and retention testing\" shows distress, which diagnosis is most reasonable?","options":["只在低壓差做短時試驗可能漏掉後續持續侵蝕。","裂縫或異常只出現一次就可以忽略，不需要記錄或追蹤。","顆粒可以重排就保證任何變形後仍連續"],"optionsEn":["A short low-head test may miss continuing erosion at later conditions.","A crack or anomaly that appears only once can be ignored without logging or follow-up.","Particle rearrangement guarantees continuity after any amount of deformation"],"answer":0,"explanation":"只在低壓差做短時試驗可能漏掉後續持續侵蝕。 需以量測區分可能原因。","explanationEn":"A short low-head test may miss continuing erosion at later conditions. Discriminate candidate causes by measurement."},"unit":9,"unitFacet":"failure","order":4,"sequence":36},{"id":"b242-v15-37","title":"變形相容與連續性：機制與系統路徑","titleEn":"Deformation compatibility and continuity: mechanism and system paths","estimatedMinutes":20,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["b-src-water-manuals","v15s-usbr-filters","v15s-fema-seepage","v15s-usbr-embankment-history"],"prerequisiteIds":["b242-v15-36"],"objective":"說明「變形相容與連續性」如何影響土石壩反濾層設計的受力、變形、水流或訊號表現，並畫出相關輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界。","objectiveEn":"Explain how “Deformation compatibility and continuity” governs forces, deformation, flow or signals in “Filter-zone design for embankment dams”, and map the relevant inputs, transfer paths and boundaries.","instruction":"壩體沉陷會使反濾帶彎折、剪切或與剛性構造分離，顆粒材料可重排但不保證任意變形後仍連續。簡化平均剪應變只描述位移差與帶厚的比例，不能直接推得滲透能力；應把施工後測量、沉陷觀測與材料大型試驗連成證據。 驗證時應比較相鄰沉陷測點與接觸面開口並檢查變形後材料連續性，並辨識以下失效情境：與剛性牆面脫離會形成繞過反濾的集中水路。這有助於確認模型的水流、受力或量測邊界是否仍成立。 師傅任務：以自由體圖、流路圖或訊號圖畫出相關物理量如何經過「變形相容與連續性」傳到系統邊界，標出哪些量由設計決定、哪些由材料、施工或環境決定，再用三句話寫出機制摘要。","instructionEn":"Dam settlement can bend or shear a filter zone and separate it from rigid structures. Granular rearrangement does not guarantee continuity after arbitrary deformation. An average shear-strain estimate describes relative displacement across thickness, not remaining conductivity; combine as-built surveys, settlement observations and representative large-scale material tests. Test this interpretation with the following evidence: Compare neighboring settlement points and interface openings and examine post-deformation material continuity. In particular, distinguish this failure mechanism: Separation from a rigid wall creates a concentrated path around the filter. That distinction determines whether the model boundary or measurement assumption remains valid. Mentor task: draw a free-body, flow or signal diagram showing how relevant physical quantities pass through “Deformation compatibility and continuity” to the system boundary, mark which quantities are fixed by design and which by materials, construction or environment, then summarise the mechanism in three sentences.","observation":"量級提示：原創教學假設：RelativeOffset=0.045 m; transitionThickness=0.75 m; averageShearStrain=0.045/0.75=0.060 dimensionless。","observationEn":"Order-of-magnitude cue: Original teaching assumptions: RelativeOffset=0.045 m; transitionThickness=0.75 m; averageShearStrain=0.045/0.75=0.060 dimensionless.","failure":"常見誤解：「顆粒可以重排就保證任何變形後仍連續」這個說法忽略了上述機制；請在系統圖上指出它錯在哪一個環節。","failureEn":"Common misconception: \"Particle rearrangement guarantees continuity after any amount of deformation\" It ignores the mechanism above; mark on your system diagram where it breaks down.","check":"系統圖標明「變形相容與連續性」的輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界；三句摘要能解釋本步列出的誤解為何不成立。","checkEn":"The system diagram shows inputs, transfer paths and boundaries for “Deformation compatibility and continuity”; the three-sentence summary explains why the listed misconception fails.","knowledge":[{"id":"b242-v15-37-k1","title":"變形相容與連續性","titleEn":"Deformation compatibility and continuity","text":"壩體沉陷會使反濾帶彎折、剪切或與剛性構造分離，顆粒材料可重排但不保證任意變形後仍連續。簡化平均剪應變只描述位移差與帶厚的比例，不能直接推得滲透能力；應把施工後測量、沉陷觀測與材料大型試驗連成證據。","textEn":"Dam settlement can bend or shear a filter zone and separate it from rigid structures. Granular rearrangement does not guarantee continuity after arbitrary deformation.","sourceIds":["b-src-water-manuals","v15s-usbr-filters","v15s-fema-seepage","v15s-usbr-embankment-history"]},{"id":"b242-v15-37-k2","title":"誤解辨析","titleEn":"Misconception check","text":"誤解：顆粒可以重排就保證任何變形後仍連續 正確的工程判斷必須回到傳力機制與量級。","textEn":"Misconception: Particle rearrangement guarantees continuity after any amount of deformation Sound engineering judgement goes back to the load path and magnitude.","sourceIds":["b-src-water-manuals","v15s-usbr-filters","v15s-fema-seepage","v15s-usbr-embankment-history"]}],"quiz":{"question":"關於「變形相容與連續性」，下列哪一項敘述正確？","questionEn":"Which statement about \"Deformation compatibility and continuity\" is correct?","options":["顆粒可以重排就保證任何變形後仍連續","壩體沉陷會使反濾帶彎折、剪切或與剛性構造分離，顆粒材料可重排但不保證任意變形後仍連續。","單一粒徑比可以批准所有不同土類反濾"],"optionsEn":["Particle rearrangement guarantees continuity after any amount of deformation","Dam settlement can bend or shear a filter zone and separate it from rigid structures.","One grain-size ratio can approve filters for every soil class"],"answer":1,"explanation":"壩體沉陷會使反濾帶彎折、剪切或與剛性構造分離，顆粒材料可重排但不保證任意變形後仍連續。 其餘選項是常見誤解。","explanationEn":"Dam settlement can bend or shear a filter zone and separate it from rigid structures. The other options are common misconceptions."},"unit":10,"unitFacet":"mechanism","order":5,"sequence":37},{"id":"b242-v15-38","title":"變形相容與連續性：定量估算","titleEn":"Deformation compatibility and continuity: quantitative estimate","estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["b-src-water-manuals","v15s-usbr-filters","v15s-fema-seepage","v15s-usbr-embankment-history"],"prerequisiteIds":["b242-v15-37"],"objective":"以數值模型估算「變形相容與連續性」的關鍵量，並判斷幾何、水頭、荷載或材料參數改變時結果的方向與幅度。","objectiveEn":"Estimate the key quantities of “Deformation compatibility and continuity” with a numerical model and judge the direction and size of change when geometry, water head, load or material parameters move.","instruction":"依下列模型逐步重算：原創教學假設：RelativeOffset=0.045 m; transitionThickness=0.75 m; averageShearStrain=0.045/0.75=0.060 dimensionless。數值只檢查量綱與機制，不是實測資料、設計設定或允收門檻。 師傅任務：保留單位重算一次，再只改變一個輸入（例如增加 10%），預測並計算輸出的變化，說明它是線性、平方或更高次方的關係，並指出規範或設計上通常如何處理這個敏感度。","instructionEn":"Recalculate step by step: Original teaching assumptions: RelativeOffset=0.045 m; transitionThickness=0.75 m; averageShearStrain=0.045/0.75=0.060 dimensionless. These values check dimensions and mechanism, not measured data, design settings or acceptance thresholds. Mentor task: redo the calculation keeping units, then change one input (for example by +10%), predict and compute the output change, state whether the dependence is linear, quadratic or steeper, and note how codes or designers usually handle this sensitivity.","observation":"如何核對：比較相鄰沉陷測點與接觸面開口並檢查變形後材料連續性。","observationEn":"How to cross-check: Compare neighboring settlement points and interface openings and examine post-deformation material continuity.","failure":"計算陷阱：單位換算錯誤、把教學假設當成真實設計值、混淆標稱值與設計值（未乘載重或強度係數），或只看結果不檢查數量級，都會讓後續設計判斷失準。","failureEn":"Calculation traps: unit slips, treating teaching assumptions as real design values, mixing nominal and factored values, or accepting a result without checking its magnitude will mislead later design decisions.","check":"依模型顯示精度重現數值，列出單位與取整方式，並提交一個參數改變後的敏感度計算與工程解釋。","checkEn":"Reproduce the model values to their displayed precision, state units and rounding, and submit a sensitivity calculation for one changed parameter with an engineering explanation.","knowledge":[{"id":"b242-v15-38-k1","title":"定量模型","titleEn":"Quantitative model","text":"原創教學假設：RelativeOffset=0.045 m; transitionThickness=0.75 m; averageShearStrain=0.045/0.75=0.060 dimensionless。數值只檢查量綱與機制，不是實測資料、設計設定或允收門檻。","textEn":"Original teaching assumptions: RelativeOffset=0.045 m; transitionThickness=0.75 m; averageShearStrain=0.045/0.75=0.060 dimensionless. These values check dimensions and mechanism, not measured data, design settings or acceptance thresholds.","sourceIds":["b-src-water-manuals","v15s-usbr-filters","v15s-fema-seepage","v15s-usbr-embankment-history"]},{"id":"b242-v15-38-k2","title":"模型邊界","titleEn":"Model boundary","text":"本步數值為教學假設或公開資料的簡化；套用到實際工程前，必須依規範荷載組合、材料試驗與現場量測重新計算並由技師簽證。","textEn":"These numbers are teaching assumptions or simplified public data; before applying them to a real structure, recalculate with code load combinations, material tests and site measurements, certified by a qualified engineer.","sourceIds":["b-src-water-manuals","v15s-usbr-filters","v15s-fema-seepage","v15s-usbr-embankment-history"]}],"quiz":{"question":"依「變形相容與連續性」的定量模型，下列哪一項敘述成立？","questionEn":"According to the quantitative model for \"Deformation compatibility and continuity\", which statement holds?","options":["界面留土合格就表示反濾自身永遠穩定","批次平均合格就可以忽略局部材料分離","原創教學假設：RelativeOffset=0.045 m; transitionThickness=0.75 m; averageShearStrain=0.045/0.75=0.060 dimensionless。"],"optionsEn":["Successful interface retention proves permanent internal filter stability","An acceptable batch average makes local segregation irrelevant","Original teaching assumptions: RelativeOffset=0.045 m; transitionThickness=0.75 m; averageShearStrain=0.045/0.75=0.060 dimensionless."],"answer":2,"explanation":"原創教學假設：RelativeOffset=0.045 m; transitionThickness=0.75 m; averageShearStrain=0.045/0.75=0.060 dimensionless。 重算時請保留單位。","explanationEn":"Original teaching assumptions: RelativeOffset=0.045 m; transitionThickness=0.75 m; averageShearStrain=0.045/0.75=0.060 dimensionless. Keep units when recalculating."},"unit":10,"unitFacet":"model","order":6,"sequence":38},{"id":"b242-v15-39","title":"變形相容與連續性：試驗與驗證","titleEn":"Deformation compatibility and continuity: testing and verification","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["b-src-water-manuals","v15s-usbr-filters","v15s-fema-seepage","v15s-usbr-embankment-history"],"prerequisiteIds":["b242-v15-38"],"objective":"設計一項可重複的試驗、量測或檢查，驗證「變形相容與連續性」是否符合模型與規範預期，並在量測前訂出允收準則與停工點。","objectiveEn":"Design a repeatable test, measurement or inspection that verifies whether “Deformation compatibility and continuity” meets the model and code expectation, fixing acceptance criteria and hold points before measuring.","instruction":"比較相鄰沉陷測點與接觸面開口並檢查變形後材料連續性。應將原始量測與本單元模型的輸入條件對齊，並針對「與剛性牆面脫離會形成繞過反濾的集中水路」取得獨立證據；同時保留儀器校正、測點位置與時間，避免把不同工況的資料直接相減。 師傅任務：把上述方法寫成試驗或量測計畫，列出儀器與感測器、基準點或參考試體、步驟、比較對象、允收準則與停工點，並估計三項主要不確定度來源。","instructionEn":"Compare neighboring settlement points and interface openings and examine post-deformation material continuity. Match raw observations to the input conditions of this unit and obtain independent evidence for this specific scenario: Separation from a rigid wall creates a concentrated path around the filter. Preserve calibration, location and timing so that unlike operating states are not directly subtracted. Mentor task: turn this into a test or measurement plan listing instruments and sensors, datums or reference specimens, procedure, comparison baseline, acceptance criteria and hold points, and estimate the three largest uncertainty contributions.","observation":"現場實務：交接時以比較相鄰沉陷測點與接觸面開口並檢查變形後材料連續性作為可追溯證據，保存對應材料、構形與工況版本。針對與剛性牆面脫離會形成繞過反濾的集中水路，由負責工程師設定需補驗的項目與停留點，不能把教學結果當作現場操作許可。","observationEn":"Site practice: At handover, use the following traceable evidence: Compare neighboring settlement points and interface openings and examine post-deformation material continuity. Record material, geometry and operating-state versions. Address this scenario: Separation from a rigid wall creates a concentrated path around the filter. The responsible engineer defines additional checks and hold points; the teaching result is not field operating authorization.","failure":"注意干擾：與剛性牆面脫離會形成繞過反濾的集中水路。 只量一次、沒有可追溯的基準，或不記錄溫度、水頭與施工荷重，就無法分辨真正的偏差與量測誤差。","failureEn":"Watch for interference: Separation from a rigid wall creates a concentrated path around the filter. A single reading, no traceable datum, or unrecorded temperature, water head and construction loads make real deviations indistinguishable from measurement error.","check":"提交試驗或量測計畫：儀器、基準、步驟、允收準則、停工點與不確定度預算，並說明如何判定合格或不合格、由誰簽認。","checkEn":"Submit the test or measurement plan: instruments, datums, procedure, acceptance criteria, hold points and uncertainty budget, with the pass/fail rule and who signs it off.","knowledge":[{"id":"b242-v15-39-k1","title":"驗證方法","titleEn":"Verification method","text":"比較相鄰沉陷測點與接觸面開口並檢查變形後材料連續性。應將原始量測與本單元模型的輸入條件對齊，並針對「與剛性牆面脫離會形成繞過反濾的集中水路」取得獨立證據；同時保留儀器校正、測點位置與時間，避免把不同工況的資料直接相減。","textEn":"Compare neighboring settlement points and interface openings and examine post-deformation material continuity. Match raw observations to the input conditions of this unit and obtain independent evidence for this specific scenario: Separation from a rigid wall creates a concentrated path around the filter. Preserve calibration, location and timing so that unlike operating states are not directly subtracted.","sourceIds":["b-src-water-manuals","v15s-usbr-filters","v15s-fema-seepage","v15s-usbr-embankment-history"]},{"id":"b242-v15-39-k2","title":"現場實務","titleEn":"Site practice","text":"交接時以比較相鄰沉陷測點與接觸面開口並檢查變形後材料連續性作為可追溯證據，保存對應材料、構形與工況版本。針對與剛性牆面脫離會形成繞過反濾的集中水路，由負責工程師設定需補驗的項目與停留點，不能把教學結果當作現場操作許可。","textEn":"At handover, use the following traceable evidence: Compare neighboring settlement points and interface openings and examine post-deformation material continuity. Record material, geometry and operating-state versions. Address this scenario: Separation from a rigid wall creates a concentrated path around the filter. The responsible engineer defines additional checks and hold points; the teaching result is not field operating authorization.","sourceIds":["b-src-water-manuals","v15s-usbr-filters","v15s-fema-seepage","v15s-usbr-embankment-history"]}],"quiz":{"question":"要驗證「變形相容與連續性」，下列哪一個做法最恰當？","questionEn":"Which approach best verifies \"Deformation compatibility and continuity\"?","options":["比較相鄰沉陷測點與接觸面開口並檢查變形後材料連續性。","不確定度太難估計，報告中只寫最佳值即可。","留土功能正常就表示排水出口一定暢通"],"optionsEn":["Compare neighboring settlement points and interface openings and examine post-deformation material continuity.","Uncertainty is too hard to estimate, so the report may state only the best value.","Successful soil retention guarantees an unobstructed drainage outlet"],"answer":0,"explanation":"比較相鄰沉陷測點與接觸面開口並檢查變形後材料連續性。 驗證需要基準、重複性與事先訂定的允收準則。","explanationEn":"Compare neighboring settlement points and interface openings and examine post-deformation material continuity. Verification needs a datum, repeatability and acceptance criteria fixed in advance."},"unit":10,"unitFacet":"verification","order":7,"sequence":39},{"id":"b242-v15-40","title":"變形相容與連續性：失效診斷","titleEn":"Deformation compatibility and continuity: failure diagnosis","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["b-src-water-manuals","v15s-usbr-filters","v15s-fema-seepage","v15s-usbr-embankment-history"],"prerequisiteIds":["b242-v15-39"],"objective":"從症狀倒推「變形相容與連續性」的失效或劣化原因，提出能區分原因的檢查、矯正與預防措施。","objectiveEn":"Work back from symptoms to the failure or deterioration causes of “Deformation compatibility and continuity” and propose discriminating checks, corrective actions and prevention.","instruction":"與剛性牆面脫離會形成繞過反濾的集中水路。診斷時應採取以下查核：比較相鄰沉陷測點與接觸面開口並檢查變形後材料連續性，確認異常是否同時出現在相關量測；未釐清原因就調整門檻，會使真正的機制變化被資料處理掩蓋。 師傅任務：建立失效樹——症狀、兩個以上可能原因、能區分它們的量測或檢測，以及矯正與預防措施；並說明此失效如何影響整體結構的安全、使用性、耐久或營運。","instructionEn":"Separation from a rigid wall creates a concentrated path around the filter. Diagnose it by the following check: Compare neighboring settlement points and interface openings and examine post-deformation material continuity. Establish whether related measurements corroborate the anomaly; changing thresholds before identifying the cause can conceal a real change in the governing mechanism. Mentor task: build a fault tree with the symptom, at least two candidate causes, a measurement or inspection that tells them apart, and corrective and preventive actions; explain how the failure affects whole-structure safety, serviceability, durability or operation.","observation":"連結機制：這有助於確認模型的水流、受力或量測邊界是否仍成立。","observationEn":"Link to the mechanism: That distinction determines whether the model boundary or measurement assumption remains valid.","failure":"誤判風險：若相信「顆粒可以重排就保證任何變形後仍連續」，上述症狀可能被錯誤處理而反覆出現。","failureEn":"Misdiagnosis risk: believing \"Particle rearrangement guarantees continuity after any amount of deformation\" leads to mishandling the symptom so it keeps returning.","check":"完成失效樹與矯正措施，指出哪一項量測或檢測能最快確認根因、需要哪些人簽認，以及如何防止再發。","checkEn":"Complete the fault tree and corrective actions, name the measurement or inspection that confirms the root cause fastest, who must sign off, and how recurrence is prevented.","knowledge":[{"id":"b242-v15-40-k1","title":"失效模式","titleEn":"Failure mode","text":"與剛性牆面脫離會形成繞過反濾的集中水路。診斷時應採取以下查核：比較相鄰沉陷測點與接觸面開口並檢查變形後材料連續性，確認異常是否同時出現在相關量測；未釐清原因就調整門檻，會使真正的機制變化被資料處理掩蓋。","textEn":"Separation from a rigid wall creates a concentrated path around the filter. Diagnose it by the following check: Compare neighboring settlement points and interface openings and examine post-deformation material continuity. Establish whether related measurements corroborate the anomaly; changing thresholds before identifying the cause can conceal a real change in the governing mechanism.","sourceIds":["b-src-water-manuals","v15s-usbr-filters","v15s-fema-seepage","v15s-usbr-embankment-history"]},{"id":"b242-v15-40-k2","title":"根因確認","titleEn":"Root-cause confirmation","text":"根因必須以可區分的量測或檢測確認；只補強外觀、更換構件或放寬允收值可能掩蓋問題。","textEn":"Confirm the root cause with a discriminating measurement or inspection; cosmetic repair, swapping components or relaxing limits can mask the problem.","sourceIds":["b-src-water-manuals","v15s-usbr-filters","v15s-fema-seepage","v15s-usbr-embankment-history"]}],"quiz":{"question":"在「變形相容與連續性」出現異常時，下列哪一項判斷最合理？","questionEn":"When \"Deformation compatibility and continuity\" shows distress, which diagnosis is most reasonable?","options":["先更換最貴的構件；只要症狀消失，就代表已找到根因。","與剛性牆面脫離會形成繞過反濾的集中水路。","單一粒徑比可以批准所有不同土類反濾"],"optionsEn":["Replace the most expensive component first; if the symptom disappears, the root cause has been found.","Separation from a rigid wall creates a concentrated path around the filter.","One grain-size ratio can approve filters for every soil class"],"answer":1,"explanation":"與剛性牆面脫離會形成繞過反濾的集中水路。 需以量測區分可能原因。","explanationEn":"Separation from a rigid wall creates a concentrated path around the filter. Discriminate candidate causes by measurement."},"unit":10,"unitFacet":"failure","order":8,"sequence":40}],"order":5}],"sourceIds":["b-src-water-manuals","v15s-usbr-filters","v15s-fema-seepage","v15s-usbr-embankment-history"],"curriculumVersion":15,"stepCount":40,"estimatedMinutes":1000}};
